{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KbuWUnSFVCNU3e3LMYPzRY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.85.2)\n2\t\n3\tEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\n4\tfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n5\t\n6\t**The engine is yours to change.** This copy is yours to fix, extend or rewrite in any way you see fit: `my-3d2dge.js`\n7\tis the engine, readable, with every module, and every page and test here loads it (`modules/` and `my-3d2dge-agent.js`\n8\tare separate copies). If you hand the game back, a line on what you changed and why helps: it shows what the engine\n9\tlacks.\n10\t\n11\t## Start here\n12\t\n13\t1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n14\t   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n15\t2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n16\t   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n17\t   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n18\t   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n19\t   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n20\t   `game/` and make it yours.\n21\t3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n22\t   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n23\t4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n24\t5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n25\t   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n26\t   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n27\t6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n28\t   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n29\t   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n30\t   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n31\t   before you use it.\n32\t\n33\t## What is here\n34\t\n35\t| File | What it is |\n36\t| --- | --- |\n37\t| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n38\t| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n39\t| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n40\t| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n41\t| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n42\t| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n43\t| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n44\t| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n45\t| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n46\t| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n47\t| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n48\t| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n49\t| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n50\t\n51\tNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n52\t(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\n53\tengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n54\t\n55\t## Run, test, check\n56\t\n57\t```sh\n58\tnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\n59\tnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\n60\tnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\n61\tnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\n62\tnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\n63\tnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\n64\tnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n65\t```\n66\t\n67\tOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\n68\tthe two scripts into the page.\n69\t\n70\t## Testing a game without a browser\n71\t\n72\t`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped.\n73\t\n74\t- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n75\t- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n76\t- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n77\t  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n78\t- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n79\t\n80\tThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"17318b25-a6b7-4609-afac-2701a85a6514","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:49:51.020Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/README.md","content":"# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.85.2)\n\nEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\nfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n\n**The engine is yours to change.** This copy is yours to fix, extend or rewrite in any way you see fit: `my-3d2dge.js`\nis the engine, readable, with every module, and every page and test here loads it (`modules/` and `my-3d2dge-agent.js`\nare separate copies). If you hand the game back, a line on what you changed and why helps: it shows what the engine\nlacks.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n   `game/` and make it yours.\n3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n   before you use it.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n\nNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\nengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n\n## Run, test, check\n\n```sh\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\nthe two scripts into the page.\n\n## Testing a game without a browser\n\n`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped.\n\n- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n\nThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KbuWUnSFVCNU3e3LMYPzRY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyBXQe6tvXhuQyjFwXq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019N4YX49HPFHawaqQFmbs5M","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/kits/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1557,"cache_read_input_tokens":30130,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1557},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"fd10075f-8a14-48b3-99b4-4621fa375c44","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:49:51.501Z","request_id":"req_011CggyBXBzb8GNSahjKJ2Cc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019N4YX49HPFHawaqQFmbs5M":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/kits/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019N4YX49HPFHawaqQFmbs5M","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# The genre kits (v0.85.2)\n2\t\n3\tA kit is a complete small game in one genre, written to be copied: its title, play and end, the modules it rests on,\n4\tits sound, touch controls and a phone's screen. The API card's Genre playbook (`API.md`) names a kit for each genre (its\n5\t\"Copy slice\" column); the table says which file is which. Each kit is the same game as the single-file kit on the site\n6\t(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/kits/<id>), readable, on this package's engine.\n7\t\n8\t- **`<id>.js`**, its game: the starter's shell (the title menu, the keys every kit shares, the proof), the slice, and the\n9\t  start, as the single-file kit holds them between `GAME START` and `GAME END`. Its header says what it plays, its keys,\n10\t  its deep links and how it works.\n11\t- **`<id>.html`** plays it (open it, or `node tools/check.mjs kits/<id>.html#<id>`); `#<id>` starts the slice, and\n12\t  `#<id>/<part>` jumps into a part.\n13\t- **`node kits/test.mjs <id>`** runs it headless: the slice plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice.\n14\t\n15\t**Start a game from one:** copy `<id>.js` to `game/game.js` (and, if its page loads an asset set, that `<script>` line into\n16\t`game/index.html` before `game.js`). Then replace the starter's title menu with your own title scene and keep only your\n17\tgame, as its header says. Its test: copy `kits/test.mjs`'s three stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`) into\n18\t`game/test.mjs`. A game of several genres reads the kits it mixes and builds on the full engine, which has every module.\n19\t\n20\t| Kit | Files | What it plays | Modules | Deep links |\n21\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n22\t| ADVENTURE | [adventure.js](adventure.js), [adventure.html](adventure.html) | a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana | none | #adventure |\n23\t| POINT-AND-CLICK | [pointclick.js](pointclick.js), [pointclick.html](pointclick.html) | an adventure of three rooms: a dock, a tavern, a lighthouse; four puzzles, the nine verbs or a verb coin, an inventory, a riddle contest | click, story | #pointclick |\n24\t| PLATFORMER | [platformer.js](platformer.js), [platformer.html](platformer.html) | a side-scroller: a night approach to a castle in five zones, a sword, a dash, candles, a 2.5D view; Castlevania, Mega Man X, Klonoa | none | #platformer |\n25\t| METROIDVANIA | [metroidvania.js](metroidvania.js), [metroidvania.html](metroidvania.html) | a world of rooms: its map, two abilities that open its gates, a save room, two bosses | rooms | #metroidvania, #metroidvania/miniboss, #metroidvania/boss, #metroidvania/map |\n26\t| SHOOTER | [shooter.js](shooter.js), [shooter.html](shooter.html) | a vertical shoot-'em-up stage, then a horizontal one: waves, power-ups, bosses; 1943 and Raiden, then Gradius and R-Type | arcade | #shooter, #shooter/horizontal |\n27\t| ARCADE | [arcade.js](arcade.js), [arcade.html](arcade.html) | a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks | arcade, grid, gen | #arcade, #arcade/maze, #arcade/formation, #arcade/rocks |\n28\t| PINBALL | [pinball.js](pinball.js), [pinball.html](pinball.html) | one table: flippers, bumpers, a ramp, drop targets, a spinner, a kickback, a mission, multiball, tilt, a dot-matrix display | physics, arcade | #pinball |\n29\t| ARTILLERY | [artillery.js](artillery.js), [artillery.html](artillery.html) | two teams of three on an island every blast carves: turns, aim and power, wind, a rocket, a bouncing grenade, a cluster bomb, falls and the sea, a CPU that tries its shots in simulation | physics, terrain, grid | #artillery, #artillery/cpu |\n30\t| PUZZLE | [puzzle.js](puzzle.js), [puzzle.html](puzzle.html) | falling blocks and falling pairs that chain, versus with a second player or the CPU; Tetris, Puyo Puyo | grid | #puzzle |\n31\t| RHYTHM | [rhythm.js](rhythm.js), [rhythm.html](rhythm.html) | four lanes on the music clock: two songs, notes, jumps, holds, a rapping teacher to answer, a dancer and a crowd on the beat, grades, the audio offset | songs, rhythm | #rhythm, #rhythm/stepup, #rhythm/rapschool, #rhythm/calibrate |\n32\t| RPG | [rpg.js](rpg.js), [rpg.html](rpg.html) | a JRPG's journey: a town, a world map, a cave and its boss, the ATB battle, menus and save slots | story, rpg | #rpg, #rpg/battle |\n33\t| ROGUELIKE | [roguelike.js](roguelike.js), [roguelike.html](roguelike.html) | a turn-based crypt of ten generated floors: fields of view and fog, turns by speed, potions and scrolls; Rogue, Mystery Dungeon | grid, gen | #roguelike |\n34\t| TACTICS | [tactics.js](tactics.js), [tactics.html](tactics.html) | an isometric battle on a map of heights: charge time or phases, facing, arcs, areas, a scoring AI | grid, story | #tactics, #tactics/battle, #tactics/phases |\n35\t| RTS | [rts.js](rts.js), [rts.html](rts.html) | real-time strategy: workers, gold, a barracks and a stable, three kinds to fight, fog, an enemy camp that builds and attacks in waves | grid, strategy | #rts |\n36\t| SIM | [sim.js](sim.js), [sim.html](sim.html) | a theme park: paths, four rides and two shops, guests with needs and money, prices, a rating, day and night, time controls | grid, strategy | #sim |\n37\t| BRAWLER | [brawler.js](brawler.js), [brawler.html](brawler.html) | a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage | none | #brawler |\n38\t| FIGHTING | [fighting.js](fighting.js), [fighting.html](fighting.html) | one on one: three fighters, versus, arcade, training | fight | #fighting, #fighting/versus, #fighting/arcade, #fighting/training |\n39\t| ANIMATION LAB | [animlab.js](animlab.js), [animlab.html](animlab.html) | every move, pose, skin and view of the character rigs | none | #animlab |\n40\t| KART | [kart.js](kart.js), [kart.html](kart.html) | Mode 7 karts: six on a circuit, three laps, items, two players in a split screen | mode7, drive | #kart, #kart/race, #kart/vs |\n41\t| ROAD | [road.js](road.js), [road.html](road.html) | a pseudo-3D coast road against the clock: curves, hills, a tunnel, traffic, checkpoints, a radio | road | #road, #road/drive |\n42\t| SPORTS | [sports.js](sports.js), [sports.html](sports.html) | two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam | none | #sports, #sports/match, #sports/vs |\n43\t| STEALTH | [stealth.js](stealth.js), [stealth.html](stealth.html) | third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear | none | #stealth |\n44\t\n45\t**3D:** the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows, are not in this package. They are on the\n46\tsite (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d, /kits/3d-<genre>) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge:\n47\t`engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`, its header the 3D manual; `src/starter3d/`). Here, a 3D game is built on the 2D engine's views,\n48\ta world in x, y and z drawn from any angle (`API.md`, Coordinates).\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"499db2db-bfe1-418f-a572-20127c1c6362","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:49:51.512Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/kits/README.md","content":"# The genre kits (v0.85.2)\n\nA kit is a complete small game in one genre, written to be copied: its title, play and end, the modules it rests on,\nits sound, touch controls and a phone's screen. The API card's Genre playbook (`API.md`) names a kit for each genre (its\n\"Copy slice\" column); the table says which file is which. Each kit is the same game as the single-file kit on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/kits/<id>), readable, on this package's engine.\n\n- **`<id>.js`**, its game: the starter's shell (the title menu, the keys every kit shares, the proof), the slice, and the\n  start, as the single-file kit holds them between `GAME START` and `GAME END`. Its header says what it plays, its keys,\n  its deep links and how it works.\n- **`<id>.html`** plays it (open it, or `node tools/check.mjs kits/<id>.html#<id>`); `#<id>` starts the slice, and\n  `#<id>/<part>` jumps into a part.\n- **`node kits/test.mjs <id>`** runs it headless: the slice plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice.\n\n**Start a game from one:** copy `<id>.js` to `game/game.js` (and, if its page loads an asset set, that `<script>` line into\n`game/index.html` before `game.js`). Then replace the starter's title menu with your own title scene and keep only your\ngame, as its header says. Its test: copy `kits/test.mjs`'s three stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`) into\n`game/test.mjs`. A game of several genres reads the kits it mixes and builds on the full engine, which has every module.\n\n| Kit | Files | What it plays | Modules | Deep links |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ADVENTURE | [adventure.js](adventure.js), [adventure.html](adventure.html) | a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana | none | #adventure |\n| POINT-AND-CLICK | [pointclick.js](pointclick.js), [pointclick.html](pointclick.html) | an adventure of three rooms: a dock, a tavern, a lighthouse; four puzzles, the nine verbs or a verb coin, an inventory, a riddle contest | click, story | #pointclick |\n| PLATFORMER | [platformer.js](platformer.js), [platformer.html](platformer.html) | a side-scroller: a night approach to a castle in five zones, a sword, a dash, candles, a 2.5D view; Castlevania, Mega Man X, Klonoa | none | #platformer |\n| METROIDVANIA | [metroidvania.js](metroidvania.js), [metroidvania.html](metroidvania.html) | a world of rooms: its map, two abilities that open its gates, a save room, two bosses | rooms | #metroidvania, #metroidvania/miniboss, #metroidvania/boss, #metroidvania/map |\n| SHOOTER | [shooter.js](shooter.js), [shooter.html](shooter.html) | a vertical shoot-'em-up stage, then a horizontal one: waves, power-ups, bosses; 1943 and Raiden, then Gradius and R-Type | arcade | #shooter, #shooter/horizontal |\n| ARCADE | [arcade.js](arcade.js), [arcade.html](arcade.html) | a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks | arcade, grid, gen | #arcade, #arcade/maze, #arcade/formation, #arcade/rocks |\n| PINBALL | [pinball.js](pinball.js), [pinball.html](pinball.html) | one table: flippers, bumpers, a ramp, drop targets, a spinner, a kickback, a mission, multiball, tilt, a dot-matrix display | physics, arcade | #pinball |\n| ARTILLERY | [artillery.js](artillery.js), [artillery.html](artillery.html) | two teams of three on an island every blast carves: turns, aim and power, wind, a rocket, a bouncing grenade, a cluster bomb, falls and the sea, a CPU that tries its shots in simulation | physics, terrain, grid | #artillery, #artillery/cpu |\n| PUZZLE | [puzzle.js](puzzle.js), [puzzle.html](puzzle.html) | falling blocks and falling pairs that chain, versus with a second player or the CPU; Tetris, Puyo Puyo | grid | #puzzle |\n| RHYTHM | [rhythm.js](rhythm.js), [rhythm.html](rhythm.html) | four lanes on the music clock: two songs, notes, jumps, holds, a rapping teacher to answer, a dancer and a crowd on the beat, grades, the audio offset | songs, rhythm | #rhythm, #rhythm/stepup, #rhythm/rapschool, #rhythm/calibrate |\n| RPG | [rpg.js](rpg.js), [rpg.html](rpg.html) | a JRPG's journey: a town, a world map, a cave and its boss, the ATB battle, menus and save slots | story, rpg | #rpg, #rpg/battle |\n| ROGUELIKE | [roguelike.js](roguelike.js), [roguelike.html](roguelike.html) | a turn-based crypt of ten generated floors: fields of view and fog, turns by speed, potions and scrolls; Rogue, Mystery Dungeon | grid, gen | #roguelike |\n| TACTICS | [tactics.js](tactics.js), [tactics.html](tactics.html) | an isometric battle on a map of heights: charge time or phases, facing, arcs, areas, a scoring AI | grid, story | #tactics, #tactics/battle, #tactics/phases |\n| RTS | [rts.js](rts.js), [rts.html](rts.html) | real-time strategy: workers, gold, a barracks and a stable, three kinds to fight, fog, an enemy camp that builds and attacks in waves | grid, strategy | #rts |\n| SIM | [sim.js](sim.js), [sim.html](sim.html) | a theme park: paths, four rides and two shops, guests with needs and money, prices, a rating, day and night, time controls | grid, strategy | #sim |\n| BRAWLER | [brawler.js](brawler.js), [brawler.html](brawler.html) | a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage | none | #brawler |\n| FIGHTING | [fighting.js](fighting.js), [fighting.html](fighting.html) | one on one: three fighters, versus, arcade, training | fight | #fighting, #fighting/versus, #fighting/arcade, #fighting/training |\n| ANIMATION LAB | [animlab.js](animlab.js), [animlab.html](animlab.html) | every move, pose, skin and view of the character rigs | none | #animlab |\n| KART | [kart.js](kart.js), [kart.html](kart.html) | Mode 7 karts: six on a circuit, three laps, items, two players in a split screen | mode7, drive | #kart, #kart/race, #kart/vs |\n| ROAD | [road.js](road.js), [road.html](road.html) | a pseudo-3D coast road against the clock: curves, hills, a tunnel, traffic, checkpoints, a radio | road | #road, #road/drive |\n| SPORTS | [sports.js](sports.js), [sports.html](sports.html) | two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam | none | #sports, #sports/match, #sports/vs |\n| STEALTH | [stealth.js](stealth.js), [stealth.html](stealth.html) | third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear | none | #stealth |\n\n**3D:** the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows, are not in this package. They are on the\nsite (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d, /kits/3d-<genre>) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge:\n`engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`, its header the 3D manual; `src/starter3d/`). Here, a 3D game is built on the 2D engine's views,\na world in x, y and z drawn from any angle (`API.md`, Coordinates).\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019N4YX49HPFHawaqQFmbs5M","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
