{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NU9U3y2o1RkVEAWcT5GhAC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// The SPORTS kit's game (two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n2\t// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/68-sports.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n3\t// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. sports.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs sports runs it headless.\n4\t/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n5\t * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n6\t * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n7\t * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n8\t * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n9\t * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n10\t * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n11\t * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n12\t * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n13\t * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n14\t * ======================================================================== */\n15\t(() => {\n16\t'use strict';\n17\tconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n18\t\n19\t/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n20\t * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\n21\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\n22\tconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\n23\tconst scenes = {};\n24\tlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\n25\tconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n26\t// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n27\t// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\n28\tconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n29\t// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\n30\tconst SLICES = [\n31\t  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n32\t  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n33\t  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n34\t  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n35\t  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n36\t  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n37\t  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n38\t  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n39\t  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n40\t  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n41\t  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n42\t  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n43\t  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n44\t  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n45\t  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n46\t  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n47\t  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n48\t  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n49\t  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n50\t  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n51\t  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n52\t  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n53\t];\n54\t/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n55\t   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n56\t   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n57\t   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\n58\tconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\n59\taddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n60\t  if (e.repeat) return;\n61\t  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n62\t  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n63\t  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n64\t  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n65\t  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n66\t});\n67\t\n68\t/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n69\t * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\n70\tconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n71\t  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\n72\tconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\n73\tconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n74\t  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n75\t  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n76\t  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n77\t  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n78\t  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n79\t  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n80\t];\n81\tHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n82\t// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\n83\tconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n84\t// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\n85\tconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n86\t/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n87\t * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n88\t * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n89\t * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n90\t * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\n91\tconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n92\t  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n93\t  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n94\t  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n95\t  try {\n96\t    if (fresh) fresh();\n97\t    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n98\t    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n99\t    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n100\t    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n101\t    return h >>> 0;\n102\t  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n103\t};\n104\t// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\n105\tconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n106\t// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\n107\tconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n108\t/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n109\t *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\n110\tconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\n111\tlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\n112\tscenes.title = {\n113\t  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n114\t  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n115\t  update(dt) {\n116\t    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n117\t    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n118\t    const t = game.time;\n119\t    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n120\t      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n121\t      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n122\t    });\n123\t  },\n124\t  draw(r) {\n125\t    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n126\t    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n127\t    titleBg.draw(r);\n128\t    stage.draw(r);\n129\t    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n130\t    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n131\t    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n132\t    r.overlay(g => {\n133\t      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n134\t      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n135\t      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n136\t    });\n137\t    titleMenu.draw(r);\n138\t    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n139\t      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n140\t    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"63779ef5-9084-494f-bdb7-a22b7841a345","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:27.337Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/kits/sports.js","content":"// The SPORTS kit's game (two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/68-sports.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. sports.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs sports runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });","numLines":140,"startLine":1,"totalLines":592}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NU9U3y2o1RkVEAWcT5GhAC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyERewroQYzA62kUjw3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still in research: reading the engine's sports kit (the closest starting point for an Olympics game), then the AI Hub multiplayer library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6681,"cache_read_input_tokens":109281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6681},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"9efc49a2-6adb-43f4-80ad-f03eb8cf8519","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:28.807Z","request_id":"req_011CggyERSZ4xZvbcQSyDF6Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyERewroQYzA62kUjw3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EFRwYe6NksjQZp3ruWCyQD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/kits/sports.js","offset":140,"limit":130},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6681,"cache_read_input_tokens":109281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6681},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"030431af-543d-4762-87c1-f4d7bc4dece8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:29.833Z","request_id":"req_011CggyERSZ4xZvbcQSyDF6Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EFRwYe6NksjQZp3ruWCyQD":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/kits/sports.js","offset":140,"limit":130}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFRwYe6NksjQZp3ruWCyQD","type":"tool_result","content":"140\t    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n141\t  }\n142\t};\n143\t\n144\t/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\n145\tconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\n146\tconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n147\t  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\n148\tscenes.over = {\n149\t  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n150\t  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n151\t  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n152\t  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n153\t  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n154\t    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n155\t    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n156\t  }\n157\t};\n158\t\n159\t/* =====================================================================================\n160\t * SLICE 22  SPORTS  (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).\n161\t * Two against two in a walled cage, for up to four players: the GULLS against the RUST, two halves on the clock, a\n162\t * golden goal if it ends level. The ball is a Body: it rolls, bounces off the ground and the boards, and curls.\n163\t * KEYS: the stick runs; J passes (to the teammate the stick points at, led to where it is going), L lobs one over a\n164\t * defender (its arc solved by E.arc to land at the teammate's feet), K held fills the shot meter and shoots on letting go\n165\t * (the stick across the goal aims it; pushed sideways just after, it curls: aftertouch). Without the ball: J slides in\n166\t * to tackle, K switches to the teammate nearer the ball. TOUCH: the stick, PASS, SHOOT (hold), LOB.\n167\t * PLAYERS: MATCH is you against the CPU; VERSUS lets players 2 to 4 in (2 on the keyboard, or Start on a pad): player 2\n168\t * takes the RUST, 3 and 4 the second of each side. The rest are run by formation: with the ball, the other one runs\n169\t * ahead on the far side; without it, the nearer presses and the other covers the goal. Commentary on Dialog's radio.\n170\t * Deep links: #sports/match (a match against the CPU), #sports/vs (VERSUS: players 2 to 4 join).\n171\t * HOW IT WORKS: a TileMap cage (boards that cut low before the camera, nets), the ball and the players as E.Body, rigs\n172\t * that kick and slide (E.Attack), E.arc for the lob, game.allowJoin for players; SPORTS.run(n) is the proof,\n173\t * SPORTS.bot() plays a match through to its whistle and then a short one with four players.\n174\t * ===================================================================================== */\n175\tconst SPORTS = (() => {\n176\t  const A = game.audio, T = 16, FW = 36, FH = 22, ND = 2, GOAL = 5, BAR = 28, HALF = 60, GOLDEN = 45, PI = Math.PI;\n177\t  /* ---- THE CAGE: a field of FW x FH tiles inside boards (cut low where they hide it), a goal in each end with its net,\n178\t   * a stand of three tiers behind the north boards; built from rows: # boards, N net, . the field, : the net's floor,\n179\t   * 1 2 3 the stand's tiers (back to front), , outside ---- */\n180\t  const STAND = 3, COLS = ND + FW + 2 + ND, ROWS = STAND + FH + 2, MID = FH / 2, goalRow = r => r > MID - GOAL / 2 && r <= MID + GOAL / 2;\n181\t  const rows = [];\n182\t  for (let R = 0; R < ROWS; R++) {\n183\t    let s = ''; const r = R - STAND;   // (the cage's own row)\n184\t    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n185\t      const field = c > ND && c <= ND + FW && r > 0 && r <= FH, endCol = c === ND || c === ND + FW + 1, net = (c < ND || c > ND + FW + 1);\n186\t      if (r < 0) s += c >= ND && c <= ND + FW + 1 ? String(R + 1) : ',';\n187\t      else if (field) s += '.';\n188\t      else if (endCol && r > 0 && r <= FH) s += goalRow(r) ? '.' : '#';\n189\t      else if ((r === 0 || r === FH + 1) && c >= ND && c <= ND + FW + 1) s += '#';\n190\t      else if (net && goalRow(r)) s += c === 0 || c === COLS - 1 ? 'N' : ':';\n191\t      else if (net && (goalRow(r + 1) || goalRow(r - 1))) s += 'N';\n192\t      else s += ',';\n193\t    }\n194\t    rows.push(s);\n195\t  }\n196\t  const X0 = (ND + 1) * T, X1 = (ND + 1 + FW) * T, Y0 = (STAND + 1) * T, Y1 = (STAND + FH + 1) * T, CX = (X0 + X1) / 2, CY = (Y0 + Y1) / 2, GH = GOAL * T / 2;\n197\t  // the pitch: mown stripes with the grass's own grain, painted lines a little worn (the halfway line, the centre circle,\n198\t  // an arc before each goal), the nets' shadow on their floor, tarmac outside\n199\t  const line = (x, y) => {\n200\t    const d = Math.hypot(x - CX, y - CY), ex = Math.min(Math.abs(x - X0), Math.abs(x - X1)), ey = Math.min(Math.abs(y - Y0), Math.abs(y - Y1));\n201\t    if (ex < 1.5 || ey < 1.5 || Math.abs(x - CX) < 1 || Math.abs(d - 48) < 1) return true;\n202\t    for (const gx of [X0, X1]) if (Math.abs(Math.hypot(x - gx, y - CY) - 72) < 1 && Math.abs(x - gx) < 72) return true;\n203\t    return false;\n204\t  };\n205\t  const floorTex = (x, y, tag) => {\n206\t    const n = E.hash2(Math.floor(x), Math.floor(y)) - .5, m = E.noise2(x * .06, y * .06) * .5;\n207\t    if (tag === 'net') { const mesh = Math.floor(x) % 4 === 0 || Math.floor(y) % 4 === 0; return mesh ? [30, 66, 36] : [44 + n * 10, 92 + n * 14, 50 + n * 10]; }\n208\t    if (tag === 'out') return [44 + n * 18, 42 + n * 18, 50 + n * 18];\n209\t    if (line(x, y)) { const w = 228 + n * 24 + m * 10; return [w, w + 4, w - 8]; }\n210\t    const k = Math.floor((x - X0) / 32) % 2 ? 1 : 0, g = (k ? 140 : 106) + n * 34 + m * 24;   // (a stripe mown each way: lighter, darker)\n211\t    return [g * .42, g, g * .46];\n212\t  };\n213\t  let map = null;\n214\t  const makeMap = () => new E.TileMap({ rows, legend: { '#': 1, N: 2, 1: 5, 2: 4, 3: 3, '.': { floor: 'grass' }, ':': { floor: 'net' }, ',': { floor: 'out' } }, floorTex, outside: '#1e1c24', ao: 4,\n215\t    types: { 1: { h: 26, cut: true, cutH: 6, face: 'plank', side: '#3a4a6a', top: '#d8dce8', line: '#2a3450' }, 2: { h: BAR + 4, face: 'none', side: '#b8bcc8', top: '#e0e4ec' },\n216\t      3: { h: 34, face: 'stone', side: '#5a5468', top: '#6a6478' }, 4: { h: 44, face: 'stone', side: '#4e4a5e', top: '#5e586e' }, 5: { h: 54, face: 'stone', side: '#44405a', top: '#544e66' } } });\n217\t  // the crowd: two on each tile of the stand, in their colors, bobbing; on a goal, those of the side that scored jump\n218\t  const CROWD = [];\n219\t  for (let R = 0; R < STAND; R++) for (let c = ND; c <= ND + FW + 1; c++) for (const dx of [4, 12]) {\n220\t    const h = E.hash2(c * 3 + dx, R * 7 + 1), side = h < .5 ? 0 : 1;\n221\t    CROWD.push({ x: c * T + dx, y: R * T + 9, z: [54, 44, 34][R], side, shirt: side ? ['#c8502a', '#e07040', '#a83a1a'][(h * 30 | 0) % 3] : ['#eef0f6', '#2a5ab8', '#8ab0f0'][(h * 30 | 0) % 3], skin: ['#e0b090', '#a87050', '#6a4028', '#f0c8a8'][(h * 50 | 0) % 4], ph: h * 9 });\n222\t  }\n223\t  /* ---- THE TEAMS: their colors, names and players; the ball ---- */\n224\t  const TEAMS = [\n225\t    { name: 'GULLS', colors: { cloth: '#eef0f6', pants: '#2a5ab8', boot: '#1e2030', belt: '#2a5ab8', trim: '#2a5ab8' }, chip: '#eef0f6', players: [['NOOR', '#3a2418', '#c89070'], ['BEX', '#e8c070', '#f0c8a8']] },\n226\t    { name: 'RUST', colors: { cloth: '#c8502a', pants: '#2a2a30', boot: '#1a1a1e', belt: '#1a1a1e', trim: '#e8c070' }, chip: '#c8502a', players: [['DRAGO', '#1e1c1a', '#a87050'], ['KIT', '#6a3a22', '#e0b090']] }];\n227\t  const SPEED = 92, AI_SPEED = 86, KICK_CD = .3;\n228\t  const BALL = E.sprite(['.www.', 'wwkww', 'wkkkw', 'wwkww', '.www.'], { w: '#f4f4f0', k: '#2a2a30' });\n229\t  const BALL2 = E.sprite(['.www.', 'wkwkw', 'wwwww', 'wkwkw', '.www.'], { w: '#f4f4f0', k: '#2a2a30' });\n230\t  const SOUNDS = {\n231\t    kick: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 200, dur: .07, vol: .3, filter: 'lowpass' }, thump: { wave: 'sine', freq: 120, to: 70, dur: .08, vol: .3 },\n232\t    whistle: { wave: 'square', freq: 2200, vib: [30, .05], dur: .32, vol: .14 }, post: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 1400, to: 1100, dur: .3, vol: .25 },\n233\t    crowd: { wave: 'noise', freq: 600, to: 900, dur: 1.4, vol: .18, filter: 'lowpass' }, slide: { wave: 'noise', freq: 400, to: 200, dur: .25, vol: .18 }\n234\t  };\n235\t  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n236\t  const SONG = { bpm: 140, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the cage: a bright chant over a bouncing bass\n237\t    { wave: 'square', vol: .07, notes: 'E5 . E5 G5 . E5 D5 . | C5 . C5 E5 . C5 B4 . | A4 . C5 . E5 . A5 . | G5 - - . . . . .' },\n238\t    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . | A2 . E2 . A2 . E2 . | F2 . C3 . F2 . C3 . | G2 . D3 . G2 . B2 .' },\n239\t    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h . s . h k | k . h . s h h .' }] };\n240\t\n241\t  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n242\t  let mode = 'menu', vs = false, team = [], all = [], ball = null, owner = null, last = null, clock = 0, half = 1, score = [0, 0], kickT = 0, t = 0, scripted = false;\n243\t  let stats = null, curlT = 0, golden = false, restartBy = 0, over = false, kickHold = 0;   // kickHold: the kickoff's rule (the other side out of the circle) until the ball is played\n244\t  const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['MATCH', 'VERSUS (2-4 PLAYERS)', 'BACK'], { onPick: i => i === 2 ? game.go('title') : i === 1 ? versus() : start(false) });\n245\t  const after = new E.Menu(game, ['REMATCH', 'MENU'], { y: 150, onPick: i => i === 0 ? start(vs) : toMenu() });\n246\t  const talk = new E.Dialog(game, { lines: 2, place: 'bottom', border: '#e8c070' });   // (at the bottom: clear of the score and of the touch buttons)\n247\t  const VOICE = new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, hat: 'band', colors: { cloth: '#3a3a4a', hair: '#5a3a2a', skin: '#e0b090', hat: '#2a2a30' } });\n248\t  const say = text => { if (!scripted) talk.say(text, { name: 'CAGE RADIO', auto: 2.2, modal: false, alpha: .8, portrait: VOICE, portraitOpts: { zoom: 3, turn: .4 } }); };\n249\t\n250\t  function toMenu() { mode = 'menu'; game.splitScreen(0); game.allowJoin(false); A.music('title'); menu.i = 0; }\n251\t  function versus() { vs = true; mode = 'join'; game.allowJoin({ max: 4 }); A.sfx('select'); }\n252\t  /** a match: the four on the pitch, the ball at the centre, the clock at 0; players: who holds which (the inputs) */\n253\t  function start(versus) {\n254\t    vs = versus; map = map || makeMap(); score = [0, 0]; clock = 0; half = 1; golden = false; over = false; owner = null; last = null;\n255\t    stats = { passes: 0, done: 0, shots: 0, lobs: 0, tackles: 0, goals: [], walls: 0, curled: 0 };\n256\t    all = []; team = [[], []];\n257\t    TEAMS.forEach((tm, s) => tm.players.forEach(([name, hair, skin], k) => {\n258\t      const b = new E.Body({ x: CX, y: CY, r: 5, friction: 0, gravity: 700 });\n259\t      const p = { side: s, k, name, body: b, rig: new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, build: 'heroic', size: 1.05, hair: k ? 'spiky' : 'short', colors: Object.assign({ hair, skin }, tm.colors), speedRef: 80 }),\n260\t        input: null, facing: s ? PI : 0, kick: null, slide: 0, stun: 0, cool: 0, meter: 0, charging: false, cheer: 0 };\n261\t      team[s].push(p); all.push(p);\n262\t    }));\n263\t    // who holds whom: player 1 the GULLS' first (and, alone, whichever GULL is nearer the ball); in versus 2 the RUST, 3 and 4\n264\t    // the second of each side\n265\t    const P = game.players;\n266\t    team[0][0].input = P[0];\n267\t    if (vs) { if (P[1]) team[1][0].input = P[1]; if (P[2]) team[0][1].input = P[2]; if (P[3]) team[1][1].input = P[3]; }\n268\t    ball = new E.Body({ x: CX, y: CY, r: 3, friction: 0, bounce: .55, gravity: 600 }); ball.spin = 0; ball.roll = 0;\n269\t    kickoff(0); game.allowJoin(false); A.music(SONG); game.input.consumeAll();"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"af612b2a-d46c-4090-8420-75be084da278","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:29.840Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x7ac903/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/kits/sports.js","content":"    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\nconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\nscenes.over = {\n  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 22  SPORTS  (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).\n * Two against two in a walled cage, for up to four players: the GULLS against the RUST, two halves on the clock, a\n * golden goal if it ends level. The ball is a Body: it rolls, bounces off the ground and the boards, and curls.\n * KEYS: the stick runs; J passes (to the teammate the stick points at, led to where it is going), L lobs one over a\n * defender (its arc solved by E.arc to land at the teammate's feet), K held fills the shot meter and shoots on letting go\n * (the stick across the goal aims it; pushed sideways just after, it curls: aftertouch). Without the ball: J slides in\n * to tackle, K switches to the teammate nearer the ball. TOUCH: the stick, PASS, SHOOT (hold), LOB.\n * PLAYERS: MATCH is you against the CPU; VERSUS lets players 2 to 4 in (2 on the keyboard, or Start on a pad): player 2\n * takes the RUST, 3 and 4 the second of each side. The rest are run by formation: with the ball, the other one runs\n * ahead on the far side; without it, the nearer presses and the other covers the goal. Commentary on Dialog's radio.\n * Deep links: #sports/match (a match against the CPU), #sports/vs (VERSUS: players 2 to 4 join).\n * HOW IT WORKS: a TileMap cage (boards that cut low before the camera, nets), the ball and the players as E.Body, rigs\n * that kick and slide (E.Attack), E.arc for the lob, game.allowJoin for players; SPORTS.run(n) is the proof,\n * SPORTS.bot() plays a match through to its whistle and then a short one with four players.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst SPORTS = (() => {\n  const A = game.audio, T = 16, FW = 36, FH = 22, ND = 2, GOAL = 5, BAR = 28, HALF = 60, GOLDEN = 45, PI = Math.PI;\n  /* ---- THE CAGE: a field of FW x FH tiles inside boards (cut low where they hide it), a goal in each end with its net,\n   * a stand of three tiers behind the north boards; built from rows: # boards, N net, . the field, : the net's floor,\n   * 1 2 3 the stand's tiers (back to front), , outside ---- */\n  const STAND = 3, COLS = ND + FW + 2 + ND, ROWS = STAND + FH + 2, MID = FH / 2, goalRow = r => r > MID - GOAL / 2 && r <= MID + GOAL / 2;\n  const rows = [];\n  for (let R = 0; R < ROWS; R++) {\n    let s = ''; const r = R - STAND;   // (the cage's own row)\n    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++) {\n      const field = c > ND && c <= ND + FW && r > 0 && r <= FH, endCol = c === ND || c === ND + FW + 1, net = (c < ND || c > ND + FW + 1);\n      if (r < 0) s += c >= ND && c <= ND + FW + 1 ? String(R + 1) : ',';\n      else if (field) s += '.';\n      else if (endCol && r > 0 && r <= FH) s += goalRow(r) ? '.' : '#';\n      else if ((r === 0 || r === FH + 1) && c >= ND && c <= ND + FW + 1) s += '#';\n      else if (net && goalRow(r)) s += c === 0 || c === COLS - 1 ? 'N' : ':';\n      else if (net && (goalRow(r + 1) || goalRow(r - 1))) s += 'N';\n      else s += ',';\n    }\n    rows.push(s);\n  }\n  const X0 = (ND + 1) * T, X1 = (ND + 1 + FW) * T, Y0 = (STAND + 1) * T, Y1 = (STAND + FH + 1) * T, CX = (X0 + X1) / 2, CY = (Y0 + Y1) / 2, GH = GOAL * T / 2;\n  // the pitch: mown stripes with the grass's own grain, painted lines a little worn (the halfway line, the centre circle,\n  // an arc before each goal), the nets' shadow on their floor, tarmac outside\n  const line = (x, y) => {\n    const d = Math.hypot(x - CX, y - CY), ex = Math.min(Math.abs(x - X0), Math.abs(x - X1)), ey = Math.min(Math.abs(y - Y0), Math.abs(y - Y1));\n    if (ex < 1.5 || ey < 1.5 || Math.abs(x - CX) < 1 || Math.abs(d - 48) < 1) return true;\n    for (const gx of [X0, X1]) if (Math.abs(Math.hypot(x - gx, y - CY) - 72) < 1 && Math.abs(x - gx) < 72) return true;\n    return false;\n  };\n  const floorTex = (x, y, tag) => {\n    const n = E.hash2(Math.floor(x), Math.floor(y)) - .5, m = E.noise2(x * .06, y * .06) * .5;\n    if (tag === 'net') { const mesh = Math.floor(x) % 4 === 0 || Math.floor(y) % 4 === 0; return mesh ? [30, 66, 36] : [44 + n * 10, 92 + n * 14, 50 + n * 10]; }\n    if (tag === 'out') return [44 + n * 18, 42 + n * 18, 50 + n * 18];\n    if (line(x, y)) { const w = 228 + n * 24 + m * 10; return [w, w + 4, w - 8]; }\n    const k = Math.floor((x - X0) / 32) % 2 ? 1 : 0, g = (k ? 140 : 106) + n * 34 + m * 24;   // (a stripe mown each way: lighter, darker)\n    return [g * .42, g, g * .46];\n  };\n  let map = null;\n  const makeMap = () => new E.TileMap({ rows, legend: { '#': 1, N: 2, 1: 5, 2: 4, 3: 3, '.': { floor: 'grass' }, ':': { floor: 'net' }, ',': { floor: 'out' } }, floorTex, outside: '#1e1c24', ao: 4,\n    types: { 1: { h: 26, cut: true, cutH: 6, face: 'plank', side: '#3a4a6a', top: '#d8dce8', line: '#2a3450' }, 2: { h: BAR + 4, face: 'none', side: '#b8bcc8', top: '#e0e4ec' },\n      3: { h: 34, face: 'stone', side: '#5a5468', top: '#6a6478' }, 4: { h: 44, face: 'stone', side: '#4e4a5e', top: '#5e586e' }, 5: { h: 54, face: 'stone', side: '#44405a', top: '#544e66' } } });\n  // the crowd: two on each tile of the stand, in their colors, bobbing; on a goal, those of the side that scored jump\n  const CROWD = [];\n  for (let R = 0; R < STAND; R++) for (let c = ND; c <= ND + FW + 1; c++) for (const dx of [4, 12]) {\n    const h = E.hash2(c * 3 + dx, R * 7 + 1), side = h < .5 ? 0 : 1;\n    CROWD.push({ x: c * T + dx, y: R * T + 9, z: [54, 44, 34][R], side, shirt: side ? ['#c8502a', '#e07040', '#a83a1a'][(h * 30 | 0) % 3] : ['#eef0f6', '#2a5ab8', '#8ab0f0'][(h * 30 | 0) % 3], skin: ['#e0b090', '#a87050', '#6a4028', '#f0c8a8'][(h * 50 | 0) % 4], ph: h * 9 });\n  }\n  /* ---- THE TEAMS: their colors, names and players; the ball ---- */\n  const TEAMS = [\n    { name: 'GULLS', colors: { cloth: '#eef0f6', pants: '#2a5ab8', boot: '#1e2030', belt: '#2a5ab8', trim: '#2a5ab8' }, chip: '#eef0f6', players: [['NOOR', '#3a2418', '#c89070'], ['BEX', '#e8c070', '#f0c8a8']] },\n    { name: 'RUST', colors: { cloth: '#c8502a', pants: '#2a2a30', boot: '#1a1a1e', belt: '#1a1a1e', trim: '#e8c070' }, chip: '#c8502a', players: [['DRAGO', '#1e1c1a', '#a87050'], ['KIT', '#6a3a22', '#e0b090']] }];\n  const SPEED = 92, AI_SPEED = 86, KICK_CD = .3;\n  const BALL = E.sprite(['.www.', 'wwkww', 'wkkkw', 'wwkww', '.www.'], { w: '#f4f4f0', k: '#2a2a30' });\n  const BALL2 = E.sprite(['.www.', 'wkwkw', 'wwwww', 'wkwkw', '.www.'], { w: '#f4f4f0', k: '#2a2a30' });\n  const SOUNDS = {\n    kick: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 200, dur: .07, vol: .3, filter: 'lowpass' }, thump: { wave: 'sine', freq: 120, to: 70, dur: .08, vol: .3 },\n    whistle: { wave: 'square', freq: 2200, vib: [30, .05], dur: .32, vol: .14 }, post: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 1400, to: 1100, dur: .3, vol: .25 },\n    crowd: { wave: 'noise', freq: 600, to: 900, dur: 1.4, vol: .18, filter: 'lowpass' }, slide: { wave: 'noise', freq: 400, to: 200, dur: .25, vol: .18 }\n  };\n  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n  const SONG = { bpm: 140, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the cage: a bright chant over a bouncing bass\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .07, notes: 'E5 . E5 G5 . E5 D5 . | C5 . C5 E5 . C5 B4 . | A4 . C5 . E5 . A5 . | G5 - - . . . . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . | A2 . E2 . A2 . E2 . | F2 . C3 . F2 . C3 . | G2 . D3 . G2 . B2 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h . s . h k | k . h . s h h .' }] };\n\n  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n  let mode = 'menu', vs = false, team = [], all = [], ball = null, owner = null, last = null, clock = 0, half = 1, score = [0, 0], kickT = 0, t = 0, scripted = false;\n  let stats = null, curlT = 0, golden = false, restartBy = 0, over = false, kickHold = 0;   // kickHold: the kickoff's rule (the other side out of the circle) until the ball is played\n  const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['MATCH', 'VERSUS (2-4 PLAYERS)', 'BACK'], { onPick: i => i === 2 ? game.go('title') : i === 1 ? versus() : start(false) });\n  const after = new E.Menu(game, ['REMATCH', 'MENU'], { y: 150, onPick: i => i === 0 ? start(vs) : toMenu() });\n  const talk = new E.Dialog(game, { lines: 2, place: 'bottom', border: '#e8c070' });   // (at the bottom: clear of the score and of the touch buttons)\n  const VOICE = new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, hat: 'band', colors: { cloth: '#3a3a4a', hair: '#5a3a2a', skin: '#e0b090', hat: '#2a2a30' } });\n  const say = text => { if (!scripted) talk.say(text, { name: 'CAGE RADIO', auto: 2.2, modal: false, alpha: .8, portrait: VOICE, portraitOpts: { zoom: 3, turn: .4 } }); };\n\n  function toMenu() { mode = 'menu'; game.splitScreen(0); game.allowJoin(false); A.music('title'); menu.i = 0; }\n  function versus() { vs = true; mode = 'join'; game.allowJoin({ max: 4 }); A.sfx('select'); }\n  /** a match: the four on the pitch, the ball at the centre, the clock at 0; players: who holds which (the inputs) */\n  function start(versus) {\n    vs = versus; map = map || makeMap(); score = [0, 0]; clock = 0; half = 1; golden = false; over = false; owner = null; last = null;\n    stats = { passes: 0, done: 0, shots: 0, lobs: 0, tackles: 0, goals: [], walls: 0, curled: 0 };\n    all = []; team = [[], []];\n    TEAMS.forEach((tm, s) => tm.players.forEach(([name, hair, skin], k) => {\n      const b = new E.Body({ x: CX, y: CY, r: 5, friction: 0, gravity: 700 });\n      const p = { side: s, k, name, body: b, rig: new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, build: 'heroic', size: 1.05, hair: k ? 'spiky' : 'short', colors: Object.assign({ hair, skin }, tm.colors), speedRef: 80 }),\n        input: null, facing: s ? PI : 0, kick: null, slide: 0, stun: 0, cool: 0, meter: 0, charging: false, cheer: 0 };\n      team[s].push(p); all.push(p);\n    }));\n    // who holds whom: player 1 the GULLS' first (and, alone, whichever GULL is nearer the ball); in versus 2 the RUST, 3 and 4\n    // the second of each side\n    const P = game.players;\n    team[0][0].input = P[0];\n    if (vs) { if (P[1]) team[1][0].input = P[1]; if (P[2]) team[0][1].input = P[2]; if (P[3]) team[1][1].input = P[3]; }\n    ball = new E.Body({ x: CX, y: CY, r: 3, friction: 0, bounce: .55, gravity: 600 }); ball.spin = 0; ball.roll = 0;\n    kickoff(0); game.allowJoin(false); A.music(SONG); game.input.consumeAll();","numLines":130,"startLine":140,"totalLines":592}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EFRwYe6NksjQZp3ruWCyQD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
