{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GtprFkdr6ErULU5KfwLwZJ","type":"tool_result","content":"284\t### 4.1 Tech stack\n285\t\n286\t- **Engine:** our copy of the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the core plus every module; we use\n287\t  the `road`, `rhythm`, `physics`, `arcade` and `songs` modules from it). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no CDN, no\n288\t  network at runtime.\n289\t- **Online:** AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0, unmodified, first script in `<head>`.\n290\t- **Tooling:** Node (headless tests via `vm`, as `game/test.mjs` does), Playwright 1.63.0 + Chromium (browser checks,\n291\t  hub harness, screenshots), the handoff's `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n292\t- **Deliverable:** one self-contained HTML (engine + session client + game inlined), ~1.8 MB, works from `file://`.\n293\t\n294\t### 4.2 Folder layout\n295\t\n296\t```\n297\tOlympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/\n298\t  index.html                 dev page: same <head> as the bundle; loads engine + src files in order (the list is the bundle's source of truth)\n299\t  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the engine + our changes, each marked  // OLY: <why>\n300\t  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)\n301\t  vendor/my-3d2dge/          sparse clone of the handoff: docs, kits, tools (reference + Playwright); never bundled\n302\t  src/                       the game: one IIFE per file, all attach to window.OLY (alias O)\n303\t  tests/                     run.mjs (the one command) + suites\n304\t  tools/bundle.mjs           builds the root HTML from index.html's script list\n305\t  tools/shots.mjs            screenshot/filmstrip helper around the handoff tools\n306\t```\n307\t\n308\t### 4.3 Source files (load order = bundle order)\n309\t\n310\t| File | Responsibility |\n311\t|---|---|\n312\t| `00-core.js` | creates `window.OLY`, the `E.Game` (§4.4), constants (`M`, palettes), `O.def(kind, id, spec)` registries, `O.bus` (on/emit), `O.store` (E.store wrappers), `O.rng(label)` streams (§4.7), formatting helpers |\n313\t| `01-input.js` | `OLY_KEYS` preset, per-scene presets (archery/curling/hockey add mouse), **pilots** (§5.2), `Mash` meter, `O.AutoPlayer` (bot intents → real `input.tap/hold`), idle/any-input tracker, touch-only detection, hub Create+Options guard |\n314\t| `02-prompts.js` | `O.Prompt` glyph renderer (§2.3) |\n315\t| `03-ui.js` | 10-foot widgets: `Menu10` (vertical list), `Grid10` (tile grid), `Tabs`, `Panel`, `Banner` (big stamped words), `Ticker`, `LowerThird`, `Toast`, page dots, number/time formatters; mouse hover/click via `input.pointer()`/`clicked()` |\n316\t| `04-audio.js` | SFX definitions (`audio.define`), songs (§9), `O.Voice` gibberish synth, `O.CrowdAudio`, `O.Anthem` generator, stings |\n317\t| `05-art.js` | palettes per venue, flag painter, pictograms, emblem, equipment sprites, stands + crowd painter, jumbotron (dot matrix), podium, fireworks/confetti helpers, mascot (Blob) |\n318\t| `06-pose.js` | `O.Pose` library and `O.Gear` (equipment drawn at joints), body rotation (§8.2) |\n319\t| `07-athletes.js` | `NATIONS` data (§7.1), teammates, `O.makeRig(nation, sport, opts)` outfits per sport, voice params |\n320\t| `08-commentary.js` | `O.Comms`: commentators, line banks (§7.6), cue rules, subtitles + voice + portraits |\n321\t| `09-hype.js` | `O.Hype` (meter, turbo), `O.Yikes` (stamp, count, sympathy hype), `O.Crowd` (visual excitement), slow-mo/photo helpers |\n322\t| `10-records.js` | world records seed table, games records, personal bests, top-5 tables via `E.Arcade`, points formulas, medal table, party points, laurels, cabinet |\n323\t| `11-ghosts.js` | ghost recording/playback (local turns + hub), compact samples |\n324\t| `12-eventkit.js` | the event contract, `O.defEvent`, the phase runner, formats (race / attempts / match / program), CPU simulation, results assembly, qualifying, timing widgets (`TimingBar`, `Ring`, `Balance`, `Sway`, `StrokeBeat`) |\n325\t| `20-ev-sprint.js` … `35-ev-hockey.js` | one file per event (§6), ids: `sprint javelin swim diving archery weights skijump downhill bobsled figure curling hockey` |\n326\t| `40-sc-title.js` | title, main menu, touch-only notice, attract director (§11) |\n327\t| `41-sc-games.js` | games setup, nation select/join, opening ceremony, day card, story beats, event card, turn card, results, initials, medal ceremony, medal table, torch/continue, closing + ending + credits |\n328\t| `42-sc-misc.js` | single event select, records, how to play, about & credits, pose lab |\n329\t| `43-dev.js` | dev panel, tuning sliders, cheats, overlays (§13) |\n330\t| `44-hub.js` | AI Hub session flow (§12.2) |\n331\t| `99-main.js` | registers scenes, deep links (`#ev/<id>`, `#scene/<name>`, `#attract`, `#poselab`, `#games/day/<n>`), `game.debug`, `window.__oly` for tests, `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n332\t\n333\tEach file: `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, O = OLY; ... })();`. Tests load exactly the same files in the same\n334\torder into a `vm` context (read the list from `index.html` so it can't drift).\n335\t\n336\t### 4.4 The game object\n337\t\n338\t```js\n339\tconst game = O.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS,\n340\t  id: 'olympiyikes', bg: '#0b0f24',\n341\t  menu: { items: inHub ? [] : [['Restart event', O.restartEvent], ['How to play', O.showEventCard], ['Dev mode', O.Dev.open]],\n342\t          settings: GAME_SETTINGS /* §2.5 */, quit: inHub ? false : 'title',\n343\t          controls: { mashL: 'Left (mash, pass, tuck)', mashR: 'Right (mash, check, pike)', action: 'Action (jump, throw, release)',\n344\t                      turbo: 'Yikes Turbo', alt: 'Hold (tuck, breathe, steady)' } } });\n345\t```\n346\t`inHub = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active)` (true from the client's first line). Menu items are static, so each item's\n347\tfunction is context-aware: outside an event \"Restart event\" and \"How to play\" show `game.note('Not in an event')`.\n348\t\n349\t### 4.5 Scenes\n350\t\n351\t`O.scene(name, def)` registers a wrapped engine scene. The wrapper: calls `input.consumeAll()` on enter; applies the\n352\t0.6 s lockout (`def.lock`); if the dev panel is open, runs `O.Dev.update()` instead of `def.update` and draws the panel\n353\tafter `def.draw`; draws global overlays (toasts, commentary lower third, attract banner, \"YIKES\" stamps, laurel toasts)\n354\tafter the scene; tracks idle time on menu scenes (`def.menu: true`) for the attract mode; routes `back()`.\n355\t\n356\tScenes: `title`, `menu`, `touchonly` (a state of `title`), `attract`, `gamesSetup`, `nations`, `opening`, `dayCard`,\n357\t`beat`, `eventCard`, `turnCard` (overlay state inside events), `ev:<id>` ×12, `results`, `initials`, `podium`,\n358\t`medals`, `torch`, `closing`, `credits`, `single`, `records`, `howto`, `about`, `poselab`, `hubCard`, `hubSplash`.\n359\t\n360\t`O.flow` is the state machine above them: it holds the current **meet** (§4.8) and decides the next scene after each\n361\tone ends (`O.flow.next(from, payload)`), for each mode (games, quick, single, hub, attract).\n362\t\n363\t### 4.6 Engine changes (all marked `// OLY:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`; list them on the About screen)\n364\t\n365\t1. **Export the hooks:** `E.HOOKS = HOOKS;` so the game can run code at the start of every step even while paused\n366\t   (`HOOKS.input`): hub Create+Options guard, global any-input detection.\n367\t2. **Cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`:** the Humanoid (`this.t` start phase, blink timer), `Particles` and\n368\t   `hitFx`'s number jitter draw from a module-level `const cosmetic = rng(0xC05E7)` instead of `Math.random`. Then\n369\t   cosmetics never shift gameplay randomness, the hub card draws no `Math.random` numbers, and tests stay\n370\t   deterministic.\n371\t3. **Font glyphs:** add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 (`G57`) and 3×5 (`GLYPHS`) tables.\n372\t4. **PlayStation by default:** the `glyphs` setting's default becomes `'playstation'`.\n373\t5. **Pose hook on the Humanoid:** at the end of `solvePose()`, if `this.post` is a function call `this.post(this, this.J)`;\n374\t   then, if `this.bodyPitch || this.bodyRoll`, rotate every joint (and cape/hair points, as `_roll` does) about\n375\t   `this.pivot` (default: hip centre) by pitch (forward–up plane) and roll (right–up plane), **without** `_roll`'s\n376\t   floor lift. This is what flips, dives, swims, tumbles and V-style flight need (§8.2).\n377\t6. **Voice bus:** `ChipAudio` gets a `_voiceBus` gain under the master, a `voiceVolume` field honored by\n378\t   `applyVolume()`, and the settings get `voices` (Sound group, default .8). `O.Voice` connects to it.\n379\t\n380\t### 4.7 Randomness and determinism\n381\t\n382\t- **Gameplay randomness only through labeled streams:** `O.rng(label)` returns a `[0,1)` generator. In a hub session\n383\t  it is `AIHub.rng(label)` (identical on every copy); otherwise `E.rng(hash(meet.seed + '|' + label))`. Labels are\n384\t  namespaced: `'sprint:gun'`, `'javelin:wind:r2'`, `'cpu:FRM:skijump:j1'`, `'judges:diving:SUN:d3'`.\n385\t- Cosmetics (particles, blinks, crowd bob) never touch `Math.random` (engine change 2) or the gameplay streams.\n386\t- `meet.seed` comes from the clock when a meet starts; tests and the dev panel can set it.\n387\t- Every event sim is a function of (state, intents, streams), independent of drawing, so a sim can run headless,\n388\t  twice, and hash the same (the kits' \"proof\" idea).\n389\t\n390\t### 4.8 Data model\n391\t\n392\t```\n393\tNation   { id: 'SUN', name: 'SUNVALE', colors: { a, b, c }, flag: { kind, ... }, athlete: { name, rig, bio, voice },\n394\t           team: [3 names], skills: { sprint: .92, ... }, anthem: { seed, key, bpm } }\n395\tAthlete  { id, nation, name, rig, gear, pilot, lane, human, player (0-3 | null), hype, turboT, state: {}, attempts: [],\n396\t           best, notes: [], ghost }\n397\tPilot    { kind: 'human' | 'bot' | 'ghost' | 'net', input?, skill, cheat?: 'perfect' | null }\n398\tIntent   { L, R, A, T (pressed this step), Lh, Rh, Ad, Au, X (held / released), mv: [x, y], aim: [x, y] | null }\n399\tMeet     { mode, seed, events: [ids], day, players: [{ input, nation, color }], difficulty, qualifying, torches,\n400\t           medals: { SUN: { g, s, b } }, party: { P1: pts }, results: { eventId: Results }, beats: Set, yikes: { SUN: n } }\n401\tResults  { event, rows: [{ athlete, perf, display, rank, medal, notes, points }], records: [], laurels: [] }\n402\tStore    'oly:records' (top-5 per event + WR), 'oly:laurels', 'oly:cabinet', 'oly:games' (autosave),\n403\t         'oly:ghost:<event>' (best local run), 'oly:seen' (first-time tips), 'oly:tune' (only if the dev opts in)\n404\t```\n405\t\n406\t### 4.9 Bundle\n407\t\n408\t`node tools/bundle.mjs` reads `index.html`'s `<script src>` list and writes the root HTML:\n409\t\n410\t```html\n411\t<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n412\t<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, byte-for-byte */</script>\n413\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n414\t<title>Olympiyikes! — Faster. Higher. Yikes.</title>\n415\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight, for 1–4 players.\">\n416\t<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#f2b632\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,...the emblem...\">\n417\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n418\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most points across three Olympiyikes events\">\n419\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act · △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold\">\n420\t<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"The Olympic Games\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the building model's id)\">\n421\t<style>/* page + 10-foot shell overrides */</style></head><body>\n422\t<!-- E.bootSplash('OLYMPIYIKES!') markup --><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n423\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script><script>/* src/*.js concatenated */</script></body></html>\n424\t```\n425\tEscape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. The session client must stay unmodified and first after\n426\t`<meta charset>`. The bundle test (§16) checks all of this.\n427\t---\n428\t\n429\t## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n430\t\n431\t### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n432\t\n433\tEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"a9bffc76-8fdf-4c82-9f12-e2591a4a6354","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:30.622Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 4.1 Tech stack\n\n- **Engine:** our copy of the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the core plus every module; we use\n  the `road`, `rhythm`, `physics`, `arcade` and `songs` modules from it). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no CDN, no\n  network at runtime.\n- **Online:** AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0, unmodified, first script in `<head>`.\n- **Tooling:** Node (headless tests via `vm`, as `game/test.mjs` does), Playwright 1.63.0 + Chromium (browser checks,\n  hub harness, screenshots), the handoff's `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n- **Deliverable:** one self-contained HTML (engine + session client + game inlined), ~1.8 MB, works from `file://`.\n\n### 4.2 Folder layout\n\n```\nOlympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/\n  index.html                 dev page: same <head> as the bundle; loads engine + src files in order (the list is the bundle's source of truth)\n  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the engine + our changes, each marked  // OLY: <why>\n  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)\n  vendor/my-3d2dge/          sparse clone of the handoff: docs, kits, tools (reference + Playwright); never bundled\n  src/                       the game: one IIFE per file, all attach to window.OLY (alias O)\n  tests/                     run.mjs (the one command) + suites\n  tools/bundle.mjs           builds the root HTML from index.html's script list\n  tools/shots.mjs            screenshot/filmstrip helper around the handoff tools\n```\n\n### 4.3 Source files (load order = bundle order)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `00-core.js` | creates `window.OLY`, the `E.Game` (§4.4), constants (`M`, palettes), `O.def(kind, id, spec)` registries, `O.bus` (on/emit), `O.store` (E.store wrappers), `O.rng(label)` streams (§4.7), formatting helpers |\n| `01-input.js` | `OLY_KEYS` preset, per-scene presets (archery/curling/hockey add mouse), **pilots** (§5.2), `Mash` meter, `O.AutoPlayer` (bot intents → real `input.tap/hold`), idle/any-input tracker, touch-only detection, hub Create+Options guard |\n| `02-prompts.js` | `O.Prompt` glyph renderer (§2.3) |\n| `03-ui.js` | 10-foot widgets: `Menu10` (vertical list), `Grid10` (tile grid), `Tabs`, `Panel`, `Banner` (big stamped words), `Ticker`, `LowerThird`, `Toast`, page dots, number/time formatters; mouse hover/click via `input.pointer()`/`clicked()` |\n| `04-audio.js` | SFX definitions (`audio.define`), songs (§9), `O.Voice` gibberish synth, `O.CrowdAudio`, `O.Anthem` generator, stings |\n| `05-art.js` | palettes per venue, flag painter, pictograms, emblem, equipment sprites, stands + crowd painter, jumbotron (dot matrix), podium, fireworks/confetti helpers, mascot (Blob) |\n| `06-pose.js` | `O.Pose` library and `O.Gear` (equipment drawn at joints), body rotation (§8.2) |\n| `07-athletes.js` | `NATIONS` data (§7.1), teammates, `O.makeRig(nation, sport, opts)` outfits per sport, voice params |\n| `08-commentary.js` | `O.Comms`: commentators, line banks (§7.6), cue rules, subtitles + voice + portraits |\n| `09-hype.js` | `O.Hype` (meter, turbo), `O.Yikes` (stamp, count, sympathy hype), `O.Crowd` (visual excitement), slow-mo/photo helpers |\n| `10-records.js` | world records seed table, games records, personal bests, top-5 tables via `E.Arcade`, points formulas, medal table, party points, laurels, cabinet |\n| `11-ghosts.js` | ghost recording/playback (local turns + hub), compact samples |\n| `12-eventkit.js` | the event contract, `O.defEvent`, the phase runner, formats (race / attempts / match / program), CPU simulation, results assembly, qualifying, timing widgets (`TimingBar`, `Ring`, `Balance`, `Sway`, `StrokeBeat`) |\n| `20-ev-sprint.js` … `35-ev-hockey.js` | one file per event (§6), ids: `sprint javelin swim diving archery weights skijump downhill bobsled figure curling hockey` |\n| `40-sc-title.js` | title, main menu, touch-only notice, attract director (§11) |\n| `41-sc-games.js` | games setup, nation select/join, opening ceremony, day card, story beats, event card, turn card, results, initials, medal ceremony, medal table, torch/continue, closing + ending + credits |\n| `42-sc-misc.js` | single event select, records, how to play, about & credits, pose lab |\n| `43-dev.js` | dev panel, tuning sliders, cheats, overlays (§13) |\n| `44-hub.js` | AI Hub session flow (§12.2) |\n| `99-main.js` | registers scenes, deep links (`#ev/<id>`, `#scene/<name>`, `#attract`, `#poselab`, `#games/day/<n>`), `game.debug`, `window.__oly` for tests, `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n\nEach file: `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, O = OLY; ... })();`. Tests load exactly the same files in the same\norder into a `vm` context (read the list from `index.html` so it can't drift).\n\n### 4.4 The game object\n\n```js\nconst game = O.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS,\n  id: 'olympiyikes', bg: '#0b0f24',\n  menu: { items: inHub ? [] : [['Restart event', O.restartEvent], ['How to play', O.showEventCard], ['Dev mode', O.Dev.open]],\n          settings: GAME_SETTINGS /* §2.5 */, quit: inHub ? false : 'title',\n          controls: { mashL: 'Left (mash, pass, tuck)', mashR: 'Right (mash, check, pike)', action: 'Action (jump, throw, release)',\n                      turbo: 'Yikes Turbo', alt: 'Hold (tuck, breathe, steady)' } } });\n```\n`inHub = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active)` (true from the client's first line). Menu items are static, so each item's\nfunction is context-aware: outside an event \"Restart event\" and \"How to play\" show `game.note('Not in an event')`.\n\n### 4.5 Scenes\n\n`O.scene(name, def)` registers a wrapped engine scene. The wrapper: calls `input.consumeAll()` on enter; applies the\n0.6 s lockout (`def.lock`); if the dev panel is open, runs `O.Dev.update()` instead of `def.update` and draws the panel\nafter `def.draw`; draws global overlays (toasts, commentary lower third, attract banner, \"YIKES\" stamps, laurel toasts)\nafter the scene; tracks idle time on menu scenes (`def.menu: true`) for the attract mode; routes `back()`.\n\nScenes: `title`, `menu`, `touchonly` (a state of `title`), `attract`, `gamesSetup`, `nations`, `opening`, `dayCard`,\n`beat`, `eventCard`, `turnCard` (overlay state inside events), `ev:<id>` ×12, `results`, `initials`, `podium`,\n`medals`, `torch`, `closing`, `credits`, `single`, `records`, `howto`, `about`, `poselab`, `hubCard`, `hubSplash`.\n\n`O.flow` is the state machine above them: it holds the current **meet** (§4.8) and decides the next scene after each\none ends (`O.flow.next(from, payload)`), for each mode (games, quick, single, hub, attract).\n\n### 4.6 Engine changes (all marked `// OLY:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`; list them on the About screen)\n\n1. **Export the hooks:** `E.HOOKS = HOOKS;` so the game can run code at the start of every step even while paused\n   (`HOOKS.input`): hub Create+Options guard, global any-input detection.\n2. **Cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`:** the Humanoid (`this.t` start phase, blink timer), `Particles` and\n   `hitFx`'s number jitter draw from a module-level `const cosmetic = rng(0xC05E7)` instead of `Math.random`. Then\n   cosmetics never shift gameplay randomness, the hub card draws no `Math.random` numbers, and tests stay\n   deterministic.\n3. **Font glyphs:** add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 (`G57`) and 3×5 (`GLYPHS`) tables.\n4. **PlayStation by default:** the `glyphs` setting's default becomes `'playstation'`.\n5. **Pose hook on the Humanoid:** at the end of `solvePose()`, if `this.post` is a function call `this.post(this, this.J)`;\n   then, if `this.bodyPitch || this.bodyRoll`, rotate every joint (and cape/hair points, as `_roll` does) about\n   `this.pivot` (default: hip centre) by pitch (forward–up plane) and roll (right–up plane), **without** `_roll`'s\n   floor lift. This is what flips, dives, swims, tumbles and V-style flight need (§8.2).\n6. **Voice bus:** `ChipAudio` gets a `_voiceBus` gain under the master, a `voiceVolume` field honored by\n   `applyVolume()`, and the settings get `voices` (Sound group, default .8). `O.Voice` connects to it.\n\n### 4.7 Randomness and determinism\n\n- **Gameplay randomness only through labeled streams:** `O.rng(label)` returns a `[0,1)` generator. In a hub session\n  it is `AIHub.rng(label)` (identical on every copy); otherwise `E.rng(hash(meet.seed + '|' + label))`. Labels are\n  namespaced: `'sprint:gun'`, `'javelin:wind:r2'`, `'cpu:FRM:skijump:j1'`, `'judges:diving:SUN:d3'`.\n- Cosmetics (particles, blinks, crowd bob) never touch `Math.random` (engine change 2) or the gameplay streams.\n- `meet.seed` comes from the clock when a meet starts; tests and the dev panel can set it.\n- Every event sim is a function of (state, intents, streams), independent of drawing, so a sim can run headless,\n  twice, and hash the same (the kits' \"proof\" idea).\n\n### 4.8 Data model\n\n```\nNation   { id: 'SUN', name: 'SUNVALE', colors: { a, b, c }, flag: { kind, ... }, athlete: { name, rig, bio, voice },\n           team: [3 names], skills: { sprint: .92, ... }, anthem: { seed, key, bpm } }\nAthlete  { id, nation, name, rig, gear, pilot, lane, human, player (0-3 | null), hype, turboT, state: {}, attempts: [],\n           best, notes: [], ghost }\nPilot    { kind: 'human' | 'bot' | 'ghost' | 'net', input?, skill, cheat?: 'perfect' | null }\nIntent   { L, R, A, T (pressed this step), Lh, Rh, Ad, Au, X (held / released), mv: [x, y], aim: [x, y] | null }\nMeet     { mode, seed, events: [ids], day, players: [{ input, nation, color }], difficulty, qualifying, torches,\n           medals: { SUN: { g, s, b } }, party: { P1: pts }, results: { eventId: Results }, beats: Set, yikes: { SUN: n } }\nResults  { event, rows: [{ athlete, perf, display, rank, medal, notes, points }], records: [], laurels: [] }\nStore    'oly:records' (top-5 per event + WR), 'oly:laurels', 'oly:cabinet', 'oly:games' (autosave),\n         'oly:ghost:<event>' (best local run), 'oly:seen' (first-time tips), 'oly:tune' (only if the dev opts in)\n```\n\n### 4.9 Bundle\n\n`node tools/bundle.mjs` reads `index.html`'s `<script src>` list and writes the root HTML:\n\n```html\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, byte-for-byte */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Olympiyikes! — Faster. Higher. Yikes.</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight, for 1–4 players.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#f2b632\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,...the emblem...\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most points across three Olympiyikes events\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act · △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold\">\n<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"The Olympic Games\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the building model's id)\">\n<style>/* page + 10-foot shell overrides */</style></head><body>\n<!-- E.bootSplash('OLYMPIYIKES!') markup --><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script><script>/* src/*.js concatenated */</script></body></html>\n```\nEscape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. The session client must stay unmodified and first after\n`<meta charset>`. The bundle test (§16) checks all of this.\n---\n\n## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n\n### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n\nEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its","numLines":150,"startLine":284,"totalLines":1715}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GtprFkdr6ErULU5KfwLwZJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
