{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2YajkbSwUE5Lu3eku2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GbS9HUZ8PUBfcLJiN7W5CE","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":432,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":460158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1397},"output_tokens":73,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"758ba85d-f27a-447e-8b11-3095174daebc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:58.135Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2YaUdKJHrXcJkYeScT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GbS9HUZ8PUBfcLJiN7W5CE":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":432,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GbS9HUZ8PUBfcLJiN7W5CE","type":"tool_result","content":"432\t## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n433\t\n434\t### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n435\t\n436\tEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its\n437\ttunables in the tuning registry (§5.13), its card in How to Play, its segment in the attract playlist and, if\n438\t`hub.ok`, in the hub deal.\n439\t\n440\t```js\n441\tO.defEvent({\n442\t  id: 'sprint', name: '100m DASH', short: '100m', season: 'summer', venue: 'stadium', pictogram: 'sprint',\n443\t  music: 'sprint', view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS, camera: { zoom: [.8, 1.6] }, M: 12,\n444\t  format: { type: 'race', attempts: 1, maxHumans: 4 },                  // race | attempts | match | program\n445\t  measure: { unit: 's', better: 'lower', fmt: v => v.toFixed(2) + ' s',\n446\t             wr: [9.48, 'TRB', 'MAX OVERDRIVE'], qualify: { Easy: 12.30, Normal: 11.40, Hard: 10.60 } },\n447\t  points: t => 25.4347 * Math.pow(Math.max(0, 18 - t), 1.81),          // ≈ 0..1250 (WR level ≈ 1100–1250), used by party + hub\n448\t  tune: { vMax: [11.6, 8, 16, .1, 'Top speed (m/s)'], ... },           // [default, min, max, step, label]\n449\t  howto: { goal: 'Fastest to the line wins.', rows: [[['mashL', 'mashR'], 'Alternate to run'], [['action'], 'React to the gun · dip at the line'], [['turbo'], 'Turbo when the flame is full']] },\n450\t  laurel: { id: 'rocket', name: 'ROCKET MAN', text: 'React in 0.120 s or less and win', test: (ctx, a, res) => ... },\n451\t  hub: { ok: true, attempts: 1, seconds: 35 }, attract: { seconds: 18, featured: 'perfect' },\n452\t  build(ctx) {},            // once per scene entry: venue, props, crowd, static data (heavy work: boot steps or here)\n453\t  intro(ctx, t) {},         // optional cinematic (lane introductions); returns true when finished; skippable\n454\t  start(ctx) {},            // per heat / attempt: place athletes, reset per-attempt state\n455\t  ready(ctx, dt) {},        // marks / countdown; returns true when play begins\n456\t  step(ctx, dt) {},         // the simulation: reads ctx.intent(a) for each active athlete; never reads game.input directly\n457\t  bot(ctx, a) {},           // returns an Intent for a CPU/attract/autopilot athlete (skill a.pilot.skill, cheat a.pilot.cheat)\n458\t  done(ctx) {},             // true when the heat / attempt is over\n459\t  perf(ctx, a) {},          // the performance number, or null (DNF / foul / DQ: put the reason in a.notes)\n460\t  draw(ctx, r) {}, hud(ctx, r) {}                                     // skipped headless\n461\t});\n462\t```\n463\t\n464\t**The runner's phases:** `intro` → `ready` → `play` (`step` until `done`) → `finish` (2–3 s celebration, slow-mo,\n465\t\"WORLD RECORD!\" bursts) → `between` (turn card / next round / standings) → back to `start` or → `done` → the flow\n466\tgets the `Results`. `intro` is skipped in hub, attract and on retries; any phase can be jumped to from the dev panel.\n467\t\n468\t**`ctx`** (what the runner gives every hook): `def, meet, game, athletes, humans, active` (those in the current\n469\theat/attempt), `round, attempt, phase, phaseT, t` (seconds of play), `rng(label)` (namespaced by event and attempt),\n470\t`T` (live tunables of this event: `ctx.T.vMax`), `G` (global tunables), `intent(a)`, `emit(name, data)` (bus: comms,\n471\tcrowd, hype, sfx, laurels, tests listen), `finish(a, perf, notes)`, `dnf(a, why)`, `dq(a, why)`, `slowmo(scale, s)`,\n472\t`cam` helpers, `ghosts`.\n473\t\n474\t**Sims are separable from scenes:** each event's state lives in plain objects created by `start`; `step` only touches\n475\tthem. The runner can create a **sandbox ctx** (no scene, no drawing, its own stream labels) to simulate unseen CPU\n476\tattempts by running `start`/`ready`/`step` with bot pilots until `done` (§5.3). Tests use the same sandbox.\n477\t\n478\t### 5.2 Pilots, intents and the autoplayer\n479\t\n480\t- A **pilot** fills an athlete's `Intent` each step: `human` (from its `game.players[i]` input: `pressed('mashL')`,\n481\t  `down('alt')`, `move()`, pointer for aim), `bot` (from `def.bot(ctx, a)`), `ghost` (replays a recording, §5.9),\n482\t  `net` (a hub ghost: drawn only, never simulated).\n483\t- Mash assist is applied in the human pilot (§2.5): One button → every `mashL`/`mashR` press is reported as the\n484\t  alternation the meter expects; Hold → while either is held, synthesize alternations at 72% of `G.mashRateMax`.\n485\t- **`O.AutoPlayer`** drives a *human* athlete through the real input path: each step it asks `def.bot` for an intent\n486\t  and turns it into `input.tap`/`input.hold` calls on that player's input. Used by the dev \"Autopilot\" cheat and by\n487\t  the scripted playthrough test (so menus, prompts, lockouts and the human pilot all get exercised).\n488\t- Cheats are pilot flags: `cheat: 'perfect'` makes `bot` return frame-perfect inputs and keeps hype full (attract,\n489\t  dev \"God mode\").\n490\t- **Fresh presses only:** a human intent ignores buttons still held from before the current phase began (`Ad`, `Lh`,\n491\t  `Rh`, `X` become true only after a press inside the phase), so Space or ✕ held through the event card never starts\n492\t  a javelin's angle or a dive's tuck.\n493\t\n494\t### 5.3 Formats\n495\t\n496\t| Format | Used by | How the runner plays it |\n497\t|---|---|---|\n498\t| `race` | 100m, 50m Free | one heat, all 8 athletes live (humans in the middle lanes 3–6, CPUs fill) |\n499\t| `attempts` | Javelin (3), Diving (3), Archery (6 arrows as 2 ends), Weightlifting (3), Ski Jump (2), Downhill (1), Bobsled (2) | rounds × athletes in start order. Humans play live. CPU attempts: the **2 most relevant** (current leader, the rival, or whoever can overtake a human) play live as **highlights** at 1.5× game speed (✕ skips to the result); the rest are simulated instantly in a sandbox and appear on the standings board |\n500\t| `program` | Figure Skating | like `attempts` with 1 attempt; CPU programs are simulated (score cards shown in the kiss & cry) |\n501\t| `match` | Curling, Ice Hockey | the event runs its own match vs one CPU (or human) nation; the other placings come from `O.Sim.placings(eventId, nations)` (skill-weighted draws from a stream), so all 8 nations get a rank |\n502\t\n503\tTurn order: humans in join order, CPUs by ascending skill (best last, like a real final). Between rounds the standings\n504\tboard shows the top 4 and every human.\n505\t\n506\t### 5.4 Input widgets (src/12-eventkit.js; each has `update`, `press`/`read` and a 10-foot `draw`)\n507\t\n508\t- **`Mash`** (`window: .5 s`): counts *alternations* (a press of the other button than the last one). `rate` = EMA of\n509\t  alternations per second; a same-button press counts 0.25 and grows `same` (the streak resets on a true\n510\t  alternation). Events map `rate` to power with `power = clamp((rate - G.mashRateMin) / (G.mashRateMax - G.mashRateMin), 0, 1) ** .75`\n511\t  (defaults: `mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5` Hz). HUD: the two glyphs pulsing alternately + a 10-segment rate bar.\n512\t- **`TimingBar`**: a needle sweeping a bar (ping-pong, `hz`), zones `[{ from, to, name, q }]`; `press()` → `{ q, zone }`.\n513\t  Windows scale with difficulty and Timing assist.\n514\t- **`Ring`**: a ring shrinking onto a target ring over `dur`; `press()` → signed error in ms → PERFECT ≤ 60 ms,\n515\t  GOOD ≤ 140 ms (×window scale), else BAD.\n516\t- **`Balance`**: a needle `b ∈ [-1, 1]` with drift `b'' = noise(t) * drift - b' * damp`, corrected by the stick axis\n517\t  (`b' += -axis * k * dt`); out of `[-1, 1]` = lost. Noise from the event's stream (deterministic).\n518\t- **`Sway`**: archery reticle: Lissajous + value noise, amplitude driven by the event (§6.5).\n519\t- **`StrokeBeat`**: swimming: alternating expected buttons on a tempo that follows speed; judged like `Ring`.\n520\t\n521\t### 5.5 Hype and YIKES TURBO\n522\t\n523\t- Each athlete has `hype ∈ [0, 1]`, shown as a **flame meter** beside its name (fills orange → white-hot; full = the\n524\t  turbo glyph flashes: \"△ TURBO!\"). Gains come from the event (perfect starts, perfect timing, clean gates, combos),\n525\t  scaled by `G.hypeGain` (1.0); decay `G.hypeDecay` (0.02/s) when not full.\n526\t- Pressing `turbo` with a full flame fires **YIKES TURBO** for `G.turboTime` (3 s): the event's own effect\n527\t  (listed per event), the athlete bursts into (harmless, cartoon) flames (`particles.fire` at the feet/hands + glow\n528\t  light), the music's `hype` layer fades in (`audio.layer('hype', 1, .3)`), the crowd surges, commentary cue\n529\t  `turbo`. `G.turboPower` (1.0) scales every event's turbo multiplier.\n530\t- CPU bots fire turbo at their event's best moment with probability = skill.\n531\t\n532\t### 5.6 CPU rivals and difficulty\n533\t\n534\t- Every nation's athlete has a skill per event (§7.1). Effective skill = `clamp(skill * G.cpuSkillScale + offset, .05, .99)`\n535\t  with offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06 for Easy / Normal / Hard (all three offsets are dev sliders).\n536\t- Bots play **the same rules through intents** (no pre-rolled results): mash rate, reaction time, timing error,\n537\t  aim error, steering noise, turbo use all derive from skill plus noise from the event's stream. This keeps balance\n538\t  honest and lets tests measure it.\n539\t- The rival (Turbonia's Max Overdrive; if a human picked Turbonia, the CPU nation with the highest average skill) gets\n540\t  +0.03 and always plays live highlights.\n541\t\n542\t### 5.7 Results, qualifying, points, records, medals\n543\t\n544\t- **Ranking** by best performance (`better`), ties by the event's tie rule (stated per event), then by earlier\n545\t  attempt. Nulls (DNF/foul/DQ) rank last in their order.\n546\t- **Medals** to ranks 1–3 (match events: winner gold, loser silver, simulated bronze match).\n547\t- **Qualifying (The Games, 1 player, Qualifying On):** a human result worse than `qualify[difficulty]` → \"YIKES! NO\n548\t  QUALIFYING MARK\" → lose a torch (3 per Games) and retry the event (CPU results stand; the retry replaces yours).\n549\t  0 torches → GAMES OVER → CONTINUE? (10 s countdown): yes restores 3 torches and retries; no → title (records and\n550\t  laurels are kept). Match events have no qualifying check. Multi-human Games default Qualifying Off.\n551\t- **Points** (≈ 0–1250, per event formula; a world-record performance is worth ≈ 1100–1250 in every event): party totals in Quick Games / multi-human Games and the hub score.\n552\t- **Party points** (multi-human): 10 8 6 5 4 3 2 1 by rank among all 8; the overall champion is crowned at the end.\n553\t- **Records:** in-world World Records (seed table in §7.5), Games Records (best ever on this device, `oly:records`),\n554\t  Personal Bests per nation. A beaten WR → \"WORLD RECORD!\" banner, fireworks, WR sting, commentary, the jumbotron.\n555\t  Top-5 tables per event with **initials** (`E.Arcade`: `cab.qualifies`, `cab.enter`, `cab.table`), skipped in hub.\n556\t- **Medal table:** gold, then silver, then bronze, then nation name.\n557\t\n558\t### 5.8 Yikes moments\n559\t\n560\t`O.Yikes.trigger(a, kind, at)`: a giant comic stamp **\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"** (or the kind's own word: \"FALSE START!\",\n561\t\"BELLY FLOP!\", \"BONK!\", \"FOUL!\") with shake, the descending-trombone sting, crowd gasp + \"OOOH\", a commentary cue,\n562\t`yikes[nation]++` (shown at the closing ceremony as the \"Yikes reel\"), and **sympathy hype +0.15** (`G.yikesHype`), so\n563\ta comeback is always possible. Reduce-motion keeps the stamp still. Each event lists its yikes kinds; every one must\n564\tbe reachable by ordinary bad play (tests force each).\n565\t\n566\t### 5.9 Ghosts\n567\t\n568\t`O.Ghost.rec(a)` samples `[t, x, y, z, facing, poseCode, extra]` at 20 Hz into a compact array; `O.Ghost.at(track, t)`\n569\tinterpolates; `O.Ghost.draw(ctx, r, state, { tint, name })` draws a translucent rig (`r.actor(..., { alpha: .45 })`\n570\ttinted with the player/seat color) plus a name tag. Uses: the leader's run in Downhill/Bobsled, the previous\n571\tplayer's attempt in turn-based multiplayer, your best local run per event (stored, ≤ 3000 samples), and hub ghosts\n572\t(§12.2) which arrive as the same samples over the network.\n573\t\n574\t### 5.10 Commentary\n575\t\n576\t- Two commentators plus the stadium PA (§7.6): **CHIP BELLOWS** (play-by-play, booming hyperbole), **DAME VERA\n577\t  VELOCITY** (seven-time champion turned colour commentator, dry and sentimental), and the PA announcer (echo).\n578\t- `O.Comms.cue(key, vars, { prio })`: picks a line from the event bank, falling back to the generic bank; never two\n579\t  lines within 3.5 s, each key has a cooldown, higher priority interrupts (WR > yikes > photo finish > lead change >\n580\t  filler). Lines may be two-speaker exchanges.\n581\t- Display: a **lower third** with the speaker's live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, and up to 2 lines of\n582\t  subtitles at scale 2 (Text size Huge = larger), above the prompt strip and clear of the touch area. Voice: `O.Voice`\n583\t  gibberish (§9.3); the portrait's mouth moves while it speaks. Setting \"Commentary\" picks voices+subs / subs / off.\n584\t- Vars: `{name}`, `{nation}`, `{time}`, `{dist}`, `{rival}`, `{place}`.\n585\t\n586\t### 5.11 Crowd, jumbotron, camera, slow-mo\n587\t\n588\t- **Stands** are TileMap tiers (or painted bands in side views) with a crowd painter: one `r.queue` per stand section\n589\t  draws hundreds of 3×5 px spectators (head + shirt in nation colors), bobbing by `O.Crowd.level` (0..1), waving flags,\n590\t  camera-flash glints, doing **the wave** when hype turbo fires or a record falls. The crowd audio follows the same\n591\t  level.\n592\t- **Jumbotron** (stadium, arena, pools): a dot-matrix panel (like the pinball kit's display) showing the event, the\n593\t  clock, the leader, \"WORLD RECORD!\" and a live portrait of the leader.\n594\t- **Camera:** `game.focus` on the human leader (or `cam.frame` on all humans, `zoom: [.6, 1]`) in races; event-\n595\t  specific shots elsewhere. `ctx.slowmo(scale, seconds)` sets `game.timeScale` (photo finish .25, landings .35) and\n596\t  restores it; reduce motion shortens it.\n597\t\n598\t### 5.12 Laurels\n599\t\n600\tOne per event (listed in §6), checked when an attempt ends; awarding shows a toast **\"LAUREL EARNED: ROCKET MAN\"**\n601\twith a golden laurel sprite, saved in `oly:laurels`, shown in Records → Laurels (12 tiles: earned gold / unearned\n602\toutline with its hint text).\n603\t\n604\t### 5.13 Tuning registry (the dev sliders' data)\n605\t\n606\t`O.tune.def(group, key, [default, min, max, step, label])`, `O.tune.get(group)` → live object (events read `ctx.T.key`\n607\tevery step, so a slider change applies immediately), `O.tune.reset(group?)`, `O.tune.changed()`,\n608\t`O.tune.json()`. Global group `G` (defaults): `cpuSkillScale 1`, `cpuOffsetEasy -.12`, `cpuOffsetNormal 0`,\n609\t`cpuOffsetHard .06`, `windowScale 1`, `hypeGain 1`, `hypeDecay .02`, `turboTime 3`, `turboPower 1`,\n610\t`mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5`, `mashHoldRate .72`, `yikesHype .15`, `slowmoScale .3`, `qualifyScale 1`,\n611\t`gameSpeed 1`. Every event defines **at least 6** of its own (listed per event).\n612\t\n613\t### 5.14 Saves\n614\t\n615\t`O.store` over `E.store`: records, laurels, cabinet (best medal per nation per event), the Games autosave (written\n616\tafter each day's medal table: meet minus runtime objects), best local ghost per event, first-time tips seen. Settings\n617\tare the engine's. Storage blocked → everything still works for the visit. In a hub session the client gives an empty\n618\tstorage (nothing to do).\n619\t\n620\t---\n621\t\n622\t## 6. The twelve events\n623\t\n624\tDay order in The Games alternates seasons: **1 100m Dash (S) · 2 Ski Jump (W) · 3 50m Freestyle (S) · 4 Curling (W) ·\n625\t5 Javelin (S) · 6 Downhill (W) · halftime · 7 Archery (S) · 8 Figure Skating (W) · 9 Weightlifting (S) ·\n626\t10 Bobsled (W) · 11 Diving (S) · 12 Ice Hockey Final (W)**.\n627\t\n628\tNumbers below are **starting values for tuning**, each one a dev slider where marked *(T)*. The *targets* are what\n629\ttests check (§16.3); retune freely as long as the targets hold.\n630\t\n631\t### 6.1 100m DASH — summer · Glory Stadium · mash"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"2d8da280-a203-4b9f-a25d-f044af30cab0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:58.143Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n\n### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n\nEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its\ntunables in the tuning registry (§5.13), its card in How to Play, its segment in the attract playlist and, if\n`hub.ok`, in the hub deal.\n\n```js\nO.defEvent({\n  id: 'sprint', name: '100m DASH', short: '100m', season: 'summer', venue: 'stadium', pictogram: 'sprint',\n  music: 'sprint', view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS, camera: { zoom: [.8, 1.6] }, M: 12,\n  format: { type: 'race', attempts: 1, maxHumans: 4 },                  // race | attempts | match | program\n  measure: { unit: 's', better: 'lower', fmt: v => v.toFixed(2) + ' s',\n             wr: [9.48, 'TRB', 'MAX OVERDRIVE'], qualify: { Easy: 12.30, Normal: 11.40, Hard: 10.60 } },\n  points: t => 25.4347 * Math.pow(Math.max(0, 18 - t), 1.81),          // ≈ 0..1250 (WR level ≈ 1100–1250), used by party + hub\n  tune: { vMax: [11.6, 8, 16, .1, 'Top speed (m/s)'], ... },           // [default, min, max, step, label]\n  howto: { goal: 'Fastest to the line wins.', rows: [[['mashL', 'mashR'], 'Alternate to run'], [['action'], 'React to the gun · dip at the line'], [['turbo'], 'Turbo when the flame is full']] },\n  laurel: { id: 'rocket', name: 'ROCKET MAN', text: 'React in 0.120 s or less and win', test: (ctx, a, res) => ... },\n  hub: { ok: true, attempts: 1, seconds: 35 }, attract: { seconds: 18, featured: 'perfect' },\n  build(ctx) {},            // once per scene entry: venue, props, crowd, static data (heavy work: boot steps or here)\n  intro(ctx, t) {},         // optional cinematic (lane introductions); returns true when finished; skippable\n  start(ctx) {},            // per heat / attempt: place athletes, reset per-attempt state\n  ready(ctx, dt) {},        // marks / countdown; returns true when play begins\n  step(ctx, dt) {},         // the simulation: reads ctx.intent(a) for each active athlete; never reads game.input directly\n  bot(ctx, a) {},           // returns an Intent for a CPU/attract/autopilot athlete (skill a.pilot.skill, cheat a.pilot.cheat)\n  done(ctx) {},             // true when the heat / attempt is over\n  perf(ctx, a) {},          // the performance number, or null (DNF / foul / DQ: put the reason in a.notes)\n  draw(ctx, r) {}, hud(ctx, r) {}                                     // skipped headless\n});\n```\n\n**The runner's phases:** `intro` → `ready` → `play` (`step` until `done`) → `finish` (2–3 s celebration, slow-mo,\n\"WORLD RECORD!\" bursts) → `between` (turn card / next round / standings) → back to `start` or → `done` → the flow\ngets the `Results`. `intro` is skipped in hub, attract and on retries; any phase can be jumped to from the dev panel.\n\n**`ctx`** (what the runner gives every hook): `def, meet, game, athletes, humans, active` (those in the current\nheat/attempt), `round, attempt, phase, phaseT, t` (seconds of play), `rng(label)` (namespaced by event and attempt),\n`T` (live tunables of this event: `ctx.T.vMax`), `G` (global tunables), `intent(a)`, `emit(name, data)` (bus: comms,\ncrowd, hype, sfx, laurels, tests listen), `finish(a, perf, notes)`, `dnf(a, why)`, `dq(a, why)`, `slowmo(scale, s)`,\n`cam` helpers, `ghosts`.\n\n**Sims are separable from scenes:** each event's state lives in plain objects created by `start`; `step` only touches\nthem. The runner can create a **sandbox ctx** (no scene, no drawing, its own stream labels) to simulate unseen CPU\nattempts by running `start`/`ready`/`step` with bot pilots until `done` (§5.3). Tests use the same sandbox.\n\n### 5.2 Pilots, intents and the autoplayer\n\n- A **pilot** fills an athlete's `Intent` each step: `human` (from its `game.players[i]` input: `pressed('mashL')`,\n  `down('alt')`, `move()`, pointer for aim), `bot` (from `def.bot(ctx, a)`), `ghost` (replays a recording, §5.9),\n  `net` (a hub ghost: drawn only, never simulated).\n- Mash assist is applied in the human pilot (§2.5): One button → every `mashL`/`mashR` press is reported as the\n  alternation the meter expects; Hold → while either is held, synthesize alternations at 72% of `G.mashRateMax`.\n- **`O.AutoPlayer`** drives a *human* athlete through the real input path: each step it asks `def.bot` for an intent\n  and turns it into `input.tap`/`input.hold` calls on that player's input. Used by the dev \"Autopilot\" cheat and by\n  the scripted playthrough test (so menus, prompts, lockouts and the human pilot all get exercised).\n- Cheats are pilot flags: `cheat: 'perfect'` makes `bot` return frame-perfect inputs and keeps hype full (attract,\n  dev \"God mode\").\n- **Fresh presses only:** a human intent ignores buttons still held from before the current phase began (`Ad`, `Lh`,\n  `Rh`, `X` become true only after a press inside the phase), so Space or ✕ held through the event card never starts\n  a javelin's angle or a dive's tuck.\n\n### 5.3 Formats\n\n| Format | Used by | How the runner plays it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `race` | 100m, 50m Free | one heat, all 8 athletes live (humans in the middle lanes 3–6, CPUs fill) |\n| `attempts` | Javelin (3), Diving (3), Archery (6 arrows as 2 ends), Weightlifting (3), Ski Jump (2), Downhill (1), Bobsled (2) | rounds × athletes in start order. Humans play live. CPU attempts: the **2 most relevant** (current leader, the rival, or whoever can overtake a human) play live as **highlights** at 1.5× game speed (✕ skips to the result); the rest are simulated instantly in a sandbox and appear on the standings board |\n| `program` | Figure Skating | like `attempts` with 1 attempt; CPU programs are simulated (score cards shown in the kiss & cry) |\n| `match` | Curling, Ice Hockey | the event runs its own match vs one CPU (or human) nation; the other placings come from `O.Sim.placings(eventId, nations)` (skill-weighted draws from a stream), so all 8 nations get a rank |\n\nTurn order: humans in join order, CPUs by ascending skill (best last, like a real final). Between rounds the standings\nboard shows the top 4 and every human.\n\n### 5.4 Input widgets (src/12-eventkit.js; each has `update`, `press`/`read` and a 10-foot `draw`)\n\n- **`Mash`** (`window: .5 s`): counts *alternations* (a press of the other button than the last one). `rate` = EMA of\n  alternations per second; a same-button press counts 0.25 and grows `same` (the streak resets on a true\n  alternation). Events map `rate` to power with `power = clamp((rate - G.mashRateMin) / (G.mashRateMax - G.mashRateMin), 0, 1) ** .75`\n  (defaults: `mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5` Hz). HUD: the two glyphs pulsing alternately + a 10-segment rate bar.\n- **`TimingBar`**: a needle sweeping a bar (ping-pong, `hz`), zones `[{ from, to, name, q }]`; `press()` → `{ q, zone }`.\n  Windows scale with difficulty and Timing assist.\n- **`Ring`**: a ring shrinking onto a target ring over `dur`; `press()` → signed error in ms → PERFECT ≤ 60 ms,\n  GOOD ≤ 140 ms (×window scale), else BAD.\n- **`Balance`**: a needle `b ∈ [-1, 1]` with drift `b'' = noise(t) * drift - b' * damp`, corrected by the stick axis\n  (`b' += -axis * k * dt`); out of `[-1, 1]` = lost. Noise from the event's stream (deterministic).\n- **`Sway`**: archery reticle: Lissajous + value noise, amplitude driven by the event (§6.5).\n- **`StrokeBeat`**: swimming: alternating expected buttons on a tempo that follows speed; judged like `Ring`.\n\n### 5.5 Hype and YIKES TURBO\n\n- Each athlete has `hype ∈ [0, 1]`, shown as a **flame meter** beside its name (fills orange → white-hot; full = the\n  turbo glyph flashes: \"△ TURBO!\"). Gains come from the event (perfect starts, perfect timing, clean gates, combos),\n  scaled by `G.hypeGain` (1.0); decay `G.hypeDecay` (0.02/s) when not full.\n- Pressing `turbo` with a full flame fires **YIKES TURBO** for `G.turboTime` (3 s): the event's own effect\n  (listed per event), the athlete bursts into (harmless, cartoon) flames (`particles.fire` at the feet/hands + glow\n  light), the music's `hype` layer fades in (`audio.layer('hype', 1, .3)`), the crowd surges, commentary cue\n  `turbo`. `G.turboPower` (1.0) scales every event's turbo multiplier.\n- CPU bots fire turbo at their event's best moment with probability = skill.\n\n### 5.6 CPU rivals and difficulty\n\n- Every nation's athlete has a skill per event (§7.1). Effective skill = `clamp(skill * G.cpuSkillScale + offset, .05, .99)`\n  with offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06 for Easy / Normal / Hard (all three offsets are dev sliders).\n- Bots play **the same rules through intents** (no pre-rolled results): mash rate, reaction time, timing error,\n  aim error, steering noise, turbo use all derive from skill plus noise from the event's stream. This keeps balance\n  honest and lets tests measure it.\n- The rival (Turbonia's Max Overdrive; if a human picked Turbonia, the CPU nation with the highest average skill) gets\n  +0.03 and always plays live highlights.\n\n### 5.7 Results, qualifying, points, records, medals\n\n- **Ranking** by best performance (`better`), ties by the event's tie rule (stated per event), then by earlier\n  attempt. Nulls (DNF/foul/DQ) rank last in their order.\n- **Medals** to ranks 1–3 (match events: winner gold, loser silver, simulated bronze match).\n- **Qualifying (The Games, 1 player, Qualifying On):** a human result worse than `qualify[difficulty]` → \"YIKES! NO\n  QUALIFYING MARK\" → lose a torch (3 per Games) and retry the event (CPU results stand; the retry replaces yours).\n  0 torches → GAMES OVER → CONTINUE? (10 s countdown): yes restores 3 torches and retries; no → title (records and\n  laurels are kept). Match events have no qualifying check. Multi-human Games default Qualifying Off.\n- **Points** (≈ 0–1250, per event formula; a world-record performance is worth ≈ 1100–1250 in every event): party totals in Quick Games / multi-human Games and the hub score.\n- **Party points** (multi-human): 10 8 6 5 4 3 2 1 by rank among all 8; the overall champion is crowned at the end.\n- **Records:** in-world World Records (seed table in §7.5), Games Records (best ever on this device, `oly:records`),\n  Personal Bests per nation. A beaten WR → \"WORLD RECORD!\" banner, fireworks, WR sting, commentary, the jumbotron.\n  Top-5 tables per event with **initials** (`E.Arcade`: `cab.qualifies`, `cab.enter`, `cab.table`), skipped in hub.\n- **Medal table:** gold, then silver, then bronze, then nation name.\n\n### 5.8 Yikes moments\n\n`O.Yikes.trigger(a, kind, at)`: a giant comic stamp **\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"** (or the kind's own word: \"FALSE START!\",\n\"BELLY FLOP!\", \"BONK!\", \"FOUL!\") with shake, the descending-trombone sting, crowd gasp + \"OOOH\", a commentary cue,\n`yikes[nation]++` (shown at the closing ceremony as the \"Yikes reel\"), and **sympathy hype +0.15** (`G.yikesHype`), so\na comeback is always possible. Reduce-motion keeps the stamp still. Each event lists its yikes kinds; every one must\nbe reachable by ordinary bad play (tests force each).\n\n### 5.9 Ghosts\n\n`O.Ghost.rec(a)` samples `[t, x, y, z, facing, poseCode, extra]` at 20 Hz into a compact array; `O.Ghost.at(track, t)`\ninterpolates; `O.Ghost.draw(ctx, r, state, { tint, name })` draws a translucent rig (`r.actor(..., { alpha: .45 })`\ntinted with the player/seat color) plus a name tag. Uses: the leader's run in Downhill/Bobsled, the previous\nplayer's attempt in turn-based multiplayer, your best local run per event (stored, ≤ 3000 samples), and hub ghosts\n(§12.2) which arrive as the same samples over the network.\n\n### 5.10 Commentary\n\n- Two commentators plus the stadium PA (§7.6): **CHIP BELLOWS** (play-by-play, booming hyperbole), **DAME VERA\n  VELOCITY** (seven-time champion turned colour commentator, dry and sentimental), and the PA announcer (echo).\n- `O.Comms.cue(key, vars, { prio })`: picks a line from the event bank, falling back to the generic bank; never two\n  lines within 3.5 s, each key has a cooldown, higher priority interrupts (WR > yikes > photo finish > lead change >\n  filler). Lines may be two-speaker exchanges.\n- Display: a **lower third** with the speaker's live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, and up to 2 lines of\n  subtitles at scale 2 (Text size Huge = larger), above the prompt strip and clear of the touch area. Voice: `O.Voice`\n  gibberish (§9.3); the portrait's mouth moves while it speaks. Setting \"Commentary\" picks voices+subs / subs / off.\n- Vars: `{name}`, `{nation}`, `{time}`, `{dist}`, `{rival}`, `{place}`.\n\n### 5.11 Crowd, jumbotron, camera, slow-mo\n\n- **Stands** are TileMap tiers (or painted bands in side views) with a crowd painter: one `r.queue` per stand section\n  draws hundreds of 3×5 px spectators (head + shirt in nation colors), bobbing by `O.Crowd.level` (0..1), waving flags,\n  camera-flash glints, doing **the wave** when hype turbo fires or a record falls. The crowd audio follows the same\n  level.\n- **Jumbotron** (stadium, arena, pools): a dot-matrix panel (like the pinball kit's display) showing the event, the\n  clock, the leader, \"WORLD RECORD!\" and a live portrait of the leader.\n- **Camera:** `game.focus` on the human leader (or `cam.frame` on all humans, `zoom: [.6, 1]`) in races; event-\n  specific shots elsewhere. `ctx.slowmo(scale, seconds)` sets `game.timeScale` (photo finish .25, landings .35) and\n  restores it; reduce motion shortens it.\n\n### 5.12 Laurels\n\nOne per event (listed in §6), checked when an attempt ends; awarding shows a toast **\"LAUREL EARNED: ROCKET MAN\"**\nwith a golden laurel sprite, saved in `oly:laurels`, shown in Records → Laurels (12 tiles: earned gold / unearned\noutline with its hint text).\n\n### 5.13 Tuning registry (the dev sliders' data)\n\n`O.tune.def(group, key, [default, min, max, step, label])`, `O.tune.get(group)` → live object (events read `ctx.T.key`\nevery step, so a slider change applies immediately), `O.tune.reset(group?)`, `O.tune.changed()`,\n`O.tune.json()`. Global group `G` (defaults): `cpuSkillScale 1`, `cpuOffsetEasy -.12`, `cpuOffsetNormal 0`,\n`cpuOffsetHard .06`, `windowScale 1`, `hypeGain 1`, `hypeDecay .02`, `turboTime 3`, `turboPower 1`,\n`mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5`, `mashHoldRate .72`, `yikesHype .15`, `slowmoScale .3`, `qualifyScale 1`,\n`gameSpeed 1`. Every event defines **at least 6** of its own (listed per event).\n\n### 5.14 Saves\n\n`O.store` over `E.store`: records, laurels, cabinet (best medal per nation per event), the Games autosave (written\nafter each day's medal table: meet minus runtime objects), best local ghost per event, first-time tips seen. Settings\nare the engine's. Storage blocked → everything still works for the visit. In a hub session the client gives an empty\nstorage (nothing to do).\n\n---\n\n## 6. The twelve events\n\nDay order in The Games alternates seasons: **1 100m Dash (S) · 2 Ski Jump (W) · 3 50m Freestyle (S) · 4 Curling (W) ·\n5 Javelin (S) · 6 Downhill (W) · halftime · 7 Archery (S) · 8 Figure Skating (W) · 9 Weightlifting (S) ·\n10 Bobsled (W) · 11 Diving (S) · 12 Ice Hockey Final (W)**.\n\nNumbers below are **starting values for tuning**, each one a dev slider where marked *(T)*. The *targets* are what\ntests check (§16.3); retune freely as long as the targets hold.\n\n### 6.1 100m DASH — summer · Glory Stadium · mash","numLines":200,"startLine":432,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GbS9HUZ8PUBfcLJiN7W5CE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
