{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2Ysz5D4PS437FfTuFD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U3KZHN5QP3dS183Z9TZPwG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":631,"limit":100},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7224,"cache_read_input_tokens":461555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7224},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"8a2cecc0-8fa5-4a85-bc98-0c1959213f0d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:03.677Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2YskSmxe1hJezubjse","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01U3KZHN5QP3dS183Z9TZPwG":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":631,"limit":100}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U3KZHN5QP3dS183Z9TZPwG","type":"tool_result","content":"631\t### 6.1 100m DASH — summer · Glory Stadium · mash\n632\t\n633\t- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Track along x: start line x = 0, finish x = 1200, run-out to 1500. 8 lanes at\n634\t  y = 20 + (lane−1)·14 (lane 1 nearest the camera). Stands (3 tiers + crowd) behind lane 8, advertising boards\n635\t  (cut low) in front of lane 1, the finish gantry with a clock, the jumbotron at the far end, the blimp above. Day,\n636\t  sunny; `lights` ambient .85 with sun-warm tint.\n637\t- **Format:** race, 8 athletes, 1 heat. Humans in lanes 4, 5, 3, 6.\n638\t- **Flow:** *intro* (camera pans lane 8 → 1 while the PA names each athlete and nation: 6 s, skippable) → \"ON YOUR\n639\t  MARKS\" (athletes crouch in the blocks) → \"SET\" (hips up; the gun comes after `1.0–2.2 s` from `rng('sprint:gun')`) →\n640\t  **BANG** (smoke puff, flash, sound) → race → photo finish → finish.\n641\t- **Reaction:** the first `mashL`/`mashR`/`action` press after the gun starts the athlete; reaction = press − gun.\n642\t  A press between SET and the gun, or a reaction < 0.100 s, is a **FALSE START**: everyone resets; the athlete gets a\n643\t  yellow card; a second one by the same athlete is a **DQ** (result null, note DQ).\n644\t- **Speed:** `vTarget = vMax · power(rate)` (§5.4); `v` approaches it at `accel` 9 m/s² *(T)* up and `decel` 5 m/s²\n645\t  *(T)* down; during the first 30 m accel is ×(0.6 + 0.4·d/30). `vMax` 11.6 m/s *(T)* (139 u/s). Turbo: `vMax` ×1.12\n646\t  *(T)*. Same-button streak 3 → **stumble** (v ×0.85 for 0.3 s); streak 5 → **FACEPLANT** (yikes: roll + down, 1.4 s\n647\t  on the ground, `faceplantTime` *(T)*).\n648\t- **Dip:** `action` within the last 2.5 m starts a lean; the torso (which is what crosses the line) leads by 0.35 m\n649\t  *(T)* if the dip lands in the last 1.2 m; earlier dips cost 10% speed for 0.3 s.\n650\t- **Finish:** time when the torso crosses x = 1200, to 0.001 (shown 0.01). Top two within 0.05 s → **PHOTO FINISH**:\n651\t  slow-mo .25 for 1 s, then a frozen sepia frame with the finish line and the two torsos, then the result.\n652\t- **Scoring:** lower time; ties by thousandths, then reaction. WR **9.48 s (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify Easy 12.30 /\n653\t  Normal 11.40 / Hard 10.60. Points `25.4347·(18 − t)^1.81`.\n654\t- **CPU:** rate `6.5 + 4.2·skill` Hz ± stream noise, reaction `0.24 − 0.11·skill ± .03`, false-start chance 2% (Normal),\n655\t  dip success = skill, turbo at 50 m.\n656\t- **Hype:** reaction < 0.15 s +0.35; each second at > 85% power +0.08; good dip +0.1.\n657\t- **Tunables:** vMax, accel, decel, turboMult, dipLead, faceplantTime, stumbleStreak, falseStartMin (0.100).\n658\t- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, FACEPLANT. **Laurel:** ROCKET MAN (reaction ≤ 0.120 s and win).\n659\t- **HUD:** per human: lane tag, mash-pair prompt pulsing, power bar, hype flame; top-right race clock; split board at\n660\t  50 m (times) on the jumbotron; reaction times shown under each lane after the start.\n661\t- **Targets (tests):** perfect bot 9.40–9.70 s (with turbo ≤ 9.55); skill .9 bot ≈ 9.8–10.2; skill .5 ≈ 10.8–11.4;\n662\t  idle human = DNF after 30 s; a press before the gun = false start; skill .9 beats .3 in ≥ 95% of 40 seeds.\n663\t- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 humans live; **hub:** yes (1 heat, ghosts in lanes).\n664\t\n665\t### 6.2 JAVELIN THROW — summer · Glory Stadium infield · mash + angle\n666\t\n667\t- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Runway x 0 → 360 (30 m), foul line (white arc) at x = 360, landing sector to\n668\t  x = 360 + 1440 (120 m) with lines every 10 m and numbers, the stadium wall at 120 m and a parking lot beyond it.\n669\t  Windsock, distance board, judges with flags. The blimp crosses above (see Over the top).\n670\t- **Format:** attempts × 3 rounds, best counts; ties by second-best.\n671\t- **Flow per attempt:** athlete at x = 0 with the javelin over the shoulder (pose `javCarry`) → run-up (mash, `vMax`\n672\t  9.0 m/s *(T)*) → **hold `action`**: the angle needle rises 0 → 80° at 55°/s *(T)* (and back down if held on,\n673\t  ping-pong) → **release** throws at the current angle → flight → landing → a judge jogs to the mark with a tape\n674\t  (1.2 s) → the distance pops up.\n675\t- **Foul:** crossing x = 360 before release → FOUL (the athlete trips over the line and rolls: yikes), red flag, no mark.\n676\t- **Physics (meters):** release speed `vRel = 13 + 1.9·vRun` m/s *(T coefficients)* at the chosen angle, from 2.0 m up;\n677\t  `a = (0, −9.81) − kD·|v_air|·v_air` with `v_air = v − (wind, 0)`, `kD = 0.0011` *(T)*. Wind per throw from\n678\t  `rng('javelin:wind:<round>:<athlete>')` in −2.0…+3.0 m/s *(T range)*. Tip-first landing requires release angle in\n679\t  20°–60°; outside → **FLAT!** (the javelin bounces, \"BOING\", no mark).\n680\t- **Camera:** follow the athlete; at release `cam.frame([javelin, predictedLanding], { zoom: [.5, 1] })`; slow-mo .35\n681\t  for the last 0.6 s; then a close shot of the javelin quivering in the turf.\n682\t- **Scoring:** higher distance (0.01 m). WR **101.20 m (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 58 / 72 / 82 m. Points\n683\t  `10.14·(d − 7)^1.05` (WR ≈ 1200).\n684\t- **CPU:** run rate by skill; release angle ~ N(38°, 7° − 5°·skill); foul chance (1 − skill)·12%; turbo on the run.\n685\t- **Turbo:** HYPER ARM: release speed ×1.12 *(T)* and the javelin trails fire.\n686\t- **Over the top:** > 120 m → OUT OF THE STADIUM: the javelin clears the wall, a car alarm whoops, the mark is\n687\t  measured at the landing point in the parking lot (counts!). The blimp (at 55–70 m altitude, crossing at a random\n688\t  x per round) can be popped by a steep, fast throw: confetti, \"BLIMP BUSTER!\", the javelin drops and its landing\n689\t  counts.\n690\t- **Tunables:** vMaxRun, angleRate, vRelBase, vRelPerRun, drag, windMax, turboMult.\n691\t- **Yikes:** FOUL!, FLAT!. **Laurel:** OUT OF THE STADIUM (> 120 m).\n692\t- **HUD:** angle gauge (a big quarter-circle dial with a green band 34°–42°), wind (arrow + m/s), run power, best mark,\n693\t  standings strip.\n694\t- **Targets:** perfect bot (38°, full run) 88–93 m; perfect + turbo + 3 m/s tailwind > 120 m possible; skill .5 ≈ 65–75 m;\n695\t  release at 10° → flat; crossing the line → foul.\n696\t- **Multiplayer:** humans alternate (the previous thrower's javelin flight shows as a ghost); **hub:** yes (2 throws).\n697\t\n698\t### 6.3 50m FREESTYLE (short course) — summer · Splash Palace · rhythm + breath\n699\t\n700\t- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. A 25 m pool (x 0 → 300) with 8 lanes 2.5 m wide (30 u), animated water floor\n701\t  (`E.tex.water` + caustics), lane ropes as rows of colored floats, backstroke flags, starting blocks, a deck, stands\n702\t  and big windows to the beach; indoor bright light. 2 lengths with a turn at x = 300.\n703\t- **Flow:** \"TAKE YOUR MARKS\" → beep after `0.8–1.6 s` → **start** (reaction as in the sprint; early = false start) →\n704\t  **dive:** holding `action` 0.2–0.6 s then releasing gives the best glide (4 + 3·q m); holding past 0.75 s →\n705\t  **BELLY FLOP START** (yikes, glide 2 m) → strokes → **turn** → strokes → **touch**.\n706\t- **Strokes (`StrokeBeat`):** expected buttons alternate `mashL`, `mashR` on a beat whose tempo follows speed\n707\t  (`50 + 50·v/vMax` strokes/min). A press within ±70 ms *(T)* of the beat is PERFECT, ±150 ms GOOD, else MISS (wasted,\n708\t  splash, −5% speed); the wrong button is a MISS. Quality `q` = EMA (1.5 s) of 1 / .6 / 0;\n709\t  `vTarget = vMax·(0.45 + 0.55·q)`, `vMax` 2.45 m/s *(T)*.\n710\t- **Breathing:** O2 drains 0.11/s *(T)*; `alt` within 0.25 s after a stroke breathes (+0.45 O2, that stroke ×0.7).\n711\t  O2 < .25 caps strokes at GOOD; O2 = 0 → **GASP!** (yikes: 1.2 s stop, cough, O2 back to .6).\n712\t- **Turn:** inside 1.6 m of the wall the prompt \"✕ TURN\" appears: press at 0.6–1.1 m → PERFECT FLIP TURN (push-off at\n713\t  1.25·vMax, hype +0.2); 1.1–1.6 m early (weak push); < 0.6 m late (normal); not pressed by the wall → **BONK!**\n714\t  (yikes, +1.0 s).\n715\t- **Touch:** `action` within the last 0.8 m reaches (−0.05 s); otherwise an automatic glide-in.\n716\t- **Scoring:** lower time. WR **19.62 s (MARINA SPLASHWORTH, WAV)**. Qualify 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6. Points\n717\t  `18.9·(35 − t)^1.5`.\n718\t- **CPU:** P(perfect) = .35 + .55·skill, P(good) the rest minus a miss rate (1 − skill)·.15; breathes every 3–4\n719\t  strokes; turn quality by skill.\n720\t- **Turbo:** DOLPHIN MODE: 3 s of automatic PERFECT strokes, vMax ×1.1, a cartoon dolphin leaps in the next lane.\n721\t- **Tunables:** vMax, perfectWindow, goodWindow, o2Drain, breathGain, turnPush, diveGlide.\n722\t- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, BELLY FLOP START, GASP!, BONK!. **Laurel:** TORPEDO (reaction < 0.15, perfect dive and\n723\t  perfect turn in one race).\n724\t- **HUD:** per human: the stroke ring with the next expected glyph, O2 bubble meter, hype flame; lap/turn indicator.\n725\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 19.4–19.9 s; skill .5 ≈ 22.5–24; never breathing → at least one GASP; missing the turn →\n726\t  BONK.\n727\t- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 live; **hub:** yes.\n728\t\n729\t### 6.4 10m PLATFORM DIVING — summer · Splash Palace · tricks + entry timing\n730\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"3595a040-7d49-47b9-b5f4-ebb5b1319e29","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:03.684Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 6.1 100m DASH — summer · Glory Stadium · mash\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Track along x: start line x = 0, finish x = 1200, run-out to 1500. 8 lanes at\n  y = 20 + (lane−1)·14 (lane 1 nearest the camera). Stands (3 tiers + crowd) behind lane 8, advertising boards\n  (cut low) in front of lane 1, the finish gantry with a clock, the jumbotron at the far end, the blimp above. Day,\n  sunny; `lights` ambient .85 with sun-warm tint.\n- **Format:** race, 8 athletes, 1 heat. Humans in lanes 4, 5, 3, 6.\n- **Flow:** *intro* (camera pans lane 8 → 1 while the PA names each athlete and nation: 6 s, skippable) → \"ON YOUR\n  MARKS\" (athletes crouch in the blocks) → \"SET\" (hips up; the gun comes after `1.0–2.2 s` from `rng('sprint:gun')`) →\n  **BANG** (smoke puff, flash, sound) → race → photo finish → finish.\n- **Reaction:** the first `mashL`/`mashR`/`action` press after the gun starts the athlete; reaction = press − gun.\n  A press between SET and the gun, or a reaction < 0.100 s, is a **FALSE START**: everyone resets; the athlete gets a\n  yellow card; a second one by the same athlete is a **DQ** (result null, note DQ).\n- **Speed:** `vTarget = vMax · power(rate)` (§5.4); `v` approaches it at `accel` 9 m/s² *(T)* up and `decel` 5 m/s²\n  *(T)* down; during the first 30 m accel is ×(0.6 + 0.4·d/30). `vMax` 11.6 m/s *(T)* (139 u/s). Turbo: `vMax` ×1.12\n  *(T)*. Same-button streak 3 → **stumble** (v ×0.85 for 0.3 s); streak 5 → **FACEPLANT** (yikes: roll + down, 1.4 s\n  on the ground, `faceplantTime` *(T)*).\n- **Dip:** `action` within the last 2.5 m starts a lean; the torso (which is what crosses the line) leads by 0.35 m\n  *(T)* if the dip lands in the last 1.2 m; earlier dips cost 10% speed for 0.3 s.\n- **Finish:** time when the torso crosses x = 1200, to 0.001 (shown 0.01). Top two within 0.05 s → **PHOTO FINISH**:\n  slow-mo .25 for 1 s, then a frozen sepia frame with the finish line and the two torsos, then the result.\n- **Scoring:** lower time; ties by thousandths, then reaction. WR **9.48 s (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify Easy 12.30 /\n  Normal 11.40 / Hard 10.60. Points `25.4347·(18 − t)^1.81`.\n- **CPU:** rate `6.5 + 4.2·skill` Hz ± stream noise, reaction `0.24 − 0.11·skill ± .03`, false-start chance 2% (Normal),\n  dip success = skill, turbo at 50 m.\n- **Hype:** reaction < 0.15 s +0.35; each second at > 85% power +0.08; good dip +0.1.\n- **Tunables:** vMax, accel, decel, turboMult, dipLead, faceplantTime, stumbleStreak, falseStartMin (0.100).\n- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, FACEPLANT. **Laurel:** ROCKET MAN (reaction ≤ 0.120 s and win).\n- **HUD:** per human: lane tag, mash-pair prompt pulsing, power bar, hype flame; top-right race clock; split board at\n  50 m (times) on the jumbotron; reaction times shown under each lane after the start.\n- **Targets (tests):** perfect bot 9.40–9.70 s (with turbo ≤ 9.55); skill .9 bot ≈ 9.8–10.2; skill .5 ≈ 10.8–11.4;\n  idle human = DNF after 30 s; a press before the gun = false start; skill .9 beats .3 in ≥ 95% of 40 seeds.\n- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 humans live; **hub:** yes (1 heat, ghosts in lanes).\n\n### 6.2 JAVELIN THROW — summer · Glory Stadium infield · mash + angle\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Runway x 0 → 360 (30 m), foul line (white arc) at x = 360, landing sector to\n  x = 360 + 1440 (120 m) with lines every 10 m and numbers, the stadium wall at 120 m and a parking lot beyond it.\n  Windsock, distance board, judges with flags. The blimp crosses above (see Over the top).\n- **Format:** attempts × 3 rounds, best counts; ties by second-best.\n- **Flow per attempt:** athlete at x = 0 with the javelin over the shoulder (pose `javCarry`) → run-up (mash, `vMax`\n  9.0 m/s *(T)*) → **hold `action`**: the angle needle rises 0 → 80° at 55°/s *(T)* (and back down if held on,\n  ping-pong) → **release** throws at the current angle → flight → landing → a judge jogs to the mark with a tape\n  (1.2 s) → the distance pops up.\n- **Foul:** crossing x = 360 before release → FOUL (the athlete trips over the line and rolls: yikes), red flag, no mark.\n- **Physics (meters):** release speed `vRel = 13 + 1.9·vRun` m/s *(T coefficients)* at the chosen angle, from 2.0 m up;\n  `a = (0, −9.81) − kD·|v_air|·v_air` with `v_air = v − (wind, 0)`, `kD = 0.0011` *(T)*. Wind per throw from\n  `rng('javelin:wind:<round>:<athlete>')` in −2.0…+3.0 m/s *(T range)*. Tip-first landing requires release angle in\n  20°–60°; outside → **FLAT!** (the javelin bounces, \"BOING\", no mark).\n- **Camera:** follow the athlete; at release `cam.frame([javelin, predictedLanding], { zoom: [.5, 1] })`; slow-mo .35\n  for the last 0.6 s; then a close shot of the javelin quivering in the turf.\n- **Scoring:** higher distance (0.01 m). WR **101.20 m (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 58 / 72 / 82 m. Points\n  `10.14·(d − 7)^1.05` (WR ≈ 1200).\n- **CPU:** run rate by skill; release angle ~ N(38°, 7° − 5°·skill); foul chance (1 − skill)·12%; turbo on the run.\n- **Turbo:** HYPER ARM: release speed ×1.12 *(T)* and the javelin trails fire.\n- **Over the top:** > 120 m → OUT OF THE STADIUM: the javelin clears the wall, a car alarm whoops, the mark is\n  measured at the landing point in the parking lot (counts!). The blimp (at 55–70 m altitude, crossing at a random\n  x per round) can be popped by a steep, fast throw: confetti, \"BLIMP BUSTER!\", the javelin drops and its landing\n  counts.\n- **Tunables:** vMaxRun, angleRate, vRelBase, vRelPerRun, drag, windMax, turboMult.\n- **Yikes:** FOUL!, FLAT!. **Laurel:** OUT OF THE STADIUM (> 120 m).\n- **HUD:** angle gauge (a big quarter-circle dial with a green band 34°–42°), wind (arrow + m/s), run power, best mark,\n  standings strip.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot (38°, full run) 88–93 m; perfect + turbo + 3 m/s tailwind > 120 m possible; skill .5 ≈ 65–75 m;\n  release at 10° → flat; crossing the line → foul.\n- **Multiplayer:** humans alternate (the previous thrower's javelin flight shows as a ghost); **hub:** yes (2 throws).\n\n### 6.3 50m FREESTYLE (short course) — summer · Splash Palace · rhythm + breath\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. A 25 m pool (x 0 → 300) with 8 lanes 2.5 m wide (30 u), animated water floor\n  (`E.tex.water` + caustics), lane ropes as rows of colored floats, backstroke flags, starting blocks, a deck, stands\n  and big windows to the beach; indoor bright light. 2 lengths with a turn at x = 300.\n- **Flow:** \"TAKE YOUR MARKS\" → beep after `0.8–1.6 s` → **start** (reaction as in the sprint; early = false start) →\n  **dive:** holding `action` 0.2–0.6 s then releasing gives the best glide (4 + 3·q m); holding past 0.75 s →\n  **BELLY FLOP START** (yikes, glide 2 m) → strokes → **turn** → strokes → **touch**.\n- **Strokes (`StrokeBeat`):** expected buttons alternate `mashL`, `mashR` on a beat whose tempo follows speed\n  (`50 + 50·v/vMax` strokes/min). A press within ±70 ms *(T)* of the beat is PERFECT, ±150 ms GOOD, else MISS (wasted,\n  splash, −5% speed); the wrong button is a MISS. Quality `q` = EMA (1.5 s) of 1 / .6 / 0;\n  `vTarget = vMax·(0.45 + 0.55·q)`, `vMax` 2.45 m/s *(T)*.\n- **Breathing:** O2 drains 0.11/s *(T)*; `alt` within 0.25 s after a stroke breathes (+0.45 O2, that stroke ×0.7).\n  O2 < .25 caps strokes at GOOD; O2 = 0 → **GASP!** (yikes: 1.2 s stop, cough, O2 back to .6).\n- **Turn:** inside 1.6 m of the wall the prompt \"✕ TURN\" appears: press at 0.6–1.1 m → PERFECT FLIP TURN (push-off at\n  1.25·vMax, hype +0.2); 1.1–1.6 m early (weak push); < 0.6 m late (normal); not pressed by the wall → **BONK!**\n  (yikes, +1.0 s).\n- **Touch:** `action` within the last 0.8 m reaches (−0.05 s); otherwise an automatic glide-in.\n- **Scoring:** lower time. WR **19.62 s (MARINA SPLASHWORTH, WAV)**. Qualify 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6. Points\n  `18.9·(35 − t)^1.5`.\n- **CPU:** P(perfect) = .35 + .55·skill, P(good) the rest minus a miss rate (1 − skill)·.15; breathes every 3–4\n  strokes; turn quality by skill.\n- **Turbo:** DOLPHIN MODE: 3 s of automatic PERFECT strokes, vMax ×1.1, a cartoon dolphin leaps in the next lane.\n- **Tunables:** vMax, perfectWindow, goodWindow, o2Drain, breathGain, turnPush, diveGlide.\n- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, BELLY FLOP START, GASP!, BONK!. **Laurel:** TORPEDO (reaction < 0.15, perfect dive and\n  perfect turn in one race).\n- **HUD:** per human: the stroke ring with the next expected glyph, O2 bubble meter, hype flame; lap/turn indicator.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 19.4–19.9 s; skill .5 ≈ 22.5–24; never breathing → at least one GASP; missing the turn →\n  BONK.\n- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 live; **hub:** yes.\n\n### 6.4 10m PLATFORM DIVING — summer · Splash Palace · tricks + entry timing\n","numLines":100,"startLine":631,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U3KZHN5QP3dS183Z9TZPwG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
