{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FGe9zET8VHfgjE1gDkwAed","type":"tool_result","content":"729\t### 6.4 10m PLATFORM DIVING — summer · Splash Palace · tricks + entry timing\n730\t\n731\t- **View:** `'side'`, M = 12. Tower at the left (platforms at 1, 3, 5, 7.5, 10 m; the 10 m edge at x = 30, z = 120),\n732\t  pool cross-section below (surface z = 0, depth to z = −60 drawn translucent with light shafts and bubbles), the 5\n733\t  judges' table, the scoreboard, stands. Camera frames the diver and the water; slow-mo .35 at entry.\n734\t- **Format:** 3 rounds; each round the diver picks 1 of 3 dives (one easy, one medium, one hard, never repeating a\n735\t  dive). Total = sum of dive scores.\n736\t- **Dive list:** Forward 2½ Pike (105B, DD 2.8, 5 half-somersaults, pike); Back 2½ Tuck (205C, DD 3.0, 5, tuck, back\n737\t  take-off); Forward 3½ Tuck (107C, DD 3.3, 7, tuck); Inward 3½ Tuck (407C, DD 3.2, 7, tuck); Forward 2½ with 2 Twists\n738\t  Pike (5154B, DD 3.6, 5 half-somersaults + 4 half-twists); **YIKES! Armstand Quintuple** (DD 4.8, 10, tuck: the\n739\t  over-the-top dive).\n740\t- **Take-off:** `TimingBar` (1.4 Hz): `vz = 4.2 + 1.6·q` m/s up, `vx = 1.0` m/s; airtime ≈ 1.9–2.1 s.\n741\t- **In the air:** hold `mashL` = TUCK (ω 12.5 rad/s *(T)*), hold `mashR` = PIKE (ω 9 rad/s *(T)*), neither = OPEN\n742\t  (1.5 rad/s *(T)*). A dial shows half-somersaults done vs required. Twist dives: each tap ←/→ while open or piked\n743\t  adds a half twist (0.25 s each). The body rotation is drawn with the Pose module's `bodyPitch` (+ yaw for twists).\n744\t- **Entry judgement:** at the surface, error `e` = |body angle − vertical (head first)| in degrees: ≤ 8 RIP (no\n745\t  splash) base 9.5; ≤ 15 → 8.5; ≤ 25 → 7.0; ≤ 45 → 5.0; ≤ 75 → 3.0; > 75 → **BELLY FLOP / BACK SLAP** (yikes) 1.0.\n746\t  Adjust: take-off +0…+0.5; wrong position −1.0; each missing/extra half-somersault −2.0; each missing half-twist −1.5;\n747\t  judge noise ±0.5 per judge from `rng('judges:...')`; clamp 0–10, round to 0.5. 5 judges, drop high and low,\n748\t  dive score = middle three × DD.\n749\t- **Scoring:** higher total. WR **338.40 (COCO BONBON, BON)** (the maximum possible is 351: three perfect dives of DD 4.8, 3.6, 3.3). Qualify 150 / 195 / 240. Points `3.4·total`.\n750\t- **CPU:** take-off q ~ skill; release error σ = (1 − skill)·35°; picks hard dives when skill > .8.\n751\t- **Turbo:** SLOW-MO SUPREMACY: time ×0.5 for 2.5 s of the dive (more control), sparkle trail.\n752\t- **Tunables:** tuckSpin, pikeSpin, openSpin, takeoffVz, ripTolerance, judgeNoise, twistTime.\n753\t- **Yikes:** BELLY FLOP (the judges hold up 0.5 cards; the splash soaks them), WRONG WAY (back slap). **Laurel:**\n754\t  PERFECT 10s (all five judges 10).\n755\t- **HUD:** dive name + DD, rotation dial, position prompt (glyph □ TUCK / ○ PIKE), twist counter, judges' cards on\n756\t  entry.\n757\t- **Targets:** perfect bot on the 4.8 dive → five 10s (score ≥ 140); skill .5 average ≈ 60–70 per dive; holding tuck\n758\t  to the water from a 2½ → over-rotation penalty or belly flop.\n759\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate; **hub:** yes (2 dives, the options dealt from `AIHub.rng`).\n760\t\n761\t### 6.5 ARCHERY — summer · Bullseye Lawn (seaside) · aim under sway\n762\t\n763\t- **View:** main = the **target close-up** (a 122 cm face, 10 rings + X, drawn ~200 px across: readable at 10 feet);\n764\t  inset (bottom-left, ~30% height) = the archer in `'side'` view at the line drawing the bow, palm trees and the sea\n765\t  behind, wind flags. During flight the inset shows the arrow leaving; the target view zooms 1.1× toward the impact.\n766\t- **Format:** attempts: 6 arrows in 2 ends of 3 (a 20 s shot clock per arrow; 12 s in hub heats). Score 0–60; ties by X count, then 10s.\n767\t- **Draw:** hold `action` 0.9 s *(T)* to full draw (string tension bar). Release before full draw → weak arrow\n768\t  (25 cm low + spread).\n769\t- **Aim:** stick/WASD moves the aim at 40 cm/s *(T)*; mouse: the pointer sets the aim directly. **Sway** adds\n770\t  `A·(sin 1.3t·cos 0.7t, sin(1.7t + 1))` + value noise, `A = A0·(1 + 0.6·max(0, held − 2.5 s))·hr`, `A0` 7 cm *(T)*,\n771\t  heart rate `hr` 1.0 → 1.6 (rises after a bad arrow and on the final arrow of the match).\n772\t- **Hold breath:** hold `alt` (L, R2 or right mouse) at full draw: sway ×0.25 for up to 2.5 s *(T)*; when the breath\n773\t  bar empties, sway ×2 for 2 s (gasping).\n774\t- **Wind:** per arrow from `rng('archery:wind:<n>')` in −4…+4 m/s; impact shift 4.5 cm per m/s *(T)* sideways. Shown\n775\t  as a flag, an arrow and a number. Aim off to compensate.\n776\t- **Release:** let go of `action` at full draw → flight 0.75 s → impact = aim + sway at release + wind shift + release\n777\t  jitter (more if the aim was moving) → ring score; X ring → \"BULLSEYE!\". An impact within 1.0 cm of an earlier arrow\n778\t  → **ROBIN HOOD** (the old arrow splits; same score).\n779\t- **Scoring:** WR **60 (6 X) — PIXEL VANCE (NEO)**. Qualify 40 / 48 / 53. Points `20·score`.\n780\t- **CPU:** aim error σ = (1 − skill)·12 + 2 cm, wind compensation accuracy = skill; CPU arrows show on a mini target\n781\t  on the standings board.\n782\t- **Turbo:** EAGLE EYE: game time ×0.4 and sway ×0.1 for 3 s of real time.\n783\t- **Tunables:** drawTime, swayA0, swayGrowth, breathTime, windMax, windShift.\n784\t- **Yikes:** STRING SLAP (releasing while gasping: \"OW!\", the arrow flies wide). **Laurel:** ROBIN HOOD.\n785\t- **Targets:** perfect bot = 60; a no-breath, no-wind-compensation bot at 4 m/s wind averages < 8 per arrow.\n786\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate per arrow; **hub:** yes (3 arrows, 12 s shot clock).\n787\t\n788\t### 6.6 WEIGHTLIFTING (clean & jerk) — summer · Iron Hall · mash + balance + timing\n789\t\n790\t- **View:** `'brawler'`; the lifter (bulky build, singlet, belt, chalked hands) faces the camera on a wooden platform;\n791\t  spotlights in a dark hall (`lights` ambient .35 + two warm spots); 3 referees with white/red lights; the bar bends\n792\t  with load; plates colored by mass (25 red, 20 blue, 15 yellow, 10 green, 5 white, 2.5 black, collars). Chalk dust.\n793\t- **Format:** attempts × 3. Pick the opening weight from 5 offered (Normal 200/210/220/230/240 kg), then +5 / +10 / +15\n794\t  for the next; the third attempt may take the **YIKES BAR** (WR + 10 kg). Best good lift counts; ties: lighter\n795\t  bodyweight is skipped, earlier success wins.\n796\t- **Load factor** `w = (kg − 150)/120`.\n797\t- **CLEAN (4.0 s *(T)*):** bar height `h` 0 → 1 (floor → shoulders): `h += (rate − 0.7·rReq)·0.12·dt` *(T)*,\n798\t  `rReq = 5.5 + 4.5·w` Hz; the bar sinks if rate < 0.5·rReq; time out → no lift.\n799\t- **RACK:** `Balance` (drift ×(1 + w)); keep |b| < .35 for 1.2 s *(T)*; |b| > 1 → drop.\n800\t- **JERK:** `Ring` (0.9 s): PERFECT → overhead wobble ×0.5; GOOD ×1; BAD → 50% fail, else wobble ×1.8.\n801\t- **HOLD:** `Balance` overhead for 2.0 s *(T)*, drift grows with w → three white lights \"GOOD LIFT!\" (a WR cracks the\n802\t  floor), else the bar drops.\n803\t- **Scoring:** WR **270 kg (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 200 / 225 / 245 kg. Points `min(1200, 9.5·(kg − 150))`.\n804\t- **CPU:** success probability `1/(1 + e^((kg − (190 + 80·skill))/6))`; picks weights like a cautious coach.\n805\t- **Turbo:** IRON WILL: balance drift ×0.2 and lift power ×1.4 for 3 s.\n806\t- **Tunables:** cleanTime, liftGain, rReqBase, rReqPerW, rackTime, holdTime, driftBase.\n807\t- **Yikes:** DROP (the bar bounces twice and the lifter sits down hard, \"OOF\"). **Laurel:** YIKES WEIGHT (lift the\n808\t  YIKES BAR).\n809\t- **HUD:** big kg number, phase name, the mash pair, the balance needle (huge, center-bottom), the jerk ring, the 3\n810\t  lights.\n811\t- **Targets:** perfect bot lifts 280; skill .5 tops out ≈ 220–230; idle → no lift; |b| > 1 → drop.\n812\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate attempts; **hub:** yes (2 attempts: 220 then 240 kg).\n813\t\n814\t### 6.7 SKI JUMP (large hill, K-125, HS-140) — winter · Mount Glory Jumping Hill · timing + flight balance\n815\t\n816\t- **View:** `'side'`, **M = 8** (the hill is big). Night, floodlights (`lights.add` along the in-run and the landing\n817\t  hill), light snow (`game.weather = { kind: 'snow', amount: .3 }`), alpine backdrop (custom `E.Backdrop` layers:\n818\t  mountains, pine forest, a starry sky), the jump tower, the K-point and HS lines, distance boards every 10 m,\n819\t  cowbell crowd and flags in the out-run.\n820\t- **Hill profile (meters, origin at the take-off edge):** in-run 95 m at 35° from the start gate, table −11°; landing\n821\t  hill: knoll `z = −3·(x/15)²` for x < 15, then a 30° slope `z = −3 − 0.58·(x − 15)` to x = 125, then easing out with\n822\t  `+0.0045·(x − 125)²` into the flat out-run. Distance is measured along the slope from the edge (precompute a\n823\t  polyline with arc lengths).\n824\t- **Format:** attempts × 2 jumps. Score per jump = distance points + style points.\n825\t- **Flow:** start gate (`action` pushes off) → **in-run:** a `Balance` needle on ↑/↓ (keep the tuck): speed ×(0.94…1.0)\n826\t  by average balance quality; `a = g·sin35° − μ·g·cos35° − kAir·v²` (μ .02, kAir .0016 *(T)*) → ≈ 25.5 m/s at the\n827\t  table with a perfect tuck. → **take-off:** press `action` in the last 4 m before the edge: last 1.0 m q = 1, 1–2.5 m\n828\t  .7, 2.5–4 m .4; no press → **FELL OFF THE TABLE** (q .1, yikes hop). Adds `vz += 2.4·q` m/s. → **flight:** body\n829\t  angle α (to the airflow) changed by ↑/↓ at 40°/s; gusts from `rng('skijump:gust')` push α; lift `aL = cL(α)·v²`\n830\t  (⊥ velocity), drag `aD = cD(α)·v²`, with `cL(α) = cL0·max(.1, 1 − ((α − 12)/30)²)`, `cL0` .00095 *(T)*,\n831\t  `cD(α) = .0006 + .00002·α` *(T)*. → **landing:** within 2.5 m above the slope the prompt \"✕ TELEMARK!\" appears;\n832\t  press within 0.35 s before contact → telemark; later/none → two-footed; landing with |α| > 40° *(T)*, or beyond\n833\t  HS + 10 m without a telemark → **CRASH** (tumble down the out-run: Pose tumble, skis fly as sprites, snow spray).\n834\t- **Scoring:** distance points `60 + (d − 125)·1.8`; style: 5 judges, telemark 17.5–19.5, two-footed 15–17, crash 6–9\n835\t  (minus wobble in flight), drop high/low, sum 3 (max 60). Event = 2 jumps. Hill record **148.0 m (INGRID\n836\t  SNOWCASTLE, FRM)**, event WR **296.4**. Qualify 160 / 210 / 245 (2-jump total). Points `3.9·total`.\n837\t- **CPU:** balance and take-off q by skill, flight α error (1 − skill)·15°, telemark chance = skill.\n838\t- **Turbo:** ROCKET SKIS: lift ×1.1 and +3 m/s² thrust for 2 s, flames from the ski tails.\n839\t- **Tunables:** kAir, takeoffBoost, cL0, cDBase, gust, telemarkWindow, crashAngle.\n840\t- **Yikes:** FELL OFF THE TABLE, CRASH. **Laurel:** OFF THE CHART (land > 150 m without crashing).\n841\t- **HUD:** speed (km/h) in the in-run, take-off zone bar, the flight angle gauge (a skier silhouette rotating over a\n842\t  green band), distance counter following the jumper, telemark prompt, judges' style cards.\n843\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 132–140 m; perfect + turbo ≥ 150 m; skill .5 ≈ 112–122 m; no take-off press → < 80 m.\n844\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate jumps; **hub:** yes (1 jump).\n845\t\n846\t### 6.8 DOWNHILL — winter · \"The Yikes Face\" · steering + tuck + gates\n847\t\n848\t- **View:** pseudo-3D `E.Road` (`segment: 200`, 1 m = 100 road units; `width: 1600`, `lanes: 0`, `draw: 220`), the"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"e474a64c-f55d-43da-b151-73aef1bbd305","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:15.358Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 6.4 10m PLATFORM DIVING — summer · Splash Palace · tricks + entry timing\n\n- **View:** `'side'`, M = 12. Tower at the left (platforms at 1, 3, 5, 7.5, 10 m; the 10 m edge at x = 30, z = 120),\n  pool cross-section below (surface z = 0, depth to z = −60 drawn translucent with light shafts and bubbles), the 5\n  judges' table, the scoreboard, stands. Camera frames the diver and the water; slow-mo .35 at entry.\n- **Format:** 3 rounds; each round the diver picks 1 of 3 dives (one easy, one medium, one hard, never repeating a\n  dive). Total = sum of dive scores.\n- **Dive list:** Forward 2½ Pike (105B, DD 2.8, 5 half-somersaults, pike); Back 2½ Tuck (205C, DD 3.0, 5, tuck, back\n  take-off); Forward 3½ Tuck (107C, DD 3.3, 7, tuck); Inward 3½ Tuck (407C, DD 3.2, 7, tuck); Forward 2½ with 2 Twists\n  Pike (5154B, DD 3.6, 5 half-somersaults + 4 half-twists); **YIKES! Armstand Quintuple** (DD 4.8, 10, tuck: the\n  over-the-top dive).\n- **Take-off:** `TimingBar` (1.4 Hz): `vz = 4.2 + 1.6·q` m/s up, `vx = 1.0` m/s; airtime ≈ 1.9–2.1 s.\n- **In the air:** hold `mashL` = TUCK (ω 12.5 rad/s *(T)*), hold `mashR` = PIKE (ω 9 rad/s *(T)*), neither = OPEN\n  (1.5 rad/s *(T)*). A dial shows half-somersaults done vs required. Twist dives: each tap ←/→ while open or piked\n  adds a half twist (0.25 s each). The body rotation is drawn with the Pose module's `bodyPitch` (+ yaw for twists).\n- **Entry judgement:** at the surface, error `e` = |body angle − vertical (head first)| in degrees: ≤ 8 RIP (no\n  splash) base 9.5; ≤ 15 → 8.5; ≤ 25 → 7.0; ≤ 45 → 5.0; ≤ 75 → 3.0; > 75 → **BELLY FLOP / BACK SLAP** (yikes) 1.0.\n  Adjust: take-off +0…+0.5; wrong position −1.0; each missing/extra half-somersault −2.0; each missing half-twist −1.5;\n  judge noise ±0.5 per judge from `rng('judges:...')`; clamp 0–10, round to 0.5. 5 judges, drop high and low,\n  dive score = middle three × DD.\n- **Scoring:** higher total. WR **338.40 (COCO BONBON, BON)** (the maximum possible is 351: three perfect dives of DD 4.8, 3.6, 3.3). Qualify 150 / 195 / 240. Points `3.4·total`.\n- **CPU:** take-off q ~ skill; release error σ = (1 − skill)·35°; picks hard dives when skill > .8.\n- **Turbo:** SLOW-MO SUPREMACY: time ×0.5 for 2.5 s of the dive (more control), sparkle trail.\n- **Tunables:** tuckSpin, pikeSpin, openSpin, takeoffVz, ripTolerance, judgeNoise, twistTime.\n- **Yikes:** BELLY FLOP (the judges hold up 0.5 cards; the splash soaks them), WRONG WAY (back slap). **Laurel:**\n  PERFECT 10s (all five judges 10).\n- **HUD:** dive name + DD, rotation dial, position prompt (glyph □ TUCK / ○ PIKE), twist counter, judges' cards on\n  entry.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot on the 4.8 dive → five 10s (score ≥ 140); skill .5 average ≈ 60–70 per dive; holding tuck\n  to the water from a 2½ → over-rotation penalty or belly flop.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate; **hub:** yes (2 dives, the options dealt from `AIHub.rng`).\n\n### 6.5 ARCHERY — summer · Bullseye Lawn (seaside) · aim under sway\n\n- **View:** main = the **target close-up** (a 122 cm face, 10 rings + X, drawn ~200 px across: readable at 10 feet);\n  inset (bottom-left, ~30% height) = the archer in `'side'` view at the line drawing the bow, palm trees and the sea\n  behind, wind flags. During flight the inset shows the arrow leaving; the target view zooms 1.1× toward the impact.\n- **Format:** attempts: 6 arrows in 2 ends of 3 (a 20 s shot clock per arrow; 12 s in hub heats). Score 0–60; ties by X count, then 10s.\n- **Draw:** hold `action` 0.9 s *(T)* to full draw (string tension bar). Release before full draw → weak arrow\n  (25 cm low + spread).\n- **Aim:** stick/WASD moves the aim at 40 cm/s *(T)*; mouse: the pointer sets the aim directly. **Sway** adds\n  `A·(sin 1.3t·cos 0.7t, sin(1.7t + 1))` + value noise, `A = A0·(1 + 0.6·max(0, held − 2.5 s))·hr`, `A0` 7 cm *(T)*,\n  heart rate `hr` 1.0 → 1.6 (rises after a bad arrow and on the final arrow of the match).\n- **Hold breath:** hold `alt` (L, R2 or right mouse) at full draw: sway ×0.25 for up to 2.5 s *(T)*; when the breath\n  bar empties, sway ×2 for 2 s (gasping).\n- **Wind:** per arrow from `rng('archery:wind:<n>')` in −4…+4 m/s; impact shift 4.5 cm per m/s *(T)* sideways. Shown\n  as a flag, an arrow and a number. Aim off to compensate.\n- **Release:** let go of `action` at full draw → flight 0.75 s → impact = aim + sway at release + wind shift + release\n  jitter (more if the aim was moving) → ring score; X ring → \"BULLSEYE!\". An impact within 1.0 cm of an earlier arrow\n  → **ROBIN HOOD** (the old arrow splits; same score).\n- **Scoring:** WR **60 (6 X) — PIXEL VANCE (NEO)**. Qualify 40 / 48 / 53. Points `20·score`.\n- **CPU:** aim error σ = (1 − skill)·12 + 2 cm, wind compensation accuracy = skill; CPU arrows show on a mini target\n  on the standings board.\n- **Turbo:** EAGLE EYE: game time ×0.4 and sway ×0.1 for 3 s of real time.\n- **Tunables:** drawTime, swayA0, swayGrowth, breathTime, windMax, windShift.\n- **Yikes:** STRING SLAP (releasing while gasping: \"OW!\", the arrow flies wide). **Laurel:** ROBIN HOOD.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot = 60; a no-breath, no-wind-compensation bot at 4 m/s wind averages < 8 per arrow.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate per arrow; **hub:** yes (3 arrows, 12 s shot clock).\n\n### 6.6 WEIGHTLIFTING (clean & jerk) — summer · Iron Hall · mash + balance + timing\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`; the lifter (bulky build, singlet, belt, chalked hands) faces the camera on a wooden platform;\n  spotlights in a dark hall (`lights` ambient .35 + two warm spots); 3 referees with white/red lights; the bar bends\n  with load; plates colored by mass (25 red, 20 blue, 15 yellow, 10 green, 5 white, 2.5 black, collars). Chalk dust.\n- **Format:** attempts × 3. Pick the opening weight from 5 offered (Normal 200/210/220/230/240 kg), then +5 / +10 / +15\n  for the next; the third attempt may take the **YIKES BAR** (WR + 10 kg). Best good lift counts; ties: lighter\n  bodyweight is skipped, earlier success wins.\n- **Load factor** `w = (kg − 150)/120`.\n- **CLEAN (4.0 s *(T)*):** bar height `h` 0 → 1 (floor → shoulders): `h += (rate − 0.7·rReq)·0.12·dt` *(T)*,\n  `rReq = 5.5 + 4.5·w` Hz; the bar sinks if rate < 0.5·rReq; time out → no lift.\n- **RACK:** `Balance` (drift ×(1 + w)); keep |b| < .35 for 1.2 s *(T)*; |b| > 1 → drop.\n- **JERK:** `Ring` (0.9 s): PERFECT → overhead wobble ×0.5; GOOD ×1; BAD → 50% fail, else wobble ×1.8.\n- **HOLD:** `Balance` overhead for 2.0 s *(T)*, drift grows with w → three white lights \"GOOD LIFT!\" (a WR cracks the\n  floor), else the bar drops.\n- **Scoring:** WR **270 kg (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 200 / 225 / 245 kg. Points `min(1200, 9.5·(kg − 150))`.\n- **CPU:** success probability `1/(1 + e^((kg − (190 + 80·skill))/6))`; picks weights like a cautious coach.\n- **Turbo:** IRON WILL: balance drift ×0.2 and lift power ×1.4 for 3 s.\n- **Tunables:** cleanTime, liftGain, rReqBase, rReqPerW, rackTime, holdTime, driftBase.\n- **Yikes:** DROP (the bar bounces twice and the lifter sits down hard, \"OOF\"). **Laurel:** YIKES WEIGHT (lift the\n  YIKES BAR).\n- **HUD:** big kg number, phase name, the mash pair, the balance needle (huge, center-bottom), the jerk ring, the 3\n  lights.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot lifts 280; skill .5 tops out ≈ 220–230; idle → no lift; |b| > 1 → drop.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate attempts; **hub:** yes (2 attempts: 220 then 240 kg).\n\n### 6.7 SKI JUMP (large hill, K-125, HS-140) — winter · Mount Glory Jumping Hill · timing + flight balance\n\n- **View:** `'side'`, **M = 8** (the hill is big). Night, floodlights (`lights.add` along the in-run and the landing\n  hill), light snow (`game.weather = { kind: 'snow', amount: .3 }`), alpine backdrop (custom `E.Backdrop` layers:\n  mountains, pine forest, a starry sky), the jump tower, the K-point and HS lines, distance boards every 10 m,\n  cowbell crowd and flags in the out-run.\n- **Hill profile (meters, origin at the take-off edge):** in-run 95 m at 35° from the start gate, table −11°; landing\n  hill: knoll `z = −3·(x/15)²` for x < 15, then a 30° slope `z = −3 − 0.58·(x − 15)` to x = 125, then easing out with\n  `+0.0045·(x − 125)²` into the flat out-run. Distance is measured along the slope from the edge (precompute a\n  polyline with arc lengths).\n- **Format:** attempts × 2 jumps. Score per jump = distance points + style points.\n- **Flow:** start gate (`action` pushes off) → **in-run:** a `Balance` needle on ↑/↓ (keep the tuck): speed ×(0.94…1.0)\n  by average balance quality; `a = g·sin35° − μ·g·cos35° − kAir·v²` (μ .02, kAir .0016 *(T)*) → ≈ 25.5 m/s at the\n  table with a perfect tuck. → **take-off:** press `action` in the last 4 m before the edge: last 1.0 m q = 1, 1–2.5 m\n  .7, 2.5–4 m .4; no press → **FELL OFF THE TABLE** (q .1, yikes hop). Adds `vz += 2.4·q` m/s. → **flight:** body\n  angle α (to the airflow) changed by ↑/↓ at 40°/s; gusts from `rng('skijump:gust')` push α; lift `aL = cL(α)·v²`\n  (⊥ velocity), drag `aD = cD(α)·v²`, with `cL(α) = cL0·max(.1, 1 − ((α − 12)/30)²)`, `cL0` .00095 *(T)*,\n  `cD(α) = .0006 + .00002·α` *(T)*. → **landing:** within 2.5 m above the slope the prompt \"✕ TELEMARK!\" appears;\n  press within 0.35 s before contact → telemark; later/none → two-footed; landing with |α| > 40° *(T)*, or beyond\n  HS + 10 m without a telemark → **CRASH** (tumble down the out-run: Pose tumble, skis fly as sprites, snow spray).\n- **Scoring:** distance points `60 + (d − 125)·1.8`; style: 5 judges, telemark 17.5–19.5, two-footed 15–17, crash 6–9\n  (minus wobble in flight), drop high/low, sum 3 (max 60). Event = 2 jumps. Hill record **148.0 m (INGRID\n  SNOWCASTLE, FRM)**, event WR **296.4**. Qualify 160 / 210 / 245 (2-jump total). Points `3.9·total`.\n- **CPU:** balance and take-off q by skill, flight α error (1 − skill)·15°, telemark chance = skill.\n- **Turbo:** ROCKET SKIS: lift ×1.1 and +3 m/s² thrust for 2 s, flames from the ski tails.\n- **Tunables:** kAir, takeoffBoost, cL0, cDBase, gust, telemarkWindow, crashAngle.\n- **Yikes:** FELL OFF THE TABLE, CRASH. **Laurel:** OFF THE CHART (land > 150 m without crashing).\n- **HUD:** speed (km/h) in the in-run, take-off zone bar, the flight angle gauge (a skier silhouette rotating over a\n  green band), distance counter following the jumper, telemark prompt, judges' style cards.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 132–140 m; perfect + turbo ≥ 150 m; skill .5 ≈ 112–122 m; no take-off press → < 80 m.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate jumps; **hub:** yes (1 jump).\n\n### 6.8 DOWNHILL — winter · \"The Yikes Face\" · steering + tuck + gates\n\n- **View:** pseudo-3D `E.Road` (`segment: 200`, 1 m = 100 road units; `width: 1600`, `lanes: 0`, `draw: 220`), the","numLines":120,"startLine":729,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FGe9zET8VHfgjE1gDkwAed","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
