{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S3TKZ1c1LsmC5cRzdLt5dM","type":"tool_result","content":"846\t### 6.8 DOWNHILL — winter · \"The Yikes Face\" · steering + tuck + gates\n847\t\n848\t- **View:** pseudo-3D `E.Road` (`segment: 200`, 1 m = 100 road units; `width: 1600`, `lanes: 0`, `draw: 220`), the\n849\t  skier drawn from behind at the bottom center through a custom rear view (§8.2: `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18,\n850\t  1.6, 1)`, rig facing +y, skis and poles projected with the view's `ax ay bx by bz`), snow colors (road\n851\t  `#f4f8ff/#e8f0fb`, grass `#dfe9f6/#d3e0f0` deep snow, rumble = orange netting `#ff7a2a/#f05a1a`), pines,\n852\t  spectators with flags and cowbells, banners, start hut, ice tunnel (`tunnel: true`, blue-white walls), sun glare\n853\t  (an additive flare overlay), light snow.\n854\t- **Course (≈1,440 m, 24 gates):**\n855\t\n856\t| # | Section | Length | Slope | Curves | Gates | Feature |\n857\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n858\t| 1 | Start Schuss | 150 m | 28° | 0 | 1 | start hut, crowd |\n859\t| 2 | The Corkscrew | 220 m | 22° | +4, −4, +3 | 5 | S-bends |\n860\t| 3 | Kangaroo Kicker | 60 m | 10° → 32° | 0 | 1 | crest jump |\n861\t| 4 | Pine Alley | 200 m | 20° | −2 | 3 | fences at \\|x\\| 1.05 (narrow) |\n862\t| 5 | Ice Tunnel | 120 m | 18° | +2 | 1 | tunnel, grip ×0.6 |\n863\t| 6 | The Yikes Face | 180 m | 38° | 0 | 3 | big crest jump at its top |\n864\t| 7 | Glory Bend | 260 m | 18° | +5 (long) | 4 | strong outward push |\n865\t| 8 | Finish Schuss | 250 m | 15° | ±1 | 6 | Victory Hop jump, finish arch, grandstand |\n866\t\n867\t  Build: for each section `road.add(len/2, { curve, hill: -len·tan(slope)·100 })` (in road units) and keep a parallel\n868\t  meter-based table for physics (slope per segment, features, gate list `{ s, xc }`).\n869\t- **Physics:** speed `v` along the course: `a = g·sin(slope) − (tuck ? dTuck : dUp)·v² − μ·g − carve·|steer|·v`\n870\t  (dTuck .0028, dUp .0062, μ .03, carve .18 — all *(T)*). Lateral `x` (half-roads, piste |x| ≤ 1): `x' = steer·turn(v) −\n871\t  push·curveAt(z)·v²·k`; `turn` ×0.55 while tucking. 1 < |x| < 1.25 deep snow (drag ×3); |x| ≥ 1.25 → **CRASH into the\n872\t  netting** (yikes tumble 2.0 s, respawn |x| = 1, v = 10 m/s). **Jumps:** when the slope falls away faster than a\n873\t  ballistic arc, the skier is airborne (`h'' = −g`, shadow on the snow); `action` 0.2–0.5 s before a crest = PRE-JUMP\n874\t  (half the airtime: faster). Landing with |steer| > .6 or |x| > 1 → crash. **Gates:** passing |x − xc| ≤ .32 → +2%\n875\t  speed (whoosh) and hype +0.05; missing → +0.50 s penalty (red \"+0.50\").\n876\t- **Splits:** 3 checkpoints vs the current leader (green −, red +). The leader's run is a ghost skier.\n877\t- **Scoring:** lower time incl. penalties. Course record **47.62 s (ROCKY SUMMIT, MTP)**. Qualify 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0.\n878\t  Points `8.5·(80 − t)^1.4`.\n879\t- **CPU:** simulated runs with steering toward the next gate center, tuck on straights, noise and crash chance\n880\t  (1 − skill)·15% at the Yikes Face; the top CPU run becomes the ghost.\n881\t- **Turbo:** AVALANCHE: speed ×1.18 for 3 s with a cartoon avalanche cloud chasing behind.\n882\t- **Tunables:** dTuck, dUp, turnRate, curvePush, gateBoost, missPenalty, crashSteer.\n883\t- **Yikes:** CRASH (netting), CRASH (landing). **Laurel:** CLEAN SWEEP (all 24 gates).\n884\t- **HUD:** time, speed (km/h), split popups, gate counter (n/24), a course strip (progress line with the leader's\n885\t  dot), tuck indicator, hype flame.\n886\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 46.5–48.5 s; skill .5 ≈ 53–56 s; steering hard into the netting → crash; all gates\n887\t  possible.\n888\t- **Multiplayer:** humans take turns, each seeing the best run so far as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run; other\n889\t  players' skiers as ghosts drawn as road \"cars\").\n890\t\n891\t### 6.9 TWO-MAN BOBSLED — winter · Glory Ice Track (dusk) · push + load + banked steering\n892\t\n893\t- **View:** `E.Road` again (1 m = 100 units, `width` ≈ 400: a narrow channel; tune for the look), the track as an ice channel: road = ice (`#d8eef8/#cfe6f2`),\n894\t  rumble = blue-white walls, grass = snow banks, tunnel roofs on covered sections, dusk sky with floodlights placed as\n895\t  glowing scenery, timing boards. The sled (drawn with `px.poly` boxes through the rear view, in the nation's colors,\n896\t  number on the cowl) with two rigs seated (Pose `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`), tilted by its wall height.\n897\t- **Track (≈1,300 m, 15 named curves):** Sunny Start, Glory Kink, The Twins (2), Shark Fin, Kreisel (long +6),\n898\t  Labyrinth (3, S-S-S), Omega (+6/−6), The Washing Machine, Double Trouble (2), Last Gasp, Finish Curve.\n899\t- **Flow:** **push** (first 50 m): mash; `dv/dt = 6·power·(1 − v/11)` m/s² *(T)*; the start time at 50 m is shown\n900\t  (good ≈ 4.9 s) → **load:** press `action` between 40 and 50 m (the \"LOAD\" zone flashes): in the zone no loss; early\n901\t  ×0.95 speed; missed by 50 m → automatic load with −1.5 m/s and a **YIKES** (the brakeman flails, one leg out) →\n902\t  **drive:** `a = g·sin(slope) − drag·v² − μ·g − scrape`; lateral `x'' = force·curveAt(z)·v² − steer·steerForce −\n903\t  damp·x'`; the **groove** (ideal x for this curve and speed) shows as a glowing band on a U-shaped cross-section gauge;\n904\t  |x − groove| > .25 → skid (−2%/s, sparks); |x| > 1.55 → **FLIP** (yikes: the sled slides on its roof for 2 s in\n905\t  slow-mo, then rights itself at −35% speed) → finish and braking zone.\n906\t- **Format:** attempts × 2 runs, combined time. Track record **40.11 s per run (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify (2 runs)\n907\t  92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0. Points `6.4·(120 − total)^1.4`.\n908\t- **CPU:** simulated; push rate by skill; groove error by skill.\n909\t- **Turbo:** JET SLED: speed ×1.15 and auto-groove for 3 s, a jet flame from the tail.\n910\t- **Tunables:** pushGain, loadZone, drag, curveForce, steerForce, grooveTolerance, flipHeight.\n911\t- **Yikes:** LATE LOAD, FLIP. **Laurel:** ICE DANCER (a run with no skid or wall contact).\n912\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 39.8–40.6 s per run; skill .5 ≈ 42.5–44; not steering in Omega → flip.\n913\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate runs with the best run as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run).\n914\t\n915\t### 6.10 FIGURE SKATING (free skate) — winter · Glory Ice Palace · rhythm\n916\t\n917\t- **View:** `'threequarter'`; a 60×30 m rink (ice texture with scratches and reflections), boards with sponsor-free\n918\t  banners, spotlights (ambient .45 + moving spots), the kiss & cry booth (bench, flowers, a giant plush mascot) where\n919\t  scores are read, stands. The skater follows a closed `E.Path` (a large loop with a figure-8 crossing) at a pace tied\n920\t  to the music.\n921\t- **Music/chart:** original **\"Waltz of the Yikes\"** in 3/4 at 138 bpm, ~64 s (§9.1), played through `E.Rhythm`\n922\t  (`lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right', 'action']`, holds on `action` are jumps). Windows perfect 45 / great 90 /\n923\t  good 135 ms (×1.4 with Timing assist). Chart parts: Intro 4 bars · Step Sequence A 8 · Jump Combo 1 4 (two holds) ·\n924\t  Spiral & Spin 8 · **Coach's Corner** 8 (4 bars of calls `c` from the coach, then you answer: PaRappa-style) · Step\n925\t  Sequence B 8 (denser) · Jump Combo 2 4 (the 4-beat **QUAD YIKES** hold) · Finale 4 + the final-pose note. About 140\n926\t  notes. Easy uses every other non-hold note.\n927\t- **Highway:** a horizontal highway along the bottom third (notes travel right → left to a target line), 5 lanes\n928\t  labeled with glyph icons (← ↓ ↑ → and ✕/Space), big notes (10 px), judgement words over the skater.\n929\t- **Moves:** each judged note triggers a move on the rig: ←/→ edge steps and leans; ↑ spiral (one leg high behind,\n930\t  arms out); ↓ sit spin (`rig.spin` accelerating); a hold = jump: take-off on the hold's head, airborne rotations\n931\t  (`rig.spin` 4 turns/s, arms crossed), landing on release (great/perfect → clean landing with the free leg back; a\n932\t  miss → **FALL**: slide on the backside, get up, combo lost).\n933\t- **Scoring:** TES = Σ note value × (1 / .8 / .5 / 0) scaled so a perfect program = 128; PCS = 5 components (skating\n934\t  skills, transitions, performance, composition, interpretation) 0–10 each from accuracy, max combo, falls and finish\n935\t  pose, ×2 → max 100; falls −1 each. WR **228.56 (COCO BONBON, BON)**. Qualify 120 / 150 / 180. Points\n936\t  `min(1200, 5.3·total)`.\n937\t- **CPU:** simulated accuracy ~ skill ± noise → TES/PCS; the top 2 rivals' scores revealed in the kiss & cry.\n938\t- **Turbo:** STAR POWER: 4 s, every judgement one level better, rainbow trail and glitter; afterwards the crowd throws\n939\t  plush mascots onto the ice.\n940\t- **Tunables:** perfectMs, greatMs, goodMs, lifeDrain, tesScale, pcsWeight.\n941\t- **Yikes:** FALL. **Laurel:** FULL COMBO (no misses).\n942\t- **Targets:** autoplay (`rh.hit` on every note) = full combo, ≈ 225–230; idle → life fails → program ends early with\n943\t  low score but still a result.\n944\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate programs; **hub:** no.\n945\t\n946\t### 6.11 CURLING (gold medal match) — winter · Glory Curling Club · aim + weight + sweep (physics)\n947\t\n948\t- **View:** `'topdown'`; an arcade sheet (meters): hack y = 0, near hog line 6, far hog line 22, tee (house center) 27,\n949\t  back line 28.8, width 4.75 (x ±2.375), house radius 1.83 with rings (blue/white/red), stones r = 0.30 (arcade-sized,\n950\t  granite with handles in the two nations' colors). M = 12; camera zoom 1.2 during the delivery, follows the stone,\n951\t  2.5 over the house; a house-cam inset (top-right) always shows the house. Warm club lights, a scoreboard with ends.\n952\t- **Match:** you vs one CPU nation (Mountopia unless you are Mountopia; then the best other curler), 2 ends × 4 stones\n953\t  per team, alternating; hammer to the team that did not score (end 1 by coin flip from `rng('curling:hammer')`).\n954\t- **Delivery:** (1) **AIM**: stick ←/→ (or the pointer) moves the skip's broom target across the house; (2) **CURL**:\n955\t  `mashL` in-turn, `mashR` out-turn (an arrow on the stone; the first ~30% of the predicted path shows as dots);\n956\t  (3) **WEIGHT**: `action` starts the slide; a weight meter oscillates 0 → 1 → 0 at 1.1 Hz *(T)* with bands GUARD\n957\t  .25–.45, DRAW .45–.65, TAKEOUT .65–1.0; `action` again releases at that weight (`v0 = 1.8 + 2.0·w` m/s); releasing at\n958\t  w ≥ .98 = over-throw slip (yikes, still delivered); (4) **SWEEP**: mash while the stone travels: sweep =\n959\t  rate/8 Hz (clamped) cuts friction `μ = .019·(1 − .35·sweep)` and curl ×(1 − .5·sweep).\n960\t- **Physics:** `E.Physics` with gravity 0 for collisions (`world.circle(..., { bounce: .85, friction: .1, bullet: true })`);\n961\t  each step the game applies the ice: deceleration `μ·g` along the velocity and curl `a = spin·κ/(v + .5)`\n962\t  (κ .05 *(T)*) across it. Stones that touch the side boards or pass the back line are removed; a stone that stops\n963\t  before the far hog line is removed. Collisions above 2 m/s make sparks and a CLACK.\n964\t- **Scoring per end:** the team with the stone nearest the button scores 1 per stone nearer than the opponent's\n965\t  nearest (stones touching the house only). Ties after 2 ends → an extra end.\n966\t- **CPU:** for its throw it evaluates 9 aims × 6 weights × 2 spins = 108 candidates, **each simulated in a sandbox\n967\t  physics world** (12 per frame, so no hitch), scores the outcome (own shot stone in the house +, opponent shot\n968\t  stones −, guards protecting own stones +), picks the best, then adds execution noise (aim ±.15 m, weight ±.06,\n969\t  × (1 − skill)) and sweeps by its own plan.\n970\t- **Turbo:** HYPER SWEEP: 3 s of maximum sweep regardless of mashing, glowing brooms and ice sparkles.\n971\t- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver, bronze from a simulated match between the next two nations.\n972\t- **Tunables:** mu, sweepCut, curlK, weightHz, v0Base, v0Range, cpuNoise.\n973\t- **Yikes:** OVER-THROW SLIP; a stone you throw that knocks your own shot stone out → \"OWN GOAL!\". **Laurel:** DOUBLE\n974\t  TAKEOUT (two opponent stones removed by one throw).\n975\t- **Targets:** a draw-weight throw with no sweep stops in the house (±1.5 m of the button); takeout weight on a stone\n976\t  removes it; a .9-skill CPU beats a .3-skill CPU in ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; no frame spends > 8 ms on CPU sims.\n977\t- **Multiplayer:** versus (P1 and P2 skip opposing teams) or co-op (P1 throws, P2 sweeps); **hub:** no.\n978\t\n979\t### 6.12 ICE HOCKEY FINAL (2-on-2 + goalies) — winter · Glory Arena · team action\n980\t\n981\t- **Start from `kits/sports.js`** (its cage, ball-as-Body, passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` lobs, shot meter with\n982\t  aftertouch curl, formation AI, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`) and turn it into hockey: the pitch becomes a rink\n983\t  (ice floor texture, red center line, blue lines, faceoff circles, creases), the boards get glass on top (`h` higher,\n984\t  translucent top band), nets 3 tiles wide with posts; the ball becomes a **puck** (flat sprite, `bounce` 0 on the\n985\t  ice, board restitution .65, low friction); players skate with momentum (accel 220 u/s², max 105 u/s, glide);\n986\t  add an **automatic goalie** per side (a Body on an arc in its crease that moves toward the puck–goal line at a\n987\t  skill-limited speed and saves on contact, sometimes freezing the puck for a faceoff). Arena: dark with spotlights,\n988\t  a center-hung jumbotron, goal lights and horn, organ music.\n989\t- **Match:** your nation vs the rival (Turbonia), 2 periods × 90 s of running clock *(T)*, a resurfacing machine\n990\t  crossing at intermission, sudden-death overtime 90 s, then a **shootout** (3 rounds then sudden death: a skater\n991\t  starts at center with the puck, 6 s to shoot, vs the goalie).\n992\t- **Controls:** skate (stick), `mashL` pass (to the teammate the stick points at, led), `action` hold = shot meter,\n993\t  release = shoot (stick aims; push sideways just after = curl), `mashR` = **check** without the puck (a shoulder\n994\t  lunge: a hit knocks the opponent down 1 s, the puck squirts loose; into the boards → the glass shakes, crowd \"OOOH\")\n995\t  or switch to the teammate nearer the puck when far, `alt` = skate burst (stamina bar), `turbo` = **ON FIRE** (when\n996\t  the hype is full, or automatically after 3 straight good plays: the puck burns, shots ×1.4 speed, goalies react 50%\n997\t  slower, until a goal or 8 s). Mouse: left hold/release shoots toward the cursor, right passes toward it.\n998\t- **Hype:** completed passes, hits, shots on goal, saves avoided.\n999\t- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver; bronze simulated.\n1000\t- **Tunables:** periodLength, skateAccel, skateMax, shotPower, puckFriction, goalieSpeed, checkPower.\n1001\t- **Yikes:** CHECKED INTO THE GLASS (when you get hit), OWN GOAL. **Laurel:** HAT TRICK (one skater scores 3).\n1002\t- **Targets:** bot vs bot (skill .9 vs .3) wins ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; goals happen (≥ 1 per period on average\n1003\t  at equal skill .7); a shot on an empty net scores; checks knock down.\n1004\t- **Multiplayer:** up to 4: 2v2 versus or co-op vs the CPU; **hub:** no.\n1005\t\n1006\t---\n1007\t\n1008\t## 7. Content\n1009\t\n1010\t**Originality rules:** fictional nations, athletes, venues and mascot; no Olympic rings or official emblems, no real"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"145b1e55-c7e7-4edd-9180-c567f5ac737f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:27.891Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 6.8 DOWNHILL — winter · \"The Yikes Face\" · steering + tuck + gates\n\n- **View:** pseudo-3D `E.Road` (`segment: 200`, 1 m = 100 road units; `width: 1600`, `lanes: 0`, `draw: 220`), the\n  skier drawn from behind at the bottom center through a custom rear view (§8.2: `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18,\n  1.6, 1)`, rig facing +y, skis and poles projected with the view's `ax ay bx by bz`), snow colors (road\n  `#f4f8ff/#e8f0fb`, grass `#dfe9f6/#d3e0f0` deep snow, rumble = orange netting `#ff7a2a/#f05a1a`), pines,\n  spectators with flags and cowbells, banners, start hut, ice tunnel (`tunnel: true`, blue-white walls), sun glare\n  (an additive flare overlay), light snow.\n- **Course (≈1,440 m, 24 gates):**\n\n| # | Section | Length | Slope | Curves | Gates | Feature |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Start Schuss | 150 m | 28° | 0 | 1 | start hut, crowd |\n| 2 | The Corkscrew | 220 m | 22° | +4, −4, +3 | 5 | S-bends |\n| 3 | Kangaroo Kicker | 60 m | 10° → 32° | 0 | 1 | crest jump |\n| 4 | Pine Alley | 200 m | 20° | −2 | 3 | fences at \\|x\\| 1.05 (narrow) |\n| 5 | Ice Tunnel | 120 m | 18° | +2 | 1 | tunnel, grip ×0.6 |\n| 6 | The Yikes Face | 180 m | 38° | 0 | 3 | big crest jump at its top |\n| 7 | Glory Bend | 260 m | 18° | +5 (long) | 4 | strong outward push |\n| 8 | Finish Schuss | 250 m | 15° | ±1 | 6 | Victory Hop jump, finish arch, grandstand |\n\n  Build: for each section `road.add(len/2, { curve, hill: -len·tan(slope)·100 })` (in road units) and keep a parallel\n  meter-based table for physics (slope per segment, features, gate list `{ s, xc }`).\n- **Physics:** speed `v` along the course: `a = g·sin(slope) − (tuck ? dTuck : dUp)·v² − μ·g − carve·|steer|·v`\n  (dTuck .0028, dUp .0062, μ .03, carve .18 — all *(T)*). Lateral `x` (half-roads, piste |x| ≤ 1): `x' = steer·turn(v) −\n  push·curveAt(z)·v²·k`; `turn` ×0.55 while tucking. 1 < |x| < 1.25 deep snow (drag ×3); |x| ≥ 1.25 → **CRASH into the\n  netting** (yikes tumble 2.0 s, respawn |x| = 1, v = 10 m/s). **Jumps:** when the slope falls away faster than a\n  ballistic arc, the skier is airborne (`h'' = −g`, shadow on the snow); `action` 0.2–0.5 s before a crest = PRE-JUMP\n  (half the airtime: faster). Landing with |steer| > .6 or |x| > 1 → crash. **Gates:** passing |x − xc| ≤ .32 → +2%\n  speed (whoosh) and hype +0.05; missing → +0.50 s penalty (red \"+0.50\").\n- **Splits:** 3 checkpoints vs the current leader (green −, red +). The leader's run is a ghost skier.\n- **Scoring:** lower time incl. penalties. Course record **47.62 s (ROCKY SUMMIT, MTP)**. Qualify 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0.\n  Points `8.5·(80 − t)^1.4`.\n- **CPU:** simulated runs with steering toward the next gate center, tuck on straights, noise and crash chance\n  (1 − skill)·15% at the Yikes Face; the top CPU run becomes the ghost.\n- **Turbo:** AVALANCHE: speed ×1.18 for 3 s with a cartoon avalanche cloud chasing behind.\n- **Tunables:** dTuck, dUp, turnRate, curvePush, gateBoost, missPenalty, crashSteer.\n- **Yikes:** CRASH (netting), CRASH (landing). **Laurel:** CLEAN SWEEP (all 24 gates).\n- **HUD:** time, speed (km/h), split popups, gate counter (n/24), a course strip (progress line with the leader's\n  dot), tuck indicator, hype flame.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 46.5–48.5 s; skill .5 ≈ 53–56 s; steering hard into the netting → crash; all gates\n  possible.\n- **Multiplayer:** humans take turns, each seeing the best run so far as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run; other\n  players' skiers as ghosts drawn as road \"cars\").\n\n### 6.9 TWO-MAN BOBSLED — winter · Glory Ice Track (dusk) · push + load + banked steering\n\n- **View:** `E.Road` again (1 m = 100 units, `width` ≈ 400: a narrow channel; tune for the look), the track as an ice channel: road = ice (`#d8eef8/#cfe6f2`),\n  rumble = blue-white walls, grass = snow banks, tunnel roofs on covered sections, dusk sky with floodlights placed as\n  glowing scenery, timing boards. The sled (drawn with `px.poly` boxes through the rear view, in the nation's colors,\n  number on the cowl) with two rigs seated (Pose `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`), tilted by its wall height.\n- **Track (≈1,300 m, 15 named curves):** Sunny Start, Glory Kink, The Twins (2), Shark Fin, Kreisel (long +6),\n  Labyrinth (3, S-S-S), Omega (+6/−6), The Washing Machine, Double Trouble (2), Last Gasp, Finish Curve.\n- **Flow:** **push** (first 50 m): mash; `dv/dt = 6·power·(1 − v/11)` m/s² *(T)*; the start time at 50 m is shown\n  (good ≈ 4.9 s) → **load:** press `action` between 40 and 50 m (the \"LOAD\" zone flashes): in the zone no loss; early\n  ×0.95 speed; missed by 50 m → automatic load with −1.5 m/s and a **YIKES** (the brakeman flails, one leg out) →\n  **drive:** `a = g·sin(slope) − drag·v² − μ·g − scrape`; lateral `x'' = force·curveAt(z)·v² − steer·steerForce −\n  damp·x'`; the **groove** (ideal x for this curve and speed) shows as a glowing band on a U-shaped cross-section gauge;\n  |x − groove| > .25 → skid (−2%/s, sparks); |x| > 1.55 → **FLIP** (yikes: the sled slides on its roof for 2 s in\n  slow-mo, then rights itself at −35% speed) → finish and braking zone.\n- **Format:** attempts × 2 runs, combined time. Track record **40.11 s per run (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify (2 runs)\n  92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0. Points `6.4·(120 − total)^1.4`.\n- **CPU:** simulated; push rate by skill; groove error by skill.\n- **Turbo:** JET SLED: speed ×1.15 and auto-groove for 3 s, a jet flame from the tail.\n- **Tunables:** pushGain, loadZone, drag, curveForce, steerForce, grooveTolerance, flipHeight.\n- **Yikes:** LATE LOAD, FLIP. **Laurel:** ICE DANCER (a run with no skid or wall contact).\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 39.8–40.6 s per run; skill .5 ≈ 42.5–44; not steering in Omega → flip.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate runs with the best run as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run).\n\n### 6.10 FIGURE SKATING (free skate) — winter · Glory Ice Palace · rhythm\n\n- **View:** `'threequarter'`; a 60×30 m rink (ice texture with scratches and reflections), boards with sponsor-free\n  banners, spotlights (ambient .45 + moving spots), the kiss & cry booth (bench, flowers, a giant plush mascot) where\n  scores are read, stands. The skater follows a closed `E.Path` (a large loop with a figure-8 crossing) at a pace tied\n  to the music.\n- **Music/chart:** original **\"Waltz of the Yikes\"** in 3/4 at 138 bpm, ~64 s (§9.1), played through `E.Rhythm`\n  (`lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right', 'action']`, holds on `action` are jumps). Windows perfect 45 / great 90 /\n  good 135 ms (×1.4 with Timing assist). Chart parts: Intro 4 bars · Step Sequence A 8 · Jump Combo 1 4 (two holds) ·\n  Spiral & Spin 8 · **Coach's Corner** 8 (4 bars of calls `c` from the coach, then you answer: PaRappa-style) · Step\n  Sequence B 8 (denser) · Jump Combo 2 4 (the 4-beat **QUAD YIKES** hold) · Finale 4 + the final-pose note. About 140\n  notes. Easy uses every other non-hold note.\n- **Highway:** a horizontal highway along the bottom third (notes travel right → left to a target line), 5 lanes\n  labeled with glyph icons (← ↓ ↑ → and ✕/Space), big notes (10 px), judgement words over the skater.\n- **Moves:** each judged note triggers a move on the rig: ←/→ edge steps and leans; ↑ spiral (one leg high behind,\n  arms out); ↓ sit spin (`rig.spin` accelerating); a hold = jump: take-off on the hold's head, airborne rotations\n  (`rig.spin` 4 turns/s, arms crossed), landing on release (great/perfect → clean landing with the free leg back; a\n  miss → **FALL**: slide on the backside, get up, combo lost).\n- **Scoring:** TES = Σ note value × (1 / .8 / .5 / 0) scaled so a perfect program = 128; PCS = 5 components (skating\n  skills, transitions, performance, composition, interpretation) 0–10 each from accuracy, max combo, falls and finish\n  pose, ×2 → max 100; falls −1 each. WR **228.56 (COCO BONBON, BON)**. Qualify 120 / 150 / 180. Points\n  `min(1200, 5.3·total)`.\n- **CPU:** simulated accuracy ~ skill ± noise → TES/PCS; the top 2 rivals' scores revealed in the kiss & cry.\n- **Turbo:** STAR POWER: 4 s, every judgement one level better, rainbow trail and glitter; afterwards the crowd throws\n  plush mascots onto the ice.\n- **Tunables:** perfectMs, greatMs, goodMs, lifeDrain, tesScale, pcsWeight.\n- **Yikes:** FALL. **Laurel:** FULL COMBO (no misses).\n- **Targets:** autoplay (`rh.hit` on every note) = full combo, ≈ 225–230; idle → life fails → program ends early with\n  low score but still a result.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate programs; **hub:** no.\n\n### 6.11 CURLING (gold medal match) — winter · Glory Curling Club · aim + weight + sweep (physics)\n\n- **View:** `'topdown'`; an arcade sheet (meters): hack y = 0, near hog line 6, far hog line 22, tee (house center) 27,\n  back line 28.8, width 4.75 (x ±2.375), house radius 1.83 with rings (blue/white/red), stones r = 0.30 (arcade-sized,\n  granite with handles in the two nations' colors). M = 12; camera zoom 1.2 during the delivery, follows the stone,\n  2.5 over the house; a house-cam inset (top-right) always shows the house. Warm club lights, a scoreboard with ends.\n- **Match:** you vs one CPU nation (Mountopia unless you are Mountopia; then the best other curler), 2 ends × 4 stones\n  per team, alternating; hammer to the team that did not score (end 1 by coin flip from `rng('curling:hammer')`).\n- **Delivery:** (1) **AIM**: stick ←/→ (or the pointer) moves the skip's broom target across the house; (2) **CURL**:\n  `mashL` in-turn, `mashR` out-turn (an arrow on the stone; the first ~30% of the predicted path shows as dots);\n  (3) **WEIGHT**: `action` starts the slide; a weight meter oscillates 0 → 1 → 0 at 1.1 Hz *(T)* with bands GUARD\n  .25–.45, DRAW .45–.65, TAKEOUT .65–1.0; `action` again releases at that weight (`v0 = 1.8 + 2.0·w` m/s); releasing at\n  w ≥ .98 = over-throw slip (yikes, still delivered); (4) **SWEEP**: mash while the stone travels: sweep =\n  rate/8 Hz (clamped) cuts friction `μ = .019·(1 − .35·sweep)` and curl ×(1 − .5·sweep).\n- **Physics:** `E.Physics` with gravity 0 for collisions (`world.circle(..., { bounce: .85, friction: .1, bullet: true })`);\n  each step the game applies the ice: deceleration `μ·g` along the velocity and curl `a = spin·κ/(v + .5)`\n  (κ .05 *(T)*) across it. Stones that touch the side boards or pass the back line are removed; a stone that stops\n  before the far hog line is removed. Collisions above 2 m/s make sparks and a CLACK.\n- **Scoring per end:** the team with the stone nearest the button scores 1 per stone nearer than the opponent's\n  nearest (stones touching the house only). Ties after 2 ends → an extra end.\n- **CPU:** for its throw it evaluates 9 aims × 6 weights × 2 spins = 108 candidates, **each simulated in a sandbox\n  physics world** (12 per frame, so no hitch), scores the outcome (own shot stone in the house +, opponent shot\n  stones −, guards protecting own stones +), picks the best, then adds execution noise (aim ±.15 m, weight ±.06,\n  × (1 − skill)) and sweeps by its own plan.\n- **Turbo:** HYPER SWEEP: 3 s of maximum sweep regardless of mashing, glowing brooms and ice sparkles.\n- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver, bronze from a simulated match between the next two nations.\n- **Tunables:** mu, sweepCut, curlK, weightHz, v0Base, v0Range, cpuNoise.\n- **Yikes:** OVER-THROW SLIP; a stone you throw that knocks your own shot stone out → \"OWN GOAL!\". **Laurel:** DOUBLE\n  TAKEOUT (two opponent stones removed by one throw).\n- **Targets:** a draw-weight throw with no sweep stops in the house (±1.5 m of the button); takeout weight on a stone\n  removes it; a .9-skill CPU beats a .3-skill CPU in ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; no frame spends > 8 ms on CPU sims.\n- **Multiplayer:** versus (P1 and P2 skip opposing teams) or co-op (P1 throws, P2 sweeps); **hub:** no.\n\n### 6.12 ICE HOCKEY FINAL (2-on-2 + goalies) — winter · Glory Arena · team action\n\n- **Start from `kits/sports.js`** (its cage, ball-as-Body, passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` lobs, shot meter with\n  aftertouch curl, formation AI, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`) and turn it into hockey: the pitch becomes a rink\n  (ice floor texture, red center line, blue lines, faceoff circles, creases), the boards get glass on top (`h` higher,\n  translucent top band), nets 3 tiles wide with posts; the ball becomes a **puck** (flat sprite, `bounce` 0 on the\n  ice, board restitution .65, low friction); players skate with momentum (accel 220 u/s², max 105 u/s, glide);\n  add an **automatic goalie** per side (a Body on an arc in its crease that moves toward the puck–goal line at a\n  skill-limited speed and saves on contact, sometimes freezing the puck for a faceoff). Arena: dark with spotlights,\n  a center-hung jumbotron, goal lights and horn, organ music.\n- **Match:** your nation vs the rival (Turbonia), 2 periods × 90 s of running clock *(T)*, a resurfacing machine\n  crossing at intermission, sudden-death overtime 90 s, then a **shootout** (3 rounds then sudden death: a skater\n  starts at center with the puck, 6 s to shoot, vs the goalie).\n- **Controls:** skate (stick), `mashL` pass (to the teammate the stick points at, led), `action` hold = shot meter,\n  release = shoot (stick aims; push sideways just after = curl), `mashR` = **check** without the puck (a shoulder\n  lunge: a hit knocks the opponent down 1 s, the puck squirts loose; into the boards → the glass shakes, crowd \"OOOH\")\n  or switch to the teammate nearer the puck when far, `alt` = skate burst (stamina bar), `turbo` = **ON FIRE** (when\n  the hype is full, or automatically after 3 straight good plays: the puck burns, shots ×1.4 speed, goalies react 50%\n  slower, until a goal or 8 s). Mouse: left hold/release shoots toward the cursor, right passes toward it.\n- **Hype:** completed passes, hits, shots on goal, saves avoided.\n- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver; bronze simulated.\n- **Tunables:** periodLength, skateAccel, skateMax, shotPower, puckFriction, goalieSpeed, checkPower.\n- **Yikes:** CHECKED INTO THE GLASS (when you get hit), OWN GOAL. **Laurel:** HAT TRICK (one skater scores 3).\n- **Targets:** bot vs bot (skill .9 vs .3) wins ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; goals happen (≥ 1 per period on average\n  at equal skill .7); a shot on an empty net scores; checks knock down.\n- **Multiplayer:** up to 4: 2v2 versus or co-op vs the CPU; **hub:** no.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Content\n\n**Originality rules:** fictional nations, athletes, venues and mascot; no Olympic rings or official emblems, no real","numLines":165,"startLine":846,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S3TKZ1c1LsmC5cRzdLt5dM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
