{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R26faCXWaP1fUPyyQTBfYL","type":"tool_result","content":"1008\t## 7. Content\n1009\t\n1010\t**Originality rules:** fictional nations, athletes, venues and mascot; no Olympic rings or official emblems, no real\n1011\tanthems, fanfares or broadcast themes; in-game text says \"the Games\". The hub `source` meta may say \"The Olympic\n1012\tGames\" (it is descriptive).\n1013\t\n1014\t### 7.1 Nations and their star athletes (8 = 8 lanes)\n1015\t\n1016\t| Code | Nation | Colors (a / b / c) | Flag (drawn in code) | Athlete | Rig (`new E.Humanoid`) | Voice | Personality |\n1017\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1018\t| SUN | SUNVALE | `#f2b632` gold / `#2f7fe0` sky / `#ffffff` | sky field, gold sun disc with 8 rays | **DASH GOLDBERRY** | heroic, hair short `#3a2414`, skin `#8d5a3b` | pitch 1.0, speed 1.1 | sunny optimist |\n1019\t| FRM | FROSTMARK | `#f4f8ff` snow / `#2fa8d8` glacier / `#1a3a6a` navy | white field, glacier snowflake, navy border | **INGRID SNOWCASTLE** | heroic, ponytail `#f3e6c0`, skin `#f2d4c4` | 1.3, 0.9 | deadpan |\n1020\t| TRB | TURBONIA | `#e23b2e` red / `#1e2026` carbon / `#ffd23a` yellow | diagonal red/carbon split, yellow lightning bolt | **MAX OVERDRIVE** (the rival) | heroic, spiky `#141414`, skin `#c88a5e`, red headband (`hat: band`) | 0.9, 1.25 | arrogant, loud |\n1021\t| BON | BONBONIA | `#ff7fb8` pink / `#6fe0c0` mint / `#ffffff` | vertical candy stripes, small heart | **COCO BONBON** | heroic, long `#ff9ad0`, skin `#f5c9a8`, `face: { eyes: 'big' }` | 1.45, 1.05 | theatrical |\n1022\t| VOL | VOLCANICA | `#ff6a1a` lava / `#3a2e2e` basalt / `#ffd0a0` ember | basalt field, orange volcano, yellow eruption dot | **BLAZE CINDERHART** | **bulky**, bald, skin `#6a4028` | 0.7, 0.85 | gentle giant |\n1023\t| WAV | WAVELIA | `#1fa8a0` teal / `#0e4a6a` deep / `#e8fbf7` foam | teal field, three white waves | **MARINA SPLASHWORTH** | heroic, short `#24160e`, skin `#5a3420` | 1.25, 0.95 | calm poet |\n1024\t| MTP | MOUNTOPIA | `#6a3fc8` purple / `#c8ccd8` silver / `#ffffff` | purple field, white peak, 3 silver stars | **ROCKY SUMMIT** | heroic, short `#8a5a2a`, skin `#e0b090`, beanie (`hat: cap`) | 0.95, 1.0 | folksy |\n1025\t| NEO | NEON REPUBLIC | `#e83ae0` magenta / `#14102a` night / `#3ae8f0` cyan | night field, cyan ring, magenta star | **PIXEL VANCE** | heroic, spiky `#3ae8f0`, skin `#f0c8a8` | 1.15, 1.2 | gamer slang |\n1026\t\n1027\tOutfits come from `O.makeRig(nation, sport)`: singlet + shorts (track, weights: belt), swim cap + goggles (pool),\n1028\tracing suit + helmet + goggles (downhill, bobsled, ski jump bib with number), sparkly costume (figure skating: the\n1029\tnation's colors + `trim` sequins), sweater (curling), padded jersey + helmet (hockey), team tracksuit (ceremonies).\n1030\tEvery rig size 1.25 (bulky Blaze 1.3), with the nation's 4–6 colors (never engine defaults).\n1031\t\n1032\t**CPU skill per event** (0–1; effective skill per §5.6):\n1033\t\n1034\t| | 100m | Jav | Swim | Dive | Arch | Wts | SkiJ | Down | Bob | Fig | Curl | Hock |\n1035\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1036\t| SUN | .92 | .85 | .70 | .62 | .66 | .70 | .60 | .65 | .78 | .60 | .62 | .74 |\n1037\t| FRM | .70 | .74 | .66 | .68 | .80 | .66 | .94 | .92 | .74 | .76 | .80 | .78 |\n1038\t| TRB | .93 | .90 | .78 | .70 | .72 | .82 | .80 | .84 | .95 | .62 | .66 | .93 |\n1039\t| BON | .66 | .62 | .80 | .92 | .74 | .58 | .70 | .68 | .62 | .95 | .70 | .64 |\n1040\t| VOL | .72 | .88 | .62 | .55 | .64 | .95 | .62 | .70 | .86 | .52 | .82 | .88 |\n1041\t| WAV | .74 | .68 | .95 | .88 | .70 | .64 | .66 | .62 | .64 | .80 | .72 | .66 |\n1042\t| MTP | .68 | .72 | .64 | .60 | .86 | .74 | .82 | .88 | .80 | .66 | .93 | .80 |\n1043\t| NEO | .78 | .70 | .72 | .74 | .93 | .60 | .74 | .76 | .70 | .82 | .76 | .84 |\n1044\t\n1045\t**Teammates** (bobsled brakeman, hockey partner and goalie, curling team), generated rigs in team colors:\n1046\tSUN Sunny Ray, Bo Marigold, Lux Daybright · FRM Sven Driftholm, Liv Hailstrom, Nils Frostby · TRB Rev Throttleton,\n1047\tNitro Vex, Gigi Torque · BON Taffy Swirl, Praline Dupree, Nougat Fizz · VOL Ash Kindleton, Ember Stone, Obsidia Crag ·\n1048\tWAV Coral Finley, Tide Brennan, Kai Seaborne · MTP Edelweiss Vogt, Cliff Hangar, Scree Halvorsen · NEO Byte Ortega,\n1049\tGlitch Kowalski, Vector Nakamura.\n1050\t\n1051\t**\"Up Close & Personal\" bios** (one per day card, rotating; the player's own athlete gets one on Day 1):\n1052\t- **Dash Goldberry (SUN):** \"Dash grew up on a farm in rural Sunvale, chasing the family's prize ostrich to school\n1053\t  every morning. The ostrich never once let him win. Today, he runs for Daisy.\"\n1054\t- **Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM):** \"Ingrid's grandmother taught her to ski jump off the roof of the family sauna. The sauna\n1055\t  has since been rebuilt. Twice.\"\n1056\t- **Max Overdrive (TRB):** \"Defending champion in, quote, 'everything'. Max has never lost a race, a staring contest,\n1057\t  or an argument with a mirror. His hobbies include winning and describing winning.\"\n1058\t- **Coco Bonbon (BON):** \"Coco skates every program to the songs her grandfather whistled. She says she can still hear\n1059\t  him in the crowd. Usually slightly off-key.\"\n1060\t- **Blaze Cinderhart (VOL):** \"Every winter morning, Blaze lifts the family car out of a volcanic ash drift. The car is\n1061\t  fine. The car is extremely well-defined.\"\n1062\t- **Marina Splashworth (WAV):** \"Born on a houseboat, Marina didn't touch dry land until she was four. On land she still\n1063\t  walks like the deck is moving. In the water... poetry.\"\n1064\t- **Rocky Summit (MTP):** \"Rocky's village sits so high that the mail arrives by curling stone. He has been sweeping since\n1065\t  before he could walk. His first word was 'HARD!'\"\n1066\t- **Pixel Vance (NEO):** \"Pixel learned archery from an arcade cabinet and has never seen daylight without sunglasses.\n1067\t  Pixel's coach is a toaster named Gary. Gary believes in Pixel.\"\n1068\t\n1069\t### 7.2 Venues (levels)\n1070\t\n1071\t| Venue | Events / scenes | View | Light | Key art (all drawn in code; generic props from the engine library/asset store) |\n1072\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1073\t| **Glory Stadium** (Sunny Bay) | 100m, Javelin; opening & closing ceremonies; stadium podiums | brawler | day (events), night + fireworks (ceremonies) | red 8-lane track with lane numbers, infield grass with mown stripes, 3-tier stands + crowd, the cauldron tower, jumbotron, finish gantry & clock, flags of the 8 nations on the rim, the blimp, parking lot past the wall |\n1074\t| **Splash Palace** | 50m Free, Diving | brawler / side | indoor bright, caustics | pool, lane ropes, blocks, flags line, the dive tower, judges' table, windows onto the beach, jumbotron |\n1075\t| **Bullseye Lawn** | Archery | overlay + side inset | sunny, breezy | target faces, palms, the sea, wind flags, shade tent |\n1076\t| **Iron Hall** | Weightlifting | brawler | dark, two spotlights | platform, chalk bowl, referee lights, plate rack, dim crowd |\n1077\t| **Mount Glory Jumping Hill** | Ski Jump | side | night floodlights, light snow | tower, in-run, K/HS lines, distance boards, out-run crowd with cowbells and flags |\n1078\t| **The Yikes Face** | Downhill | E.Road | bright day, sun glare, light snow | piste, orange netting, pines, start hut, ice tunnel, jumps, finish arch, grandstand |\n1079\t| **Glory Ice Track** | Bobsled | E.Road | dusk, floodlights | ice channel, named curve signs, tunnels, timing boards |\n1080\t| **Glory Ice Palace** | Figure Skating | threequarter | spotlights | rink, kiss & cry, flowers, plush rain |\n1081\t| **Glory Curling Club** | Curling | topdown | warm indoor | sheet, houses, scoreboard, pennants |\n1082\t| **Glory Arena** | Ice Hockey | threequarter | dark arena + spots | rink, glass, center jumbotron cube, goal lights, organ loft |\n1083\t\n1084\tUse `node vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/tools/asset-find.mjs \"<thing>\"` for generic props (benches, fences, pines,\n1085\tsnow blocks, banners, lamps, flags: the `kenney-holiday`, `kenney-nature`, `ambientcg` sets have snow, pines, ice and\n1086\tfences); cut the few you use into a set of your own with `tools/asset-set.mjs` and inline it.\n1087\t\n1088\t### 7.3 Story structure (The Games)\n1089\t\n1090\t| When | Beat | Content |\n1091\t|---|---|---|\n1092\t| Start | **Opening ceremony** | §7.4 |\n1093\t| Day 1 (before) | Max's welcome | in the call room: \"Lane four? Cute. I'm in lane five. Lane five is where legends warm up.\" |\n1094\t| After Day 2 | **Mascot incident 1** | Yikesy \"test-jumps\" the ski jump: a 6 s cutscene (the Blob launched, spinning, lands in a snowbank head-first). Chip: \"The mascot has... the mascot has set a personal best!\" Vera: \"And a personal worst. Simultaneously.\" |\n1095\t| After Day 4 | Curling chat | Rocky: \"Back home we curl to settle arguments. Mostly about curling.\" |\n1096\t| After Day 6 | **HALFTIME REPORT** | medal table + banter; Yikesy appears, dripping (\"rescued from the pool filter\"); Max line depends on standings (§7.6) |\n1097\t| After Day 8 | Coco's moment | Coco (any result): \"Grandpa, that one was for you.\" Vera, quietly: \"...Give me a second, Chip.\" |\n1098\t| After Day 10 | Sled scandal | Vera: \"Turbonia's sled has a spoiler. And a cup holder.\" Max: \"It's called aerodynamic hospitality.\" |\n1099\t| Day 12 (before) | **THE FINAL** | both anthems tease; Max: \"Two nations. One puck. Zero chance. For you.\" |\n1100\t| After Day 12 | Sportsmanship | win: Max: \"...Good game. Next Games I'm bringing two helmets. One for my ego.\" · loss: Max: \"Good game. You were almost me.\" |\n1101\t| End | **Closing ceremony** | §7.4; ending by rank |\n1102\t| Dynamic | Rival reactions | after any event with you and Max both in the top 4: a line from the bank (beat him / he beat you) |\n1103\t| Dynamic | Records & yikes | a WR by you → Vera's sentimental line; 5+ yikes → Vera: \"Statistically, the most entertaining athlete in Games history.\" |\n1104\t\n1105\t### 7.4 Ceremony scripts\n1106\t\n1107\t**Opening ceremony** (Glory Stadium at night, ~60 s, hold ✕ 1 s to skip):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"f1f9d264-acde-4676-be0a-1f51473f5161","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:45.433Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 7. Content\n\n**Originality rules:** fictional nations, athletes, venues and mascot; no Olympic rings or official emblems, no real\nanthems, fanfares or broadcast themes; in-game text says \"the Games\". The hub `source` meta may say \"The Olympic\nGames\" (it is descriptive).\n\n### 7.1 Nations and their star athletes (8 = 8 lanes)\n\n| Code | Nation | Colors (a / b / c) | Flag (drawn in code) | Athlete | Rig (`new E.Humanoid`) | Voice | Personality |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SUN | SUNVALE | `#f2b632` gold / `#2f7fe0` sky / `#ffffff` | sky field, gold sun disc with 8 rays | **DASH GOLDBERRY** | heroic, hair short `#3a2414`, skin `#8d5a3b` | pitch 1.0, speed 1.1 | sunny optimist |\n| FRM | FROSTMARK | `#f4f8ff` snow / `#2fa8d8` glacier / `#1a3a6a` navy | white field, glacier snowflake, navy border | **INGRID SNOWCASTLE** | heroic, ponytail `#f3e6c0`, skin `#f2d4c4` | 1.3, 0.9 | deadpan |\n| TRB | TURBONIA | `#e23b2e` red / `#1e2026` carbon / `#ffd23a` yellow | diagonal red/carbon split, yellow lightning bolt | **MAX OVERDRIVE** (the rival) | heroic, spiky `#141414`, skin `#c88a5e`, red headband (`hat: band`) | 0.9, 1.25 | arrogant, loud |\n| BON | BONBONIA | `#ff7fb8` pink / `#6fe0c0` mint / `#ffffff` | vertical candy stripes, small heart | **COCO BONBON** | heroic, long `#ff9ad0`, skin `#f5c9a8`, `face: { eyes: 'big' }` | 1.45, 1.05 | theatrical |\n| VOL | VOLCANICA | `#ff6a1a` lava / `#3a2e2e` basalt / `#ffd0a0` ember | basalt field, orange volcano, yellow eruption dot | **BLAZE CINDERHART** | **bulky**, bald, skin `#6a4028` | 0.7, 0.85 | gentle giant |\n| WAV | WAVELIA | `#1fa8a0` teal / `#0e4a6a` deep / `#e8fbf7` foam | teal field, three white waves | **MARINA SPLASHWORTH** | heroic, short `#24160e`, skin `#5a3420` | 1.25, 0.95 | calm poet |\n| MTP | MOUNTOPIA | `#6a3fc8` purple / `#c8ccd8` silver / `#ffffff` | purple field, white peak, 3 silver stars | **ROCKY SUMMIT** | heroic, short `#8a5a2a`, skin `#e0b090`, beanie (`hat: cap`) | 0.95, 1.0 | folksy |\n| NEO | NEON REPUBLIC | `#e83ae0` magenta / `#14102a` night / `#3ae8f0` cyan | night field, cyan ring, magenta star | **PIXEL VANCE** | heroic, spiky `#3ae8f0`, skin `#f0c8a8` | 1.15, 1.2 | gamer slang |\n\nOutfits come from `O.makeRig(nation, sport)`: singlet + shorts (track, weights: belt), swim cap + goggles (pool),\nracing suit + helmet + goggles (downhill, bobsled, ski jump bib with number), sparkly costume (figure skating: the\nnation's colors + `trim` sequins), sweater (curling), padded jersey + helmet (hockey), team tracksuit (ceremonies).\nEvery rig size 1.25 (bulky Blaze 1.3), with the nation's 4–6 colors (never engine defaults).\n\n**CPU skill per event** (0–1; effective skill per §5.6):\n\n| | 100m | Jav | Swim | Dive | Arch | Wts | SkiJ | Down | Bob | Fig | Curl | Hock |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SUN | .92 | .85 | .70 | .62 | .66 | .70 | .60 | .65 | .78 | .60 | .62 | .74 |\n| FRM | .70 | .74 | .66 | .68 | .80 | .66 | .94 | .92 | .74 | .76 | .80 | .78 |\n| TRB | .93 | .90 | .78 | .70 | .72 | .82 | .80 | .84 | .95 | .62 | .66 | .93 |\n| BON | .66 | .62 | .80 | .92 | .74 | .58 | .70 | .68 | .62 | .95 | .70 | .64 |\n| VOL | .72 | .88 | .62 | .55 | .64 | .95 | .62 | .70 | .86 | .52 | .82 | .88 |\n| WAV | .74 | .68 | .95 | .88 | .70 | .64 | .66 | .62 | .64 | .80 | .72 | .66 |\n| MTP | .68 | .72 | .64 | .60 | .86 | .74 | .82 | .88 | .80 | .66 | .93 | .80 |\n| NEO | .78 | .70 | .72 | .74 | .93 | .60 | .74 | .76 | .70 | .82 | .76 | .84 |\n\n**Teammates** (bobsled brakeman, hockey partner and goalie, curling team), generated rigs in team colors:\nSUN Sunny Ray, Bo Marigold, Lux Daybright · FRM Sven Driftholm, Liv Hailstrom, Nils Frostby · TRB Rev Throttleton,\nNitro Vex, Gigi Torque · BON Taffy Swirl, Praline Dupree, Nougat Fizz · VOL Ash Kindleton, Ember Stone, Obsidia Crag ·\nWAV Coral Finley, Tide Brennan, Kai Seaborne · MTP Edelweiss Vogt, Cliff Hangar, Scree Halvorsen · NEO Byte Ortega,\nGlitch Kowalski, Vector Nakamura.\n\n**\"Up Close & Personal\" bios** (one per day card, rotating; the player's own athlete gets one on Day 1):\n- **Dash Goldberry (SUN):** \"Dash grew up on a farm in rural Sunvale, chasing the family's prize ostrich to school\n  every morning. The ostrich never once let him win. Today, he runs for Daisy.\"\n- **Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM):** \"Ingrid's grandmother taught her to ski jump off the roof of the family sauna. The sauna\n  has since been rebuilt. Twice.\"\n- **Max Overdrive (TRB):** \"Defending champion in, quote, 'everything'. Max has never lost a race, a staring contest,\n  or an argument with a mirror. His hobbies include winning and describing winning.\"\n- **Coco Bonbon (BON):** \"Coco skates every program to the songs her grandfather whistled. She says she can still hear\n  him in the crowd. Usually slightly off-key.\"\n- **Blaze Cinderhart (VOL):** \"Every winter morning, Blaze lifts the family car out of a volcanic ash drift. The car is\n  fine. The car is extremely well-defined.\"\n- **Marina Splashworth (WAV):** \"Born on a houseboat, Marina didn't touch dry land until she was four. On land she still\n  walks like the deck is moving. In the water... poetry.\"\n- **Rocky Summit (MTP):** \"Rocky's village sits so high that the mail arrives by curling stone. He has been sweeping since\n  before he could walk. His first word was 'HARD!'\"\n- **Pixel Vance (NEO):** \"Pixel learned archery from an arcade cabinet and has never seen daylight without sunglasses.\n  Pixel's coach is a toaster named Gary. Gary believes in Pixel.\"\n\n### 7.2 Venues (levels)\n\n| Venue | Events / scenes | View | Light | Key art (all drawn in code; generic props from the engine library/asset store) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Glory Stadium** (Sunny Bay) | 100m, Javelin; opening & closing ceremonies; stadium podiums | brawler | day (events), night + fireworks (ceremonies) | red 8-lane track with lane numbers, infield grass with mown stripes, 3-tier stands + crowd, the cauldron tower, jumbotron, finish gantry & clock, flags of the 8 nations on the rim, the blimp, parking lot past the wall |\n| **Splash Palace** | 50m Free, Diving | brawler / side | indoor bright, caustics | pool, lane ropes, blocks, flags line, the dive tower, judges' table, windows onto the beach, jumbotron |\n| **Bullseye Lawn** | Archery | overlay + side inset | sunny, breezy | target faces, palms, the sea, wind flags, shade tent |\n| **Iron Hall** | Weightlifting | brawler | dark, two spotlights | platform, chalk bowl, referee lights, plate rack, dim crowd |\n| **Mount Glory Jumping Hill** | Ski Jump | side | night floodlights, light snow | tower, in-run, K/HS lines, distance boards, out-run crowd with cowbells and flags |\n| **The Yikes Face** | Downhill | E.Road | bright day, sun glare, light snow | piste, orange netting, pines, start hut, ice tunnel, jumps, finish arch, grandstand |\n| **Glory Ice Track** | Bobsled | E.Road | dusk, floodlights | ice channel, named curve signs, tunnels, timing boards |\n| **Glory Ice Palace** | Figure Skating | threequarter | spotlights | rink, kiss & cry, flowers, plush rain |\n| **Glory Curling Club** | Curling | topdown | warm indoor | sheet, houses, scoreboard, pennants |\n| **Glory Arena** | Ice Hockey | threequarter | dark arena + spots | rink, glass, center jumbotron cube, goal lights, organ loft |\n\nUse `node vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/tools/asset-find.mjs \"<thing>\"` for generic props (benches, fences, pines,\nsnow blocks, banners, lamps, flags: the `kenney-holiday`, `kenney-nature`, `ambientcg` sets have snow, pines, ice and\nfences); cut the few you use into a set of your own with `tools/asset-set.mjs` and inline it.\n\n### 7.3 Story structure (The Games)\n\n| When | Beat | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| Start | **Opening ceremony** | §7.4 |\n| Day 1 (before) | Max's welcome | in the call room: \"Lane four? Cute. I'm in lane five. Lane five is where legends warm up.\" |\n| After Day 2 | **Mascot incident 1** | Yikesy \"test-jumps\" the ski jump: a 6 s cutscene (the Blob launched, spinning, lands in a snowbank head-first). Chip: \"The mascot has... the mascot has set a personal best!\" Vera: \"And a personal worst. Simultaneously.\" |\n| After Day 4 | Curling chat | Rocky: \"Back home we curl to settle arguments. Mostly about curling.\" |\n| After Day 6 | **HALFTIME REPORT** | medal table + banter; Yikesy appears, dripping (\"rescued from the pool filter\"); Max line depends on standings (§7.6) |\n| After Day 8 | Coco's moment | Coco (any result): \"Grandpa, that one was for you.\" Vera, quietly: \"...Give me a second, Chip.\" |\n| After Day 10 | Sled scandal | Vera: \"Turbonia's sled has a spoiler. And a cup holder.\" Max: \"It's called aerodynamic hospitality.\" |\n| Day 12 (before) | **THE FINAL** | both anthems tease; Max: \"Two nations. One puck. Zero chance. For you.\" |\n| After Day 12 | Sportsmanship | win: Max: \"...Good game. Next Games I'm bringing two helmets. One for my ego.\" · loss: Max: \"Good game. You were almost me.\" |\n| End | **Closing ceremony** | §7.4; ending by rank |\n| Dynamic | Rival reactions | after any event with you and Max both in the top 4: a line from the bank (beat him / he beat you) |\n| Dynamic | Records & yikes | a WR by you → Vera's sentimental line; 5+ yikes → Vera: \"Statistically, the most entertaining athlete in Games history.\" |\n\n### 7.4 Ceremony scripts\n\n**Opening ceremony** (Glory Stadium at night, ~60 s, hold ✕ 1 s to skip):","numLines":100,"startLine":1008,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R26faCXWaP1fUPyyQTBfYL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
