{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2cNE3HJAXJA3y8HfR2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UYjNREWv92GKTqVFFQNQtW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":1105,"limit":130},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4996,"cache_read_input_tokens":489046,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4996},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"c8f73a63-32a2-48ed-93fe-894efd60682e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:53.892Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2cMxeve564ZiRsKbZp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UYjNREWv92GKTqVFFQNQtW":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":1105,"limit":130}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UYjNREWv92GKTqVFFQNQtW","type":"tool_result","content":"1105\t### 7.4 Ceremony scripts\n1106\t\n1107\t**Opening ceremony** (Glory Stadium at night, ~60 s, hold ✕ 1 s to skip):\n1108\t1. Fireworks over the twin city (the ski jump floodlit beyond the stadium rim). PA (echo): \"Ladies and gentlemen...\n1109\t   welcome to the Games of Mount Glory and Sunny Bay!\"\n1110\t2. Chip: \"Good evening, everybody! For the first time in history, the Summer and Winter Games are happening at the\n1111\t   SAME TIME, in the SAME PLACE!\" Vera: \"Some called it impossible. Others called it a scheduling error. Tonight we\n1112\t   call it... OLYMPIYIKES!\"\n1113\t3. **Parade of nations** (rigs marching in tracksuits behind a flag bearer, crowd waving that nation's colors), one\n1114\t   line each: SUNVALE \"where the sun never sets and the sunscreen budget is classified.\" · FROSTMARK \"their flag bearer\n1115\t   is carrying the flag AND a small sauna.\" · TURBONIA \"led by defending champion Max Overdrive, who has asked us to\n1116\t   call him 'The Defending Champion', even while he sleeps.\" · BONBONIA \"their uniforms are, legally, dessert.\" ·\n1117\t   VOLCANICA \"please don't stand too close. They're very warm people.\" · WAVELIA \"they arrived by boat. They prefer\n1118\t   it.\" · MOUNTOPIA \"they train at altitude, with less oxygen and more yodeling.\" · NEON REPUBLIC \"their uniforms\n1119\t   come with a firmware update.\" The player's nation enters last: \"And finally... the nation everyone came to see!\"\n1120\t4. **The flame (playable):** \"The final torchbearer is... YOU!\" A flaming javelin throw at the cauldron: hold\n1121\t   `action`, release in the gold zone of a `TimingBar`. Perfect: \"Bullseye! The cauldron is LIT!\" (+0.25 hype into\n1122\t   Day 1). Miss: the javelin hits the scoreboard, the scoreboard catches fire, \"...and the scoreboard is now the\n1123\t   cauldron. Olympiyikes!\" (it still lights).\n1124\t5. Max, in the tunnel (portrait close-up): \"Nice throw. Enjoy it. It's the closest you'll get to gold.\" Vera: \"Let\n1125\t   the Games... begin!\" Grand fireworks finale.\n1126\t\n1127\t**Medal ceremony** (each event, ~12 s, ✕ skips after 2 s): podium blocks 2–1–3 in the venue; athletes walk up; medals\n1128\tappear on their chests (a sprite at the neck joint); three flags rise on poles (tweens); the winner's **procedural\n1129\tanthem** (§9.5) plays; camera flashes; confetti in the winner's colors; one commentary line.\n1130\t\n1131\t**Closing ceremony** (~70 s, skippable): the final medal table on the jumbotron; all athletes dance in the infield\n1132\t(`cheer`, `wave`, spins); the \"Yikes reel\" counter for each nation; a snow cannon misfires and **puts out the\n1133\tcauldron** (\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"), then all eight star athletes relight it together with their torches; the motto appears:\n1134\t**FASTER. HIGHER. YIKES.**; the ending text; then the credits (paged).\n1135\t\n1136\t**Endings by your nation's final rank:**\n1137\t- 1st: \"Your nation tops the medal table! Back home they're renaming a mountain after you. It's a small mountain.\n1138\t  It's a hill. But it's YOUR hill.\"\n1139\t- 2nd–3rd: \"A podium nation! Respect. Max sends a fruit basket. It's mostly lemons.\"\n1140\t- 4th–8th: \"The medals didn't come, but the highlights did. Your yikes reel has four million views. Next Games, champ.\"\n1141\t- Multi-human Games add the **party champion** podium (by party points) before the ending.\n1142\t\n1143\t### 7.5 Records (in-world World Records, seeded into `oly:records`)\n1144\t\n1145\t| Event | WR | Holder | Qualify E / N / H |\n1146\t|---|---|---|---|\n1147\t| 100m Dash | 9.48 s | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 12.30 / 11.40 / 10.60 |\n1148\t| Javelin | 101.20 m | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 58 / 72 / 82 m |\n1149\t| 50m Freestyle | 19.62 s | Marina Splashworth (WAV) | 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6 |\n1150\t| 10m Diving | 338.40 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 150 / 195 / 240 |\n1151\t| Archery | 60 (6 X) | Pixel Vance (NEO) | 40 / 48 / 53 |\n1152\t| Weightlifting | 270 kg | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 200 / 225 / 245 kg |\n1153\t| Ski Jump | 296.4 (hill record 148.0 m) | Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM) | 160 / 210 / 245 |\n1154\t| Downhill | 47.62 s | Rocky Summit (MTP) | 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0 |\n1155\t| Bobsled | 40.11 s per run (80.40 total) | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0 |\n1156\t| Figure Skating | 228.56 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 120 / 150 / 180 |\n1157\t| Curling, Ice Hockey | match events: \"most points in a final\" records (curling 6, hockey 7) | Rocky Summit / Max Overdrive | — |\n1158\t\n1159\tThe top-5 table of each event starts with the WR holder plus four seeded CPU marks a little below it.\n1160\t\n1161\t### 7.6 Commentary banks (write ≥ 160 lines in total; samples below set the voice)\n1162\t\n1163\tStyle: earnest Olympic broadcast (statistics, sentiment, national pride, \"up close and personal\") colliding with\n1164\tarcade bombast. Chip exaggerates; Vera undercuts with memories and dry wit. Short lines (≤ 70 characters each half).\n1165\t\n1166\t**Generic keys:** `start, lead, close, photo, wr, gr, pb, yikes, falsestart, foul, turbo, win, lose, last, comeback,\n1167\trivalBeat, rivalWins, idle (filler), dnf`.\n1168\t- start: Chip \"And they're OFF!\" · Chip \"Here we go, folks, the moment of truth!\" · Vera \"Breathe. That's all I ever told myself. Breathe and go.\"\n1169\t- lead: Chip \"{name} takes the lead for {nation}!\" · Chip \"{name} hits the front and the crowd is ON ITS FEET!\"\n1170\t- close: Chip \"Too close to call!\" · Vera \"Somebody fetch a ruler. A very small ruler.\"\n1171\t- photo: Chip \"We go to the PHOTO!\" · Vera \"Grab some popcorn, Chip. Photos take a while.\"\n1172\t- wr: Chip \"A NEW WORLD RECORD! Somebody call the record books! Somebody call the record books' MOTHER!\" · Vera \"I held a world record once. For eleven minutes. Cherish this.\"\n1173\t- yikes: Chip \"OLYMPIYIKES! That's going on the highlight reel for a thousand years!\" · Vera \"They're okay. The snow will need counseling.\" · Chip \"OH NO. Oh no no no. Oh... yes, actually, that was amazing.\"\n1174\t- falsestart: Chip \"Too eager! The gun hadn't even THOUGHT about firing!\" · Vera \"Nerves. I once false-started a press conference.\"\n1175\t- foul: Chip \"Over the line! The judges say NO!\" · Vera \"Lines are there for a reason. Mostly to be stepped on.\"\n1176\t- turbo: Chip \"{name} is ON FIRE!\" · Chip \"LOOK at that! Is that legal? Vera, is that legal?\" Vera \"Entirely. I checked in 1988.\"\n1177\t- win: Chip \"GOLD for {nation}!\" · Vera \"Somewhere, a small town is throwing a very loud party.\"\n1178\t- rivalWins: Max \"Second place is just first loser. That's a quote. Mine.\" · Max \"Did you see me? Everybody saw me.\"\n1179\t- rivalBeat: Max \"That was a fluke. A very fast fluke.\" · Max \"I let you have that one. For morale. Yours.\" · Max \"I'm not crying. Turbonians don't cry. We vent.\"\n1180\t- halftime (lead): Max \"Halftime means nothing. I'm a second-half athlete.\" · (trail) Max \"Halfway home, and already bored of winning.\"\n1181\t\n1182\t**Per event (≥ 8 each), examples:**\n1183\t- Sprint: \"Ten seconds. A whole life of training for ten seconds.\" · \"That's not a start, that's a LAUNCH!\"\n1184\t- Javelin: \"That javelin is still climbing!\" · \"It's left the stadium! Someone check the parking lot!\"\n1185\t- Swim: \"Perfect turn! Like a dolphin with a mortgage to pay!\" · Vera \"I could never do flip turns. I did flip-flops.\"\n1186\t- Diving: \"A rip entry! You could hear a pin drop. You could NOT hear that diver!\" · \"SLAP! You could hear that one in the next time zone.\"\n1187\t- Archery: \"Dead center! The wind didn't stand a chance.\" · Vera \"I tried archery once. The target was very relieved.\"\n1188\t- Weights: \"Look at that bar BEND!\" · \"Three white lights! GOOD LIFT!\"\n1189\t- Ski jump: \"He's flying! Is he still flying? HE'S STILL FLYING!\" · Vera \"Gravity always wins. It just takes its time.\"\n1190\t- Downhill: \"One hundred and thirty kilometers an hour down a frozen cliff. On purpose.\" · \"Into the netting! The netting has done its job!\"\n1191\t- Bobsled: \"Through the Omega like it isn't even there!\" · \"They're upside down! Still fast, though!\"\n1192\t- Figure: \"A quad! A QUAD YIKES!\" · Vera \"Grandpa would be whistling now.\"\n1193\t- Curling: \"HURRY HARD! HURRY HARD!\" · \"Double takeout! The house has been CLEARED!\"\n1194\t- Hockey: \"He shoots... he SCORES!\" · \"Into the glass! The glass is fine. The glass is always fine.\"\n1195\t\n1196\t**PA lines:** \"In lane {lane}... representing {nation}... {name}!\" · \"Ladies and gentlemen, a new World Record!\" ·\n1197\t\"Please rise for the anthem of {nation}.\"\n1198\t\n1199\t### 7.7 Pictograms, emblem, flags\n1200\t\n1201\t- **12 pictograms** (16×16 `E.sprite` strings; white figure on a rounded tile, summer coral `#ff6b4a`, winter ice-blue\n1202\t  `#3fa8e8`; drawn ×2 or ×3 on cards): sprint (leaning runner), javelin (arm back, diagonal shaft), swim (head and\n1203\t  arm arc over waves), diving (inverted figure over a splash), archery (figure drawing a bow), weights (bar overhead),\n1204\t  ski jump (forward-leaning figure on long V skis), downhill (tucked skier, diagonal), bobsled (sled with two\n1205\t  helmets), figure (spinning figure, one leg out), curling (stone + broom), hockey (stick + puck + skater). Used on the\n1206\t  schedule, event cards, results, Single Event tiles, the HUD and the records tabs.\n1207\t- **Emblem \"the Yikes Flame\":** a flame split down the middle, orange (summer) and ice-blue (winter), inside a gold\n1208\t  laurel wreath. Title, ceremonies, hub card, favicon (an inline SVG data URI of the same shape).\n1209\t- **Flags:** `O.Art.flag(g, x, y, w, h, nation, wave)` draws each flag from its spec with a 2-step cloth wave and\n1210\t  shading (`E.tones`).\n1211\t\n1212\t### 7.8 Items, power-ups, opponents and hazards\n1213\t\n1214\t| Kind | Content |\n1215\t|---|---|\n1216\t| **Equipment (items)** | spikes and blocks, javelin, swim cap and goggles, bow and arrows, barbell and color-coded plates, jump skis, downhill skis and poles, the two-man sled, curling stones and brooms, hockey sticks, puck and nets, the torch. Drawn by `O.Gear` (§8.2) in the nation's colors |\n1217\t| **Golden gear (unlock)** | winning gold in an event turns that event's equipment golden for that nation in later plays (saved in the cabinet); shown in Records → Cabinet |\n1218\t| **Power-ups** | YIKES TURBO (one per event, §6: HYPER ARM, DOLPHIN MODE, SLOW-MO SUPREMACY, EAGLE EYE, IRON WILL, ROCKET SKIS, AVALANCHE, JET SLED, STAR POWER, HYPER SWEEP, ON FIRE and the sprint's TURBO); sympathy hype after a yikes; speed gates in the downhill |\n1219\t| **Collectibles** | medals (cabinet), 12 laurels, world records and top-5 places with initials |\n1220\t| **Opponents (\"enemies\")** | the 7 CPU nations' stars with per-event skills (§7.1); the rival Max Overdrive (+0.03, always shown live); CPU curling skips that plan shots by simulation; the Turbonia hockey team and the goalies |\n1221\t| **Hazards** | the starter's gun (false starts), the foul line, wind and gusts, the pool wall, the take-off table's edge, gravity under a loaded bar, orange netting, crests that launch you, the tunnel's ice, banked walls that flip a sled, the hog and back lines, the boards and the glass |\n1222\t\n1223\t---\n1224\t\n1225\t## 8. Art and animation\n1226\t\n1227\t### 8.1 Look (the engine's native style, pushed to its look target)\n1228\t\n1229\tFollow every step of API.md's \"Look target\": `res: 'ps1'` + `expand`, HD Humanoids at size 1.25 dressed in each\n1230\tnation's palette, a backdrop or painted horizon behind every view, textured floors (`floorTex` functions for track,\n1231\tgrass, pool water, ice with scratches, snow with sparkle), 3–8 props per screen (`r.prop`/`r.shape`: flags, banners,\n1232\tlamps, benches, pines, fences, barriers, cameras on tripods, medal tables), effects on every impact, `E.font.title`\n1233\tlogos, lights in every scene, faces in every dialog (portraits). The season split in palettes: summer warm (gold,\n1234\tcoral, sky), winter cool (ice blue, violet, white) with warm floodlights; UI panels navy `#0c1028` with gold `#f2b632`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"2ff2a9fd-4cc3-496e-a8bb-27304732b554","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:53.898Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 7.4 Ceremony scripts\n\n**Opening ceremony** (Glory Stadium at night, ~60 s, hold ✕ 1 s to skip):\n1. Fireworks over the twin city (the ski jump floodlit beyond the stadium rim). PA (echo): \"Ladies and gentlemen...\n   welcome to the Games of Mount Glory and Sunny Bay!\"\n2. Chip: \"Good evening, everybody! For the first time in history, the Summer and Winter Games are happening at the\n   SAME TIME, in the SAME PLACE!\" Vera: \"Some called it impossible. Others called it a scheduling error. Tonight we\n   call it... OLYMPIYIKES!\"\n3. **Parade of nations** (rigs marching in tracksuits behind a flag bearer, crowd waving that nation's colors), one\n   line each: SUNVALE \"where the sun never sets and the sunscreen budget is classified.\" · FROSTMARK \"their flag bearer\n   is carrying the flag AND a small sauna.\" · TURBONIA \"led by defending champion Max Overdrive, who has asked us to\n   call him 'The Defending Champion', even while he sleeps.\" · BONBONIA \"their uniforms are, legally, dessert.\" ·\n   VOLCANICA \"please don't stand too close. They're very warm people.\" · WAVELIA \"they arrived by boat. They prefer\n   it.\" · MOUNTOPIA \"they train at altitude, with less oxygen and more yodeling.\" · NEON REPUBLIC \"their uniforms\n   come with a firmware update.\" The player's nation enters last: \"And finally... the nation everyone came to see!\"\n4. **The flame (playable):** \"The final torchbearer is... YOU!\" A flaming javelin throw at the cauldron: hold\n   `action`, release in the gold zone of a `TimingBar`. Perfect: \"Bullseye! The cauldron is LIT!\" (+0.25 hype into\n   Day 1). Miss: the javelin hits the scoreboard, the scoreboard catches fire, \"...and the scoreboard is now the\n   cauldron. Olympiyikes!\" (it still lights).\n5. Max, in the tunnel (portrait close-up): \"Nice throw. Enjoy it. It's the closest you'll get to gold.\" Vera: \"Let\n   the Games... begin!\" Grand fireworks finale.\n\n**Medal ceremony** (each event, ~12 s, ✕ skips after 2 s): podium blocks 2–1–3 in the venue; athletes walk up; medals\nappear on their chests (a sprite at the neck joint); three flags rise on poles (tweens); the winner's **procedural\nanthem** (§9.5) plays; camera flashes; confetti in the winner's colors; one commentary line.\n\n**Closing ceremony** (~70 s, skippable): the final medal table on the jumbotron; all athletes dance in the infield\n(`cheer`, `wave`, spins); the \"Yikes reel\" counter for each nation; a snow cannon misfires and **puts out the\ncauldron** (\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"), then all eight star athletes relight it together with their torches; the motto appears:\n**FASTER. HIGHER. YIKES.**; the ending text; then the credits (paged).\n\n**Endings by your nation's final rank:**\n- 1st: \"Your nation tops the medal table! Back home they're renaming a mountain after you. It's a small mountain.\n  It's a hill. But it's YOUR hill.\"\n- 2nd–3rd: \"A podium nation! Respect. Max sends a fruit basket. It's mostly lemons.\"\n- 4th–8th: \"The medals didn't come, but the highlights did. Your yikes reel has four million views. Next Games, champ.\"\n- Multi-human Games add the **party champion** podium (by party points) before the ending.\n\n### 7.5 Records (in-world World Records, seeded into `oly:records`)\n\n| Event | WR | Holder | Qualify E / N / H |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 100m Dash | 9.48 s | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 12.30 / 11.40 / 10.60 |\n| Javelin | 101.20 m | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 58 / 72 / 82 m |\n| 50m Freestyle | 19.62 s | Marina Splashworth (WAV) | 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6 |\n| 10m Diving | 338.40 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 150 / 195 / 240 |\n| Archery | 60 (6 X) | Pixel Vance (NEO) | 40 / 48 / 53 |\n| Weightlifting | 270 kg | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 200 / 225 / 245 kg |\n| Ski Jump | 296.4 (hill record 148.0 m) | Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM) | 160 / 210 / 245 |\n| Downhill | 47.62 s | Rocky Summit (MTP) | 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0 |\n| Bobsled | 40.11 s per run (80.40 total) | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0 |\n| Figure Skating | 228.56 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 120 / 150 / 180 |\n| Curling, Ice Hockey | match events: \"most points in a final\" records (curling 6, hockey 7) | Rocky Summit / Max Overdrive | — |\n\nThe top-5 table of each event starts with the WR holder plus four seeded CPU marks a little below it.\n\n### 7.6 Commentary banks (write ≥ 160 lines in total; samples below set the voice)\n\nStyle: earnest Olympic broadcast (statistics, sentiment, national pride, \"up close and personal\") colliding with\narcade bombast. Chip exaggerates; Vera undercuts with memories and dry wit. Short lines (≤ 70 characters each half).\n\n**Generic keys:** `start, lead, close, photo, wr, gr, pb, yikes, falsestart, foul, turbo, win, lose, last, comeback,\nrivalBeat, rivalWins, idle (filler), dnf`.\n- start: Chip \"And they're OFF!\" · Chip \"Here we go, folks, the moment of truth!\" · Vera \"Breathe. That's all I ever told myself. Breathe and go.\"\n- lead: Chip \"{name} takes the lead for {nation}!\" · Chip \"{name} hits the front and the crowd is ON ITS FEET!\"\n- close: Chip \"Too close to call!\" · Vera \"Somebody fetch a ruler. A very small ruler.\"\n- photo: Chip \"We go to the PHOTO!\" · Vera \"Grab some popcorn, Chip. Photos take a while.\"\n- wr: Chip \"A NEW WORLD RECORD! Somebody call the record books! Somebody call the record books' MOTHER!\" · Vera \"I held a world record once. For eleven minutes. Cherish this.\"\n- yikes: Chip \"OLYMPIYIKES! That's going on the highlight reel for a thousand years!\" · Vera \"They're okay. The snow will need counseling.\" · Chip \"OH NO. Oh no no no. Oh... yes, actually, that was amazing.\"\n- falsestart: Chip \"Too eager! The gun hadn't even THOUGHT about firing!\" · Vera \"Nerves. I once false-started a press conference.\"\n- foul: Chip \"Over the line! The judges say NO!\" · Vera \"Lines are there for a reason. Mostly to be stepped on.\"\n- turbo: Chip \"{name} is ON FIRE!\" · Chip \"LOOK at that! Is that legal? Vera, is that legal?\" Vera \"Entirely. I checked in 1988.\"\n- win: Chip \"GOLD for {nation}!\" · Vera \"Somewhere, a small town is throwing a very loud party.\"\n- rivalWins: Max \"Second place is just first loser. That's a quote. Mine.\" · Max \"Did you see me? Everybody saw me.\"\n- rivalBeat: Max \"That was a fluke. A very fast fluke.\" · Max \"I let you have that one. For morale. Yours.\" · Max \"I'm not crying. Turbonians don't cry. We vent.\"\n- halftime (lead): Max \"Halftime means nothing. I'm a second-half athlete.\" · (trail) Max \"Halfway home, and already bored of winning.\"\n\n**Per event (≥ 8 each), examples:**\n- Sprint: \"Ten seconds. A whole life of training for ten seconds.\" · \"That's not a start, that's a LAUNCH!\"\n- Javelin: \"That javelin is still climbing!\" · \"It's left the stadium! Someone check the parking lot!\"\n- Swim: \"Perfect turn! Like a dolphin with a mortgage to pay!\" · Vera \"I could never do flip turns. I did flip-flops.\"\n- Diving: \"A rip entry! You could hear a pin drop. You could NOT hear that diver!\" · \"SLAP! You could hear that one in the next time zone.\"\n- Archery: \"Dead center! The wind didn't stand a chance.\" · Vera \"I tried archery once. The target was very relieved.\"\n- Weights: \"Look at that bar BEND!\" · \"Three white lights! GOOD LIFT!\"\n- Ski jump: \"He's flying! Is he still flying? HE'S STILL FLYING!\" · Vera \"Gravity always wins. It just takes its time.\"\n- Downhill: \"One hundred and thirty kilometers an hour down a frozen cliff. On purpose.\" · \"Into the netting! The netting has done its job!\"\n- Bobsled: \"Through the Omega like it isn't even there!\" · \"They're upside down! Still fast, though!\"\n- Figure: \"A quad! A QUAD YIKES!\" · Vera \"Grandpa would be whistling now.\"\n- Curling: \"HURRY HARD! HURRY HARD!\" · \"Double takeout! The house has been CLEARED!\"\n- Hockey: \"He shoots... he SCORES!\" · \"Into the glass! The glass is fine. The glass is always fine.\"\n\n**PA lines:** \"In lane {lane}... representing {nation}... {name}!\" · \"Ladies and gentlemen, a new World Record!\" ·\n\"Please rise for the anthem of {nation}.\"\n\n### 7.7 Pictograms, emblem, flags\n\n- **12 pictograms** (16×16 `E.sprite` strings; white figure on a rounded tile, summer coral `#ff6b4a`, winter ice-blue\n  `#3fa8e8`; drawn ×2 or ×3 on cards): sprint (leaning runner), javelin (arm back, diagonal shaft), swim (head and\n  arm arc over waves), diving (inverted figure over a splash), archery (figure drawing a bow), weights (bar overhead),\n  ski jump (forward-leaning figure on long V skis), downhill (tucked skier, diagonal), bobsled (sled with two\n  helmets), figure (spinning figure, one leg out), curling (stone + broom), hockey (stick + puck + skater). Used on the\n  schedule, event cards, results, Single Event tiles, the HUD and the records tabs.\n- **Emblem \"the Yikes Flame\":** a flame split down the middle, orange (summer) and ice-blue (winter), inside a gold\n  laurel wreath. Title, ceremonies, hub card, favicon (an inline SVG data URI of the same shape).\n- **Flags:** `O.Art.flag(g, x, y, w, h, nation, wave)` draws each flag from its spec with a 2-step cloth wave and\n  shading (`E.tones`).\n\n### 7.8 Items, power-ups, opponents and hazards\n\n| Kind | Content |\n|---|---|\n| **Equipment (items)** | spikes and blocks, javelin, swim cap and goggles, bow and arrows, barbell and color-coded plates, jump skis, downhill skis and poles, the two-man sled, curling stones and brooms, hockey sticks, puck and nets, the torch. Drawn by `O.Gear` (§8.2) in the nation's colors |\n| **Golden gear (unlock)** | winning gold in an event turns that event's equipment golden for that nation in later plays (saved in the cabinet); shown in Records → Cabinet |\n| **Power-ups** | YIKES TURBO (one per event, §6: HYPER ARM, DOLPHIN MODE, SLOW-MO SUPREMACY, EAGLE EYE, IRON WILL, ROCKET SKIS, AVALANCHE, JET SLED, STAR POWER, HYPER SWEEP, ON FIRE and the sprint's TURBO); sympathy hype after a yikes; speed gates in the downhill |\n| **Collectibles** | medals (cabinet), 12 laurels, world records and top-5 places with initials |\n| **Opponents (\"enemies\")** | the 7 CPU nations' stars with per-event skills (§7.1); the rival Max Overdrive (+0.03, always shown live); CPU curling skips that plan shots by simulation; the Turbonia hockey team and the goalies |\n| **Hazards** | the starter's gun (false starts), the foul line, wind and gusts, the pool wall, the take-off table's edge, gravity under a loaded bar, orange netting, crests that launch you, the tunnel's ice, banked walls that flip a sled, the hog and back lines, the boards and the glass |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art and animation\n\n### 8.1 Look (the engine's native style, pushed to its look target)\n\nFollow every step of API.md's \"Look target\": `res: 'ps1'` + `expand`, HD Humanoids at size 1.25 dressed in each\nnation's palette, a backdrop or painted horizon behind every view, textured floors (`floorTex` functions for track,\ngrass, pool water, ice with scratches, snow with sparkle), 3–8 props per screen (`r.prop`/`r.shape`: flags, banners,\nlamps, benches, pines, fences, barriers, cameras on tripods, medal tables), effects on every impact, `E.font.title`\nlogos, lights in every scene, faces in every dialog (portraits). The season split in palettes: summer warm (gold,\ncoral, sky), winter cool (ice blue, violet, white) with warm floodlights; UI panels navy `#0c1028` with gold `#f2b632`","numLines":130,"startLine":1105,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UYjNREWv92GKTqVFFQNQtW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
