{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2czLSAtNYFDq5CRhsd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UJpsDUC74HtDmTLgGXXPej","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":1234,"limit":150},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5833,"cache_read_input_tokens":494042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5833},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"b998acd3-2d9d-426b-85ce-1737b77ecc9e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:06.795Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2cz6HvZSYS5HpZJxyr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UJpsDUC74HtDmTLgGXXPej":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","offset":1234,"limit":150}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UJpsDUC74HtDmTLgGXXPej","type":"tool_result","content":"1234\tcoral, sky), winter cool (ice blue, violet, white) with warm floodlights; UI panels navy `#0c1028` with gold `#f2b632`\n1235\ttrim. Screenshots should compare with the best PS1-era 2D, not NES.\n1236\t\n1237\t### 8.2 Pose layer (`O.Pose`, src/06-pose.js) and the engine's pose hook\n1238\t\n1239\t- The Humanoid already animates runs, jumps (`air`), crouch, kneel, cheer, wave, hips, down, die, rolls (`flip`),\n1240\t  climbs, landings (`rig.land`) and every move in `E.MOVES` (use `new E.Attack('throw')` for the javelin release,\n1241\t  `'bash'` for hockey checks, `'twohand'` for slapshots, `'cast'` for the torch raise). **Use these first.**\n1242\t- For what it lacks, `O.Pose.set(rig, name, params)` installs `rig.post = (rig, J) => ...` (engine change 5). A pose\n1243\t  edits joints in the rig's own frame `[forward, right, up]`: `J.hipC, hipL/R, kneeL/R, footL/R, shC, shL/R, elbowL/R,\n1244\t  handL/R, head`, using helpers `armTo(J, side, target, hint)` and `legTo(J, side, target, hint)` (two-bone IK with\n1245\t  `E.ik3` and the rig's limb lengths `rig.o.armUpper/armLower/legUpper/legLower`), `lean(J, fwd, side)`,\n1246\t  `look(J, dir)`. Poses blend in/out with a weight (ease .15 s). Whole-body rotations set `rig.bodyPitch`,\n1247\t  `rig.bodyRoll`, `rig.pivot`.\n1248\t- **Pose list** (each previewable in the Pose Lab, `#poselab`): `blocks` (sprint crouch, hands on the line), `set`\n1249\t  (hips up), `dip` (torso thrown forward), `javCarry` (right hand above the shoulder), `javWithdraw`, `swimCrawl(phase,\n1250\t  breath)` (prone via bodyPitch 90°, arms on circles around the shoulders, flutter kick, head turned on breaths),\n1251\t  `diveStart(u)`, `flipTurn(u)`, `armsUp` (diving stance), `tuck`, `pike`, `layout`, `entry` (hands joined over the\n1252\t  head), `bellyFlop`, `archerDraw(u)` (bow arm extended to the target, string hand to the jaw), `archerRelease`,\n1253\t  `liftSetup`, `liftClean(h)` (hands on the bar, bar height h), `liftRack`, `liftJerk(u)` (split stance, arms locked\n1254\t  overhead), `liftDrop(u)`, `skiTuck`, `skiFlight(α)` (V-style: straight body leaning over the skis, arms back),\n1255\t  `telemark`, `tumble(t)`, `bobPush`, `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`, `skateGlide`, `skateSpiral`, `sitSpin`, `skateJump`\n1256\t  (arms crossed), `skateLand`, `curlSlide` (deep lunge, hand on the stone), `sweep(phase)`, `skipPoint`,\n1257\t  `hockeyStride`, `stickHandle`, `goalieStance`, `kneeSlide` (goal celebration), `flagCarry`, `torchRaise`, `bowHead`\n1258\t  (receiving a medal), `medalBite`, `podiumWave`, `faceplant` (built-in `flip` roll + `down`).\n1259\t- **Gear** (`O.Gear`, drawn with `r.queue` at projected joint positions so it depth-sorts with the rig): javelin,\n1260\t  bow + string + arrow, barbell + plates (ellipses facing the camera) with bend, skis (two long quads from the feet\n1261\t  along the ski direction, V in flight), poles, helmets/goggles, swim cap/goggles, bobsled (boxes through the view,\n1262\t  like `kits/kart.js` `box()`), curling stone and broom, hockey stick (line from hands to a blade on the ice) and puck,\n1263\t  medals, flags on poles, torch (with `particles.fire` and a light).\n1264\t- **Rear view for E.Road events:** `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18, 1.6, 1)`; a rig with `facing: Math.PI / 2` faces\n1265\t  into the screen. Draw it inside the road's overlay at the skier's screen point (`rig.draw(g, sx, sy, REAR)`); for\n1266\t  ghosts and other sleds at a distance, cache views per quantized scale (`E.View(..., scale)` at 12 steps) as\n1267\t  `m7.view(k)` does in the kart kit.\n1268\t- **Check every pose** with `tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#poselab/<pose> --steps \"wait:300 rec:16:2\" --seed 1`: no\n1269\t  joints through the body, no snapping when blending, readable silhouettes at 1×.\n1270\t\n1271\t### 8.3 Effects\n1272\t\n1273\tFireworks (`particles.explosion(..., { debris: false })` + colored `glints`, launched with trails), confetti (`bits`\n1274\tin nation colors), splashes (blue/white `bit` particles sized by entry error; a rip makes only bubbles), snow spray\n1275\t(white dust on carves and crashes), sparks (sled scrapes, curling clacks, skate stops), chalk dust, camera flashes\n1276\t(white glints in the stands), turbo flames (`fire` + emissive glow), the gun's smoke puff, speed lines and sun\n1277\tglare overlays on the road events, the \"YIKES!\" stamp, the WR burst (rays + stars), the plush rain.\n1278\t\n1279\t### 8.4 Lighting per venue\n1280\t\n1281\t`game.lights.enabled = true` in every venue's enter: stadium day ambient .85 warm; stadium night .4 + stadium\n1282\tfloodlights + fireworks flashes; pool .8 cool + caustic glows; lawn .9; Iron Hall .35 + two warm spots; ski jump .35\n1283\t+ floodlights along the hill; ice palace .45 + moving colored spots; curling .6 warm; arena .4 + spots + goal light\n1284\tflash. E.Road scenes draw as overlays (unlit): bake the mood into their colors and add additive glow sprites.\n1285\t\n1286\t### 8.5 The mascot: YIKESY\n1287\t\n1288\tAn `E.Blob({ R: 9, ears: 'cat', feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#f8f8ff', dk: '#d8e2f0', lt: '#ffffff' } })`\n1289\t(a round snow-yeti) with a flame tuft on its head (fire particles + glow) and a half-orange/half-blue scarf drawn on\n1290\ttop. Appears on the title, in ceremonies, story beats, the attract mode, the curling scoreboard, as plush toys on the\n1291\tice, and in the Pose Lab. Voice: squeaky gibberish (pitch 1.9).\n1292\t\n1293\t---\n1294\t\n1295\t## 9. Audio (all in code)\n1296\t\n1297\t### 9.1 Music (engine songs `{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks }`, every one original)\n1298\t\n1299\t| Id | Where | Feel | BPM | Notes |\n1300\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1301\t| `title` | title, menus' first entry | heroic brass fanfare with a comic chromatic \"yikes\" slide, then triumph | 120 | motif below |\n1302\t| `menu` | main menu, setup screens | bright funk-pop loop | 112 | |\n1303\t| `parade` | opening ceremony | march, snare rolls | 116 | |\n1304\t| `sprint` | 100m | chiptune drum & bass | 172 | `hype` drum layer |\n1305\t| `javelin` | javelin | funky groove | 104 | |\n1306\t| `swim` | 50m free | bubbly arpeggios | 128 | |\n1307\t| `diving` | diving | sparse, timpani, suspense | 90 | |\n1308\t| `archery` | archery | tense minimal + heartbeat kick | 80 | heartbeat speeds with `hr` |\n1309\t| `iron` | weightlifting | heavy rock riff (saw bass) | 96 | |\n1310\t| `alpine` | ski jump | floodlit alpine pulse, bells | 124 | |\n1311\t| `yikesface` | downhill | driving rock | 150 | |\n1312\t| `icesurf` | bobsled | surf rock | 160 | |\n1313\t| `waltz` | figure skating | \"Waltz of the Yikes\", 3/4 (bars of 12 steps) | 138 | the rhythm chart's song |\n1314\t| `lounge` | curling | lounge jazz (swing feel) | 92 | |\n1315\t| `organ` | hockey | stadium organ + chant | 132 | goal horn sting |\n1316\t| `table` | results, medal table | proud, warm | 100 | |\n1317\t| `closing` | closing ceremony, credits | emotional anthem turning into a party | 96 → 128 | |\n1318\t| stings | WR, YIKES (descending trombone \"wah-wah-wah-waaah\"), laurel, qualify fail, games over, victory, goal horn | | | `audio.sting` |\n1319\t\n1320\tEvery event song names a `hype` track (`on: false`) faded in during turbo. Title motif (lead, one token a 16th, bars\n1321\tof 16): `G4 - - - C5 - - - E5 - - - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - B5 - A5 - G5 - - - | A5 - - - F5 - - - D5 - - - G5 - - - |\n1322\tE5 - - - D#5 - - - D5 - - - C#5 - - - | C5 - - - . . G4 - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - - - - - . . . .`\n1323\tover a bass `C3 C3 G2 G2 | A2 A2 E2 E2 | F2 F2 G2 G2 | C3 B2 Bb2 A2 | F2 G2 C3 - | C3 - - -` (quarters) and drums\n1324\t`k . . . s . . . k . k . s . . .` with a snare roll into the last bar. Keep the \"rise, comic slide, recover\" shape:\n1325\tit is the game's sonic logo.\n1326\t\n1327\t### 9.2 Sound effects (`audio.define`, layered voices; names → recipe)\n1328\t\n1329\t`gun` (noise burst 1800→200 Hz .12 s + sine 90→40 .3 s), `beep` (sine 880 .15), `step` (engine preset, pitched by\n1330\tspeed), `whoosh`, `thunk` (javelin into turf: noise lowpass + sine 140→60), `boing` (triangle 300→600→300 with vib),\n1331\t`twang` (pulse 220→180 with fast vibrato), `thwack` (noise 3000→800 .05 + sine 180), `clank` (square 800 + noise,\n1332\tmetallic `arp`), `slam` (bar drop: boom preset + rattle), `splash` (noise 2000→300 .5, size by vol), `slap` (belly\n1333\tflop: noise 4000→900 .08 + boom), `bubbles` (sine blips 600–1200), `swish` (ski carve: noise highpass 2–4 kHz),\n1334\t`crunch` (snow), `rumble` (sled: low noise loop by speed), `scrape` (noise 3–6 kHz + square 70), `clack` (stone:\n1335\tnoise 1500 .04 + square 400), `brush` (sweep: noise bursts), `puck` (click 2000 .03), `check` (boom + noise),\n1336\t`glass` (noise 5 kHz + triangle 1200 shimmer), `horn` (saw 220 + 277 + 330 1.2 s), `buzzer` (square 180 .8 s),\n1337\t`whistle` (from the sports kit), `cowbell` (square 560 + 840 decay), `camera` (click + highpass noise), `firework`\n1338\t(explode + crackle bits), `medal` (chime triangle C6–E6–G6), `cough` (noise formant), `alarm` (car alarm: square\n1339\t880↔660), `pop` (blimp: noise 3000→100), `yikes` sting. All go through the engine's sfx bus (volume settings apply).\n1340\t\n1341\t### 9.3 Voices: `O.Voice.speak(text, voice)` (Animalese/Simlish gibberish)\n1342\t\n1343\t- Split the line into syllables (`/[^aeiouy\\s]*[aeiouy]+[^aeiouy\\s]*|[.,!?]/gi`). For each syllable: vowel → formants\n1344\t  (a 730/1090, e 530/1840, i 270/2290, o 570/840, u 300/870, y 300/2000 Hz) scaled by the voice's `formant` (female\n1345\t  1.15, child/mascot 1.5); pitch `f0 = voice.base · 2^((hashOffset + contour)/12)` with `hashOffset` −3…+3 semitones\n1346\t  from a hash of the syllable (deterministic: never `Math.random`), contour rising on a question's last syllable,\n1347\t  falling on a period, +4 semitones and faster on \"!\". Duration `(.075 + .012·len) / voice.speed`, gap .02 s, pauses\n1348\t  .12 (comma) / .22 (period).\n1349\t- Source: an `OscillatorNode` (sawtooth for Chip, triangle for Vera, square for the PA, pulse for Max) with a little\n1350\t  vibrato and a −1 semitone fall at the end; consonant onsets add a 12 ms highpassed noise tick; two parallel band-pass\n1351\t  filters at F1 (Q 6) and F2 (Q 9); envelope 5 ms attack, 25 ms release; into the voice bus (engine change 6). The PA\n1352\t  adds a `DelayNode` echo (.18 s, feedback .3).\n1353\t- Returns the line's duration (subtitle timing, portrait mouth). Headless or before the first input: returns the\n1354\t  duration and makes no sound.\n1355\t- Voices: Chip (base 140 Hz, speed 1.15), Vera (210, .95), PA (120, .8, echo), Max (150, 1.25), each athlete per §7.1\n1356\t  (base 130 Hz × pitch), Yikesy (420, 1.4), crowd chant (6 detuned voices on \"O-LY-YI-KES!\").\n1357\t\n1358\t### 9.4 Crowd\n1359\t\n1360\t`O.CrowdAudio`: a looping noise source → band-pass (900 Hz, Q .7) → gain = `crowd volume × (.15 + .6·level)`, plus a\n1361\tlow murmur layer; events: cheer swell (level → 1, filter up), gasp (fast filter fall), \"OOOH\" (a cluster of 6 voices on\n1362\t\"oooh\"), applause (deterministic clap bursts), the chant, cowbells (winter outdoor), organ stabs (arena). Starts at the\n1363\tfirst user input (browsers' rule), ducks under the pause menu.\n1364\t\n1365\t### 9.5 Anthems\n1366\t\n1367\t`O.Anthem.song(nation)`: deterministic from the nation's seed: a major key (C, D, Eb, F, G or Bb), 8 bars of 4/4 at\n1368\t84–96 bpm, rhythm cells drawn from a small set (half + 2 quarters, dotted quarter + eighth + half, 4 quarters), melody\n1369\ton chord tones on strong beats over I–IV–V–I–vi–IV–V–I, brass lead (saw), harmony (square, quiet), bass (triangle),\n1370\ttimpani (low sine `k`) on downbeats and a snare roll into bar 8. ≈ 20 s, played once at the medal ceremony (and a\n1371\t4-bar excerpt for \"THE FINAL\" tease). Two nations never share a melody (test).\n1372\t\n1373\t### 9.6 Mix\n1374\t\n1375\tDefaults: master .7 (engine), music .5, effects 1, voices .8, crowd .7. While a commentary line plays, music ducks\n1376\t×0.7. Pause ducks everything (engine). Sound on/off and every volume live in the engine's Settings → Sound.\n1377\t\n1378\t---\n1379\t\n1380\t## 10. Modes and flow\n1381\t\n1382\t### 10.1 The Games (the campaign)\n1383\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"bafa14b5-8130-4bf8-8a2c-8ee403a7466b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:06.807Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"coral, sky), winter cool (ice blue, violet, white) with warm floodlights; UI panels navy `#0c1028` with gold `#f2b632`\ntrim. Screenshots should compare with the best PS1-era 2D, not NES.\n\n### 8.2 Pose layer (`O.Pose`, src/06-pose.js) and the engine's pose hook\n\n- The Humanoid already animates runs, jumps (`air`), crouch, kneel, cheer, wave, hips, down, die, rolls (`flip`),\n  climbs, landings (`rig.land`) and every move in `E.MOVES` (use `new E.Attack('throw')` for the javelin release,\n  `'bash'` for hockey checks, `'twohand'` for slapshots, `'cast'` for the torch raise). **Use these first.**\n- For what it lacks, `O.Pose.set(rig, name, params)` installs `rig.post = (rig, J) => ...` (engine change 5). A pose\n  edits joints in the rig's own frame `[forward, right, up]`: `J.hipC, hipL/R, kneeL/R, footL/R, shC, shL/R, elbowL/R,\n  handL/R, head`, using helpers `armTo(J, side, target, hint)` and `legTo(J, side, target, hint)` (two-bone IK with\n  `E.ik3` and the rig's limb lengths `rig.o.armUpper/armLower/legUpper/legLower`), `lean(J, fwd, side)`,\n  `look(J, dir)`. Poses blend in/out with a weight (ease .15 s). Whole-body rotations set `rig.bodyPitch`,\n  `rig.bodyRoll`, `rig.pivot`.\n- **Pose list** (each previewable in the Pose Lab, `#poselab`): `blocks` (sprint crouch, hands on the line), `set`\n  (hips up), `dip` (torso thrown forward), `javCarry` (right hand above the shoulder), `javWithdraw`, `swimCrawl(phase,\n  breath)` (prone via bodyPitch 90°, arms on circles around the shoulders, flutter kick, head turned on breaths),\n  `diveStart(u)`, `flipTurn(u)`, `armsUp` (diving stance), `tuck`, `pike`, `layout`, `entry` (hands joined over the\n  head), `bellyFlop`, `archerDraw(u)` (bow arm extended to the target, string hand to the jaw), `archerRelease`,\n  `liftSetup`, `liftClean(h)` (hands on the bar, bar height h), `liftRack`, `liftJerk(u)` (split stance, arms locked\n  overhead), `liftDrop(u)`, `skiTuck`, `skiFlight(α)` (V-style: straight body leaning over the skis, arms back),\n  `telemark`, `tumble(t)`, `bobPush`, `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`, `skateGlide`, `skateSpiral`, `sitSpin`, `skateJump`\n  (arms crossed), `skateLand`, `curlSlide` (deep lunge, hand on the stone), `sweep(phase)`, `skipPoint`,\n  `hockeyStride`, `stickHandle`, `goalieStance`, `kneeSlide` (goal celebration), `flagCarry`, `torchRaise`, `bowHead`\n  (receiving a medal), `medalBite`, `podiumWave`, `faceplant` (built-in `flip` roll + `down`).\n- **Gear** (`O.Gear`, drawn with `r.queue` at projected joint positions so it depth-sorts with the rig): javelin,\n  bow + string + arrow, barbell + plates (ellipses facing the camera) with bend, skis (two long quads from the feet\n  along the ski direction, V in flight), poles, helmets/goggles, swim cap/goggles, bobsled (boxes through the view,\n  like `kits/kart.js` `box()`), curling stone and broom, hockey stick (line from hands to a blade on the ice) and puck,\n  medals, flags on poles, torch (with `particles.fire` and a light).\n- **Rear view for E.Road events:** `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18, 1.6, 1)`; a rig with `facing: Math.PI / 2` faces\n  into the screen. Draw it inside the road's overlay at the skier's screen point (`rig.draw(g, sx, sy, REAR)`); for\n  ghosts and other sleds at a distance, cache views per quantized scale (`E.View(..., scale)` at 12 steps) as\n  `m7.view(k)` does in the kart kit.\n- **Check every pose** with `tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#poselab/<pose> --steps \"wait:300 rec:16:2\" --seed 1`: no\n  joints through the body, no snapping when blending, readable silhouettes at 1×.\n\n### 8.3 Effects\n\nFireworks (`particles.explosion(..., { debris: false })` + colored `glints`, launched with trails), confetti (`bits`\nin nation colors), splashes (blue/white `bit` particles sized by entry error; a rip makes only bubbles), snow spray\n(white dust on carves and crashes), sparks (sled scrapes, curling clacks, skate stops), chalk dust, camera flashes\n(white glints in the stands), turbo flames (`fire` + emissive glow), the gun's smoke puff, speed lines and sun\nglare overlays on the road events, the \"YIKES!\" stamp, the WR burst (rays + stars), the plush rain.\n\n### 8.4 Lighting per venue\n\n`game.lights.enabled = true` in every venue's enter: stadium day ambient .85 warm; stadium night .4 + stadium\nfloodlights + fireworks flashes; pool .8 cool + caustic glows; lawn .9; Iron Hall .35 + two warm spots; ski jump .35\n+ floodlights along the hill; ice palace .45 + moving colored spots; curling .6 warm; arena .4 + spots + goal light\nflash. E.Road scenes draw as overlays (unlit): bake the mood into their colors and add additive glow sprites.\n\n### 8.5 The mascot: YIKESY\n\nAn `E.Blob({ R: 9, ears: 'cat', feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#f8f8ff', dk: '#d8e2f0', lt: '#ffffff' } })`\n(a round snow-yeti) with a flame tuft on its head (fire particles + glow) and a half-orange/half-blue scarf drawn on\ntop. Appears on the title, in ceremonies, story beats, the attract mode, the curling scoreboard, as plush toys on the\nice, and in the Pose Lab. Voice: squeaky gibberish (pitch 1.9).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Audio (all in code)\n\n### 9.1 Music (engine songs `{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks }`, every one original)\n\n| Id | Where | Feel | BPM | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `title` | title, menus' first entry | heroic brass fanfare with a comic chromatic \"yikes\" slide, then triumph | 120 | motif below |\n| `menu` | main menu, setup screens | bright funk-pop loop | 112 | |\n| `parade` | opening ceremony | march, snare rolls | 116 | |\n| `sprint` | 100m | chiptune drum & bass | 172 | `hype` drum layer |\n| `javelin` | javelin | funky groove | 104 | |\n| `swim` | 50m free | bubbly arpeggios | 128 | |\n| `diving` | diving | sparse, timpani, suspense | 90 | |\n| `archery` | archery | tense minimal + heartbeat kick | 80 | heartbeat speeds with `hr` |\n| `iron` | weightlifting | heavy rock riff (saw bass) | 96 | |\n| `alpine` | ski jump | floodlit alpine pulse, bells | 124 | |\n| `yikesface` | downhill | driving rock | 150 | |\n| `icesurf` | bobsled | surf rock | 160 | |\n| `waltz` | figure skating | \"Waltz of the Yikes\", 3/4 (bars of 12 steps) | 138 | the rhythm chart's song |\n| `lounge` | curling | lounge jazz (swing feel) | 92 | |\n| `organ` | hockey | stadium organ + chant | 132 | goal horn sting |\n| `table` | results, medal table | proud, warm | 100 | |\n| `closing` | closing ceremony, credits | emotional anthem turning into a party | 96 → 128 | |\n| stings | WR, YIKES (descending trombone \"wah-wah-wah-waaah\"), laurel, qualify fail, games over, victory, goal horn | | | `audio.sting` |\n\nEvery event song names a `hype` track (`on: false`) faded in during turbo. Title motif (lead, one token a 16th, bars\nof 16): `G4 - - - C5 - - - E5 - - - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - B5 - A5 - G5 - - - | A5 - - - F5 - - - D5 - - - G5 - - - |\nE5 - - - D#5 - - - D5 - - - C#5 - - - | C5 - - - . . G4 - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - - - - - . . . .`\nover a bass `C3 C3 G2 G2 | A2 A2 E2 E2 | F2 F2 G2 G2 | C3 B2 Bb2 A2 | F2 G2 C3 - | C3 - - -` (quarters) and drums\n`k . . . s . . . k . k . s . . .` with a snare roll into the last bar. Keep the \"rise, comic slide, recover\" shape:\nit is the game's sonic logo.\n\n### 9.2 Sound effects (`audio.define`, layered voices; names → recipe)\n\n`gun` (noise burst 1800→200 Hz .12 s + sine 90→40 .3 s), `beep` (sine 880 .15), `step` (engine preset, pitched by\nspeed), `whoosh`, `thunk` (javelin into turf: noise lowpass + sine 140→60), `boing` (triangle 300→600→300 with vib),\n`twang` (pulse 220→180 with fast vibrato), `thwack` (noise 3000→800 .05 + sine 180), `clank` (square 800 + noise,\nmetallic `arp`), `slam` (bar drop: boom preset + rattle), `splash` (noise 2000→300 .5, size by vol), `slap` (belly\nflop: noise 4000→900 .08 + boom), `bubbles` (sine blips 600–1200), `swish` (ski carve: noise highpass 2–4 kHz),\n`crunch` (snow), `rumble` (sled: low noise loop by speed), `scrape` (noise 3–6 kHz + square 70), `clack` (stone:\nnoise 1500 .04 + square 400), `brush` (sweep: noise bursts), `puck` (click 2000 .03), `check` (boom + noise),\n`glass` (noise 5 kHz + triangle 1200 shimmer), `horn` (saw 220 + 277 + 330 1.2 s), `buzzer` (square 180 .8 s),\n`whistle` (from the sports kit), `cowbell` (square 560 + 840 decay), `camera` (click + highpass noise), `firework`\n(explode + crackle bits), `medal` (chime triangle C6–E6–G6), `cough` (noise formant), `alarm` (car alarm: square\n880↔660), `pop` (blimp: noise 3000→100), `yikes` sting. All go through the engine's sfx bus (volume settings apply).\n\n### 9.3 Voices: `O.Voice.speak(text, voice)` (Animalese/Simlish gibberish)\n\n- Split the line into syllables (`/[^aeiouy\\s]*[aeiouy]+[^aeiouy\\s]*|[.,!?]/gi`). For each syllable: vowel → formants\n  (a 730/1090, e 530/1840, i 270/2290, o 570/840, u 300/870, y 300/2000 Hz) scaled by the voice's `formant` (female\n  1.15, child/mascot 1.5); pitch `f0 = voice.base · 2^((hashOffset + contour)/12)` with `hashOffset` −3…+3 semitones\n  from a hash of the syllable (deterministic: never `Math.random`), contour rising on a question's last syllable,\n  falling on a period, +4 semitones and faster on \"!\". Duration `(.075 + .012·len) / voice.speed`, gap .02 s, pauses\n  .12 (comma) / .22 (period).\n- Source: an `OscillatorNode` (sawtooth for Chip, triangle for Vera, square for the PA, pulse for Max) with a little\n  vibrato and a −1 semitone fall at the end; consonant onsets add a 12 ms highpassed noise tick; two parallel band-pass\n  filters at F1 (Q 6) and F2 (Q 9); envelope 5 ms attack, 25 ms release; into the voice bus (engine change 6). The PA\n  adds a `DelayNode` echo (.18 s, feedback .3).\n- Returns the line's duration (subtitle timing, portrait mouth). Headless or before the first input: returns the\n  duration and makes no sound.\n- Voices: Chip (base 140 Hz, speed 1.15), Vera (210, .95), PA (120, .8, echo), Max (150, 1.25), each athlete per §7.1\n  (base 130 Hz × pitch), Yikesy (420, 1.4), crowd chant (6 detuned voices on \"O-LY-YI-KES!\").\n\n### 9.4 Crowd\n\n`O.CrowdAudio`: a looping noise source → band-pass (900 Hz, Q .7) → gain = `crowd volume × (.15 + .6·level)`, plus a\nlow murmur layer; events: cheer swell (level → 1, filter up), gasp (fast filter fall), \"OOOH\" (a cluster of 6 voices on\n\"oooh\"), applause (deterministic clap bursts), the chant, cowbells (winter outdoor), organ stabs (arena). Starts at the\nfirst user input (browsers' rule), ducks under the pause menu.\n\n### 9.5 Anthems\n\n`O.Anthem.song(nation)`: deterministic from the nation's seed: a major key (C, D, Eb, F, G or Bb), 8 bars of 4/4 at\n84–96 bpm, rhythm cells drawn from a small set (half + 2 quarters, dotted quarter + eighth + half, 4 quarters), melody\non chord tones on strong beats over I–IV–V–I–vi–IV–V–I, brass lead (saw), harmony (square, quiet), bass (triangle),\ntimpani (low sine `k`) on downbeats and a snare roll into bar 8. ≈ 20 s, played once at the medal ceremony (and a\n4-bar excerpt for \"THE FINAL\" tease). Two nations never share a melody (test).\n\n### 9.6 Mix\n\nDefaults: master .7 (engine), music .5, effects 1, voices .8, crowd .7. While a commentary line plays, music ducks\n×0.7. Pause ducks everything (engine). Sound on/off and every volume live in the engine's Settings → Sound.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Modes and flow\n\n### 10.1 The Games (the campaign)\n","numLines":150,"startLine":1234,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UJpsDUC74HtDmTLgGXXPej","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
