{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RENcTw2mFhbKLVuNXz4Gne","type":"tool_result","content":"1380\t## 10. Modes and flow\n1381\t\n1382\t### 10.1 The Games (the campaign)\n1383\t\n1384\t```\n1385\tmenu → gamesSetup → nations (join + pick) → opening\n1386\t  → for day 1..12: [beat before?] → dayCard → eventCard → ev:<id> → results → [initials]\n1387\t        → (failed qualifying? → torch → retry the event | 0 torches → gamesOver → continue? retry : title)\n1388\t        → podium → medals → [beat after?] → autosave\n1389\t  → closing → ending (+ party podium if several humans) → credits → title\n1390\t```\n1391\t- **Setup:** Length (Full 12 days / Quick 4 with its playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On by default for 1 player,\n1392\t  Off for several).\n1393\t- **Nations:** every human picks a different nation; CPU nations take the rest (8 total always compete).\n1394\t- **Day card + event card** always shown; the event card waits until every human pressed `confirm` (\"READY\" in their\n1395\t  color) or P1 presses Start.\n1396\t- **Autosave** after each day's medal table (`oly:games`); CONTINUE GAMES resumes at the next day card. Quitting to\n1397\t  the title (the engine asks first) keeps the autosave. Finishing the Games deletes it and fills the cabinet.\n1398\t- **Quick Games:** playlists *Track & Pool* (100m, Javelin, 50m Free, Diving), *Snow & Ice* (Ski Jump, Downhill,\n1399\t  Bobsled, Curling), *Greatest Hits* (100m, Ski Jump, Diving, Ice Hockey), *Random 4* (2 summer + 2 winter from a\n1400\t  stream). A short flame-lighting opening (no parade), rival reactions only, party podium at the end.\n1401\t\n1402\t### 10.2 Single Event\n1403\t\n1404\tsingle (event grid) → nations (join + pick) → eventCard (with **Practice** on △: no CPUs, unlimited attempts, no\n1405\trecords) → ev → results → [initials] → short podium → a menu: **Retry · Change event · Main menu**.\n1406\t\n1407\t### 10.3 Records, How to Play, Settings, About\n1408\t\n1409\t- **Records:** one tab per event (top-5 table with initials, nation flag, date-free), **Laurels** (12 tiles with hints),\n1410\t  **Cabinet** (nation × event best medal icons). ←/→ or L1/R1 switch tabs.\n1411\t- **How to Play:** *Basics* (4 pages: mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) then the 12 event cards.\n1412\t- **Settings:** `game.menu('settings')` (engine HTML, scaled), with the Game group of §2.5.\n1413\t- **About & Credits** (paged, 10-foot): (1) **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists), (2) **Testing\n1414\t  Feedback**, (3) **Engine Feedback**, (4) **Prompt Feedback** (the answers to TASK.md's questions, the same text as\n1415\t  the chat reply and `exit-interview.json`), (5) **Credits** (planned and built by which models, engine and version,\n1416\t  AI Hub client version, the engine changes of §4.6, asset sets used with their CC0 sources), (6) **Controls** (the\n1417\t  action map with glyphs for the current device).\n1418\t\n1419\t---\n1420\t\n1421\t## 11. Attract mode\n1422\t\n1423\t- **Trigger:** 10 s without input on the title or any main-menu screen (title, menu, single, records, howto, about,\n1424\t  gamesSetup, nations before anyone joined). \"Input\" = any key, mouse button, wheel, mouse movement > 4 px, gamepad\n1425\t  button or stick past the dead zone, touch. Tracked per step in the scene wrapper (`E.HOOKS.input` catches presses\n1426\t  while menus are open).\n1427\t- **Playlist** (a director scene; every segment loads the real event scene with `meet.mode = 'attract'`):\n1428\t  `LOGO (4 s) → EVENT → RECORDS TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → MEDAL TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → LAUREL / TIP CARD (5 s) → EVENT → loop`,\n1429\t  events rotating through all 12 across loops: sprint, skijump, diving, downhill, curling, figure, hockey, javelin,\n1430\t  swim, archery, weights, bobsled. Each event has `attract.setup(ctx)` that starts at its showcase moment: the sprint\n1431\t  from SET, the ski jump from the gate with rocket skis, the YIKES quintuple dive, the downhill from the Yikes Face\n1432\t  jump, a curling end set up for a double takeout, figure skating from Jump Combo 2, 25 s of 2-on-2 hockey ending in an\n1433\t  ON FIRE goal, the out-of-the-stadium javelin, a perfect flip turn, a Robin Hood arrow, the YIKES BAR lift, the\n1434\t  Labyrinth on the bobsled. Segment length = `attract.seconds` (15–25 s).\n1435\t- **Cheating is allowed:** every athlete is a bot; the featured one uses `cheat: 'perfect'` (frame-perfect inputs,\n1436\t  infinite hype). Each loop also shows one scripted wipeout by a non-featured athlete, so the demo shows what can go\n1437\t  wrong.\n1438\t- **Overlay:** \"DEMO\" badge, the small logo, \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" with the glyph of the last device (touch-only: the\n1439\t  \"Controller or keyboard required\" line instead), commentary subtitles on.\n1440\t- **Exit:** any input → title (the input is consumed so it doesn't also press anything there). Attract never writes\n1441\t  records, laurels, saves or ghosts.\n1442\t\n1443\t---\n1444\t\n1445\t## 12. Multiplayer\n1446\t\n1447\t### 12.1 Local (the game on its own)\n1448\t\n1449\t- Players join on the Nations screen (and in Single Event) with `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`: Start/✕ on a\n1450\t  free gamepad, or **2** on the keyboard (the halves split); ○/Esc leaves before the event starts\n1451\t  (`game.removePlayer`). Each player's color is `E.PLAYER_COLORS[i]` and tag P1–P4.\n1452\t- Formats: races put humans in middle lanes, simultaneously (one shared camera framing the humans); attempts/programs\n1453\t  take turns with a **turn card** (\"P2 — YOUR TURN\") and the previous player's attempt as a ghost; matches offer\n1454\t  **Versus** (P1 vs P2, or 2v2 in hockey) or **Co-op** (humans on one team; curling co-op = one throws, one sweeps).\n1455\t- Every prompt, pause (\"P2 PAUSED\") and Controls page is per player (engine).\n1456\t\n1457\t### 12.2 AI Hub sessions: \"Hub Heats\" in **ghost** mode\n1458\t\n1459\tWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded heat of the same three events at the same moments on the hub's clock, and\n1460\tshows the other players as ghosts in neighbouring lanes, so it plays like a real head-to-head final with no\n1461\thost-authoritative sync.\n1462\t\n1463\t- **Tags** (§4.9): `hub:session 1`, `hub:session-players 1-4`, `hub:session-mode ghost`, `hub:session-minutes 4`,\n1464\t  goal and how-to. The client `vendor/hub/session.js` is pasted unmodified as the first script in `<head>`.\n1465\t- **Detect:** `AIHub.active` (true from the first line). Then the game **never shows the title, attract or menus**.\n1466\t  A boot step awaits `AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`; if it resolves `null`, boot the\n1467\t  normal game.\n1468\t- **The deal:** three events from `AIHub.rng('deal')`, one per group: A {sprint, swim}, B {javelin, archery, weights,\n1469\t  diving, skijump}, C {downhill, bobsled}; order A, B, C. Nations by seat from `AIHub.rng('nations')` (a permutation);\n1470\t  names and colors come from `info.players` (seat colors `#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`) and are drawn with the\n1471\t  pixel font, never inserted as HTML. No CPU athletes in hub heats; a translucent \"WR pace\" marker gives a target.\n1472\t- **Our own card** (`card: true`, scene `hubCard`): the venue of event 1 as backdrop, the three dealt events with\n1473\t  pictograms, the players lined up in seat colors with a READY tick each (from `card` events), \"Most points over three\n1474\t  events wins\", this player's controls (keyboard and controller columns with glyph icons), the countdown from\n1475\t  `card.left`. **Enter/✕/tap on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3), the T key or a tap on MORE TIME →\n1476\t  `AIHub.answer('more')`** (again takes it back). No menus, settings or choices on the card. **No `Math.random`\n1477\t  consumers on the card:** with engine change 2 the rigs and particles no longer call `Math.random`, so the card may\n1478\t  animate them; any randomness of the card's own comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n1479\t- **Ready:** call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as boot has built the first venue, with no key press.\n1480\t- **Start:** on `start`, show a big 3-2-1 synced to `AIHub.time()` (negative during the countdown); play begins at\n1481\t  `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n1482\t- **Slots on the hub clock:** event *i* runs in a fixed slot (`hub.seconds` per event: sprint 35, swim 45, javelin 45,\n1483\t  archery 50, weights 50, diving 45, skijump 40, downhill 70, bobsled 60). Each slot: 5 s \"GET READY\" (the event card\n1484\t  as an overlay + countdown), the heat (hub variant: attempts as in §6), then a 4 s results splash; finishing early\n1485\t  means watching the ghosts until the slot ends; reaching the slot's end unfinished finalizes the attempt (DNF scores 0\n1486\t  for that event). Everyone moves to the next event together. If the tab was hidden past a slot, finalize it and\n1487\t  jump to the current slot.\n1488\t- **Ghost traffic:** ~10 messages/s, unreliable: `{ t: 'g', e: eventId, i: slot, a: attempt, s: [x, y, z, facing,\n1489\t  poseCode, extra] }` (≈ 60–90 bytes); reliable on each attempt and event result: `{ t: 'r', e, i, perf, pts, total }`.\n1490\t  Ghosts render as translucent athletes tinted in their seat color with their hub name: other lanes in races (lanes\n1491\t  assigned by seat around yours), alongside jumpers/divers/javelins (offset slightly in depth), colored hit marks on\n1492\t  the archery target, extra platforms for weights, road \"cars\" in downhill/bobsled. Ghosts never affect your world.\n1493\t  `leave` removes that ghost.\n1494\t- **Scoring:** points per event (§6 formulas); `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: '100m · 9.87 s · 1,032 pts' })`\n1495\t  whenever points change and about once a second; after the third event: **`AIHub.result({ score: total, stats:\n1496\t  { '100m': '9.87 s', ... }, awards: [{ title: 'WORLD RECORD', detail: '100m · 9.41 s' }] })` exactly once**.\n1497\t- **`time-up`:** if no result was sent, send `AIHub.result({ score: total })` at once and freeze input (\"TIME!\").\n1498\t- **`end`:** stop taking input (all players' `input.clear()` and a flag the scene wrapper checks), `audio.music(null)`,\n1499\t  silence voices/crowd, show \"ROUND OVER\" over the venue; send nothing afterwards.\n1500\t- **Rules:** no network but the hub, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no new windows, no navigation; the pause menu has no\n1501\t  Quit, Restart or Dev mode (§4.4); Options is ignored while Create (pad button 8) is held (§2.1); storage is the\n1502\t  client's empty one (nothing to do); fullscreen requests go through the client automatically.\n1503\t\n1504\t---\n1505\t\n1506\t## 13. Dev mode (pause menu → \"Dev mode\"; the ` key also opens it; absent in hub sessions)\n1507\t\n1508\t- **Opening** closes the engine's pause menu (`game.resume()`) and sets `game.timeScale = 0` (the scene keeps updating with dt 0, so the\n1509\t  scene wrapper can run the panel); closing restores the previous time scale. **LIVE** (a toggle on the panel) lets\n1510\t  the game run at the dev speed while the panel stays open; then the panel suppresses the game's actions each step\n1511\t  (`input.suppress`), so only bots and the autopilot play.\n1512\t- **Panel:** pixel art, right 45% of the screen, 10-foot sized, tabs **TUNE · GLOBAL · CHEATS · JUMP · VIEW · DATA**\n1513\t  (L1/R1, Q/E or click). ↑/↓ choose a row, ←/→ change it (held: accelerates after .5 s), Shift/R2 = fine steps, ✕\n1514\t  resets the row, △ resets the whole tab to defaults, ○/Esc closes. Mouse: hover focuses, drag a slider, wheel nudges.\n1515\t- **TUNE:** the current event's tunables (≥ 6, listed in §6) as live sliders with their default marked; changed\n1516\t  values in gold with a count; **RESET TO DEFAULTS**; **COPY JSON** (clipboard + console) of changed values;\n1517\t  **KEEP AFTER RELOAD** (stores `oly:tune`, off by default).\n1518\t- **GLOBAL:** the global tunables (§5.13), same controls and reset.\n1519\t- **CHEATS:** Autopilot P1 (the AutoPlayer), Perfect P1, God mode (no wipeouts, fouls, DQs for humans), Infinite hype,\n1520\t  WIN NOW (gold), LOSE NOW (8th), DNF NOW, SKIP TO PHASE (each event lists its phases: e.g. ski jump: gate / take-off /\n1521\t  flight / landing; downhill: section 1–8; hockey: period 2 / overtime / shootout), NEXT ATTEMPT, UNLOCK ALL LAURELS,\n1522\t  TORCHES +3, GIVE MEDAL (gold/silver/bronze to your nation).\n1523\t- **JUMP:** any event (Single Event, P1 SUN vs CPU), any Games day (earlier days simulated), opening ceremony, closing\n1524\t  ceremony + ending (choose rank), podium and medal table with sample data, any story beat, attract, Pose Lab, the hub\n1525\t  card with a local stub hub and three fake ghosts (to see ghost rendering offline).\n1526\t- **VIEW:** rig skeletons (`rig.debug`), physics bodies (`world.draw`), radii/hitboxes, input display (each player's\n1527\t  `input.history` as glyph icons), FPS (the engine setting), state JSON (`game.debug.snapshot()`, paged), time scale\n1528\t  0.1×–4× and FRAME STEP (✕ advances one fixed step while frozen), free camera (`cam.free`) and zoom, HUD on/off,\n1529\t  lights on/off, photo mode (all UI hidden).\n1530\t- **DATA:** meet seed (view/set), reset records, reset laurels, clear the Games save, clear ghosts, sound test (any song,\n1531\t  sting, sfx, voice line), commentary test (cue any key).\n1532\t- `O.Dev.set(group, key, v)`, `O.Dev.cheat(name)`, `O.Dev.jump(target)` are the same actions for tests.\n1533\t\n1534\t---\n1535\t\n1536\t## 14. Build order and milestones\n1537\t\n1538\tBuild the spine and one complete event first, de-risk the hard techniques with spikes, then fill in events by reuse.\n1539\tEach milestone ends with `node tests/run.mjs` green and a short screenshot review."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"ae2171cb-e438-433e-a81f-6c471a8c3969","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:17.630Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 10. Modes and flow\n\n### 10.1 The Games (the campaign)\n\n```\nmenu → gamesSetup → nations (join + pick) → opening\n  → for day 1..12: [beat before?] → dayCard → eventCard → ev:<id> → results → [initials]\n        → (failed qualifying? → torch → retry the event | 0 torches → gamesOver → continue? retry : title)\n        → podium → medals → [beat after?] → autosave\n  → closing → ending (+ party podium if several humans) → credits → title\n```\n- **Setup:** Length (Full 12 days / Quick 4 with its playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On by default for 1 player,\n  Off for several).\n- **Nations:** every human picks a different nation; CPU nations take the rest (8 total always compete).\n- **Day card + event card** always shown; the event card waits until every human pressed `confirm` (\"READY\" in their\n  color) or P1 presses Start.\n- **Autosave** after each day's medal table (`oly:games`); CONTINUE GAMES resumes at the next day card. Quitting to\n  the title (the engine asks first) keeps the autosave. Finishing the Games deletes it and fills the cabinet.\n- **Quick Games:** playlists *Track & Pool* (100m, Javelin, 50m Free, Diving), *Snow & Ice* (Ski Jump, Downhill,\n  Bobsled, Curling), *Greatest Hits* (100m, Ski Jump, Diving, Ice Hockey), *Random 4* (2 summer + 2 winter from a\n  stream). A short flame-lighting opening (no parade), rival reactions only, party podium at the end.\n\n### 10.2 Single Event\n\nsingle (event grid) → nations (join + pick) → eventCard (with **Practice** on △: no CPUs, unlimited attempts, no\nrecords) → ev → results → [initials] → short podium → a menu: **Retry · Change event · Main menu**.\n\n### 10.3 Records, How to Play, Settings, About\n\n- **Records:** one tab per event (top-5 table with initials, nation flag, date-free), **Laurels** (12 tiles with hints),\n  **Cabinet** (nation × event best medal icons). ←/→ or L1/R1 switch tabs.\n- **How to Play:** *Basics* (4 pages: mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) then the 12 event cards.\n- **Settings:** `game.menu('settings')` (engine HTML, scaled), with the Game group of §2.5.\n- **About & Credits** (paged, 10-foot): (1) **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists), (2) **Testing\n  Feedback**, (3) **Engine Feedback**, (4) **Prompt Feedback** (the answers to TASK.md's questions, the same text as\n  the chat reply and `exit-interview.json`), (5) **Credits** (planned and built by which models, engine and version,\n  AI Hub client version, the engine changes of §4.6, asset sets used with their CC0 sources), (6) **Controls** (the\n  action map with glyphs for the current device).\n\n---\n\n## 11. Attract mode\n\n- **Trigger:** 10 s without input on the title or any main-menu screen (title, menu, single, records, howto, about,\n  gamesSetup, nations before anyone joined). \"Input\" = any key, mouse button, wheel, mouse movement > 4 px, gamepad\n  button or stick past the dead zone, touch. Tracked per step in the scene wrapper (`E.HOOKS.input` catches presses\n  while menus are open).\n- **Playlist** (a director scene; every segment loads the real event scene with `meet.mode = 'attract'`):\n  `LOGO (4 s) → EVENT → RECORDS TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → MEDAL TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → LAUREL / TIP CARD (5 s) → EVENT → loop`,\n  events rotating through all 12 across loops: sprint, skijump, diving, downhill, curling, figure, hockey, javelin,\n  swim, archery, weights, bobsled. Each event has `attract.setup(ctx)` that starts at its showcase moment: the sprint\n  from SET, the ski jump from the gate with rocket skis, the YIKES quintuple dive, the downhill from the Yikes Face\n  jump, a curling end set up for a double takeout, figure skating from Jump Combo 2, 25 s of 2-on-2 hockey ending in an\n  ON FIRE goal, the out-of-the-stadium javelin, a perfect flip turn, a Robin Hood arrow, the YIKES BAR lift, the\n  Labyrinth on the bobsled. Segment length = `attract.seconds` (15–25 s).\n- **Cheating is allowed:** every athlete is a bot; the featured one uses `cheat: 'perfect'` (frame-perfect inputs,\n  infinite hype). Each loop also shows one scripted wipeout by a non-featured athlete, so the demo shows what can go\n  wrong.\n- **Overlay:** \"DEMO\" badge, the small logo, \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" with the glyph of the last device (touch-only: the\n  \"Controller or keyboard required\" line instead), commentary subtitles on.\n- **Exit:** any input → title (the input is consumed so it doesn't also press anything there). Attract never writes\n  records, laurels, saves or ghosts.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Multiplayer\n\n### 12.1 Local (the game on its own)\n\n- Players join on the Nations screen (and in Single Event) with `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`: Start/✕ on a\n  free gamepad, or **2** on the keyboard (the halves split); ○/Esc leaves before the event starts\n  (`game.removePlayer`). Each player's color is `E.PLAYER_COLORS[i]` and tag P1–P4.\n- Formats: races put humans in middle lanes, simultaneously (one shared camera framing the humans); attempts/programs\n  take turns with a **turn card** (\"P2 — YOUR TURN\") and the previous player's attempt as a ghost; matches offer\n  **Versus** (P1 vs P2, or 2v2 in hockey) or **Co-op** (humans on one team; curling co-op = one throws, one sweeps).\n- Every prompt, pause (\"P2 PAUSED\") and Controls page is per player (engine).\n\n### 12.2 AI Hub sessions: \"Hub Heats\" in **ghost** mode\n\nWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded heat of the same three events at the same moments on the hub's clock, and\nshows the other players as ghosts in neighbouring lanes, so it plays like a real head-to-head final with no\nhost-authoritative sync.\n\n- **Tags** (§4.9): `hub:session 1`, `hub:session-players 1-4`, `hub:session-mode ghost`, `hub:session-minutes 4`,\n  goal and how-to. The client `vendor/hub/session.js` is pasted unmodified as the first script in `<head>`.\n- **Detect:** `AIHub.active` (true from the first line). Then the game **never shows the title, attract or menus**.\n  A boot step awaits `AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`; if it resolves `null`, boot the\n  normal game.\n- **The deal:** three events from `AIHub.rng('deal')`, one per group: A {sprint, swim}, B {javelin, archery, weights,\n  diving, skijump}, C {downhill, bobsled}; order A, B, C. Nations by seat from `AIHub.rng('nations')` (a permutation);\n  names and colors come from `info.players` (seat colors `#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`) and are drawn with the\n  pixel font, never inserted as HTML. No CPU athletes in hub heats; a translucent \"WR pace\" marker gives a target.\n- **Our own card** (`card: true`, scene `hubCard`): the venue of event 1 as backdrop, the three dealt events with\n  pictograms, the players lined up in seat colors with a READY tick each (from `card` events), \"Most points over three\n  events wins\", this player's controls (keyboard and controller columns with glyph icons), the countdown from\n  `card.left`. **Enter/✕/tap on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3), the T key or a tap on MORE TIME →\n  `AIHub.answer('more')`** (again takes it back). No menus, settings or choices on the card. **No `Math.random`\n  consumers on the card:** with engine change 2 the rigs and particles no longer call `Math.random`, so the card may\n  animate them; any randomness of the card's own comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n- **Ready:** call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as boot has built the first venue, with no key press.\n- **Start:** on `start`, show a big 3-2-1 synced to `AIHub.time()` (negative during the countdown); play begins at\n  `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n- **Slots on the hub clock:** event *i* runs in a fixed slot (`hub.seconds` per event: sprint 35, swim 45, javelin 45,\n  archery 50, weights 50, diving 45, skijump 40, downhill 70, bobsled 60). Each slot: 5 s \"GET READY\" (the event card\n  as an overlay + countdown), the heat (hub variant: attempts as in §6), then a 4 s results splash; finishing early\n  means watching the ghosts until the slot ends; reaching the slot's end unfinished finalizes the attempt (DNF scores 0\n  for that event). Everyone moves to the next event together. If the tab was hidden past a slot, finalize it and\n  jump to the current slot.\n- **Ghost traffic:** ~10 messages/s, unreliable: `{ t: 'g', e: eventId, i: slot, a: attempt, s: [x, y, z, facing,\n  poseCode, extra] }` (≈ 60–90 bytes); reliable on each attempt and event result: `{ t: 'r', e, i, perf, pts, total }`.\n  Ghosts render as translucent athletes tinted in their seat color with their hub name: other lanes in races (lanes\n  assigned by seat around yours), alongside jumpers/divers/javelins (offset slightly in depth), colored hit marks on\n  the archery target, extra platforms for weights, road \"cars\" in downhill/bobsled. Ghosts never affect your world.\n  `leave` removes that ghost.\n- **Scoring:** points per event (§6 formulas); `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: '100m · 9.87 s · 1,032 pts' })`\n  whenever points change and about once a second; after the third event: **`AIHub.result({ score: total, stats:\n  { '100m': '9.87 s', ... }, awards: [{ title: 'WORLD RECORD', detail: '100m · 9.41 s' }] })` exactly once**.\n- **`time-up`:** if no result was sent, send `AIHub.result({ score: total })` at once and freeze input (\"TIME!\").\n- **`end`:** stop taking input (all players' `input.clear()` and a flag the scene wrapper checks), `audio.music(null)`,\n  silence voices/crowd, show \"ROUND OVER\" over the venue; send nothing afterwards.\n- **Rules:** no network but the hub, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no new windows, no navigation; the pause menu has no\n  Quit, Restart or Dev mode (§4.4); Options is ignored while Create (pad button 8) is held (§2.1); storage is the\n  client's empty one (nothing to do); fullscreen requests go through the client automatically.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Dev mode (pause menu → \"Dev mode\"; the ` key also opens it; absent in hub sessions)\n\n- **Opening** closes the engine's pause menu (`game.resume()`) and sets `game.timeScale = 0` (the scene keeps updating with dt 0, so the\n  scene wrapper can run the panel); closing restores the previous time scale. **LIVE** (a toggle on the panel) lets\n  the game run at the dev speed while the panel stays open; then the panel suppresses the game's actions each step\n  (`input.suppress`), so only bots and the autopilot play.\n- **Panel:** pixel art, right 45% of the screen, 10-foot sized, tabs **TUNE · GLOBAL · CHEATS · JUMP · VIEW · DATA**\n  (L1/R1, Q/E or click). ↑/↓ choose a row, ←/→ change it (held: accelerates after .5 s), Shift/R2 = fine steps, ✕\n  resets the row, △ resets the whole tab to defaults, ○/Esc closes. Mouse: hover focuses, drag a slider, wheel nudges.\n- **TUNE:** the current event's tunables (≥ 6, listed in §6) as live sliders with their default marked; changed\n  values in gold with a count; **RESET TO DEFAULTS**; **COPY JSON** (clipboard + console) of changed values;\n  **KEEP AFTER RELOAD** (stores `oly:tune`, off by default).\n- **GLOBAL:** the global tunables (§5.13), same controls and reset.\n- **CHEATS:** Autopilot P1 (the AutoPlayer), Perfect P1, God mode (no wipeouts, fouls, DQs for humans), Infinite hype,\n  WIN NOW (gold), LOSE NOW (8th), DNF NOW, SKIP TO PHASE (each event lists its phases: e.g. ski jump: gate / take-off /\n  flight / landing; downhill: section 1–8; hockey: period 2 / overtime / shootout), NEXT ATTEMPT, UNLOCK ALL LAURELS,\n  TORCHES +3, GIVE MEDAL (gold/silver/bronze to your nation).\n- **JUMP:** any event (Single Event, P1 SUN vs CPU), any Games day (earlier days simulated), opening ceremony, closing\n  ceremony + ending (choose rank), podium and medal table with sample data, any story beat, attract, Pose Lab, the hub\n  card with a local stub hub and three fake ghosts (to see ghost rendering offline).\n- **VIEW:** rig skeletons (`rig.debug`), physics bodies (`world.draw`), radii/hitboxes, input display (each player's\n  `input.history` as glyph icons), FPS (the engine setting), state JSON (`game.debug.snapshot()`, paged), time scale\n  0.1×–4× and FRAME STEP (✕ advances one fixed step while frozen), free camera (`cam.free`) and zoom, HUD on/off,\n  lights on/off, photo mode (all UI hidden).\n- **DATA:** meet seed (view/set), reset records, reset laurels, clear the Games save, clear ghosts, sound test (any song,\n  sting, sfx, voice line), commentary test (cue any key).\n- `O.Dev.set(group, key, v)`, `O.Dev.cheat(name)`, `O.Dev.jump(target)` are the same actions for tests.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Build order and milestones\n\nBuild the spine and one complete event first, de-risk the hard techniques with spikes, then fill in events by reuse.\nEach milestone ends with `node tests/run.mjs` green and a short screenshot review.","numLines":160,"startLine":1380,"totalLines":1720}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RENcTw2mFhbKLVuNXz4Gne","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
