{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HaPxTfboc3HEn4FFkvgQsX","type":"tool_result","content":"1540\t\n1541\tBuild the spine and one complete event first, de-risk the hard techniques with spikes, then fill in events by reuse.\n1542\tEach milestone ends with `node tests/run.mjs` green and a short screenshot review.\n1543\t\n1544\t| M | Scope | Exit criteria |\n1545\t|---|---|---|\n1546\t| **M0 Setup** | §0.1 fetch; folder; `index.html`; `tests/run.mjs` + harness; `tools/bundle.mjs`; engine changes 1–4 | headless boot to a blank `title`; bundle opens via `tools/check.mjs` with no errors; tests print one line |\n1547\t| **M1 Spine** | 00–12 core files: game object, `OLY_KEYS`, pilots, `Mash` and timing widgets, `O.Prompt`, 10-foot widgets, tuning registry, streams, nations + rig factory (basic outfits), scene wrapper, `O.flow` (title → menu → single → event card → event → results → back), EventKit with formats, results/records/points, hype/turbo, yikes, comms (text first), crowd (visual), store | the 100m sim runs headless with 8 bots, deterministic twice, results and records correct; menus navigable by keys, pad codes and mouse in tests; prompts resolve to icons for every device |\n1548\t| **M2 Reference event + presentation** | 100m complete (stadium art, crowd, jumbotron, lights, music, sfx, `O.Voice`, crowd audio, commentary with portraits, HUD with glyphs, photo finish, false starts, faceplant, turbo, laurel); podium + anthem generator; medal table; dev panel v1 (TUNE/GLOBAL/CHEATS/JUMP); attract v1 (title → sprint demo → records → loop); touch-only notice; 10-foot CSS for the engine's HTML screens | all 100m targets (§6.1) pass; screenshots of title, stadium, HUD, podium, dev panel at 1920×1080 read well |\n1549\t| **M3 Risk spikes** (before more events; independent of M2) | (a) Pose layer + engine change 5: swim crawl, tuck/pike rotation, V-flight, telemark, jerk in the Pose Lab + filmstrips; (b) rear-view skier and gates on `E.Road`; (c) hub: a minimal ghost round with the sprint in the real harness via Playwright; (d) bundle from `file://` at full size; (e) curling ice model calibration (draw/takeout distances); (f) `E.Rhythm` 5-lane chart with the waltz + skater path | each spike has a passing test or an approved filmstrip; findings folded into §6 numbers |\n1550\t| **M4 Summer events** | Javelin (reuses the stadium), 50m Free, Diving, Archery, Weightlifting | each meets the event Definition of Done (below) |\n1551\t| **M5 Winter events** | Ski Jump, Downhill, Bobsled (reuses Downhill), Figure Skating, Curling, Ice Hockey (from the sports kit) | each meets the event Definition of Done |\n1552\t| **M6 The Games** | setup, nations + join, opening ceremony, day cards, all story beats, qualifying/torches/continue, halftime report, closing ceremony, endings, credits, autosave/continue, Quick Games, party points; local multiplayer in every format | the scripted playthrough (§16.3) passes for 1 player and for 2 players |\n1553\t| **M7 Front end** | attract (full playlist), Records/Laurels/Cabinet, How to Play, all Game settings, About & Credits pages | attract test passes; every menu screen reachable by keys, pad and mouse in tests |\n1554\t| **M8 AI Hub** | §12.2 complete: tags, card, deal, slots, ghosts for the 9 hub events, progress/result/time-up/end/leave, Create+Options | headless hub-stub suite passes; real harness: 2 players auto, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, host-leave → `__hubCheck.pass === true` |\n1555\t| **M9 Balance and polish** | bot statistics per event and difficulty, commentary density, audio mix, visual passes per venue, crowd, effects | every event's targets (§6) hold; screenshot review of all venues; no runtime warnings in `check.mjs` |\n1556\t| **M10 Ship** | final bundle, full test run, final screenshots, About & Credits filled with real Source Information and feedback, `exit-interview.json` (valid JSON, every field), the chat reply | §17 checklist all ticked |\n1557\t\n1558\t**Event Definition of Done:** playable start to finish by keyboard, pad (and mouse where §2.2 says), and by bots;\n1559\tCPU rivals; HUD with glyph prompts and the event card; ≥ 6 tunables; turbo; every listed yikes; laurel; ≥ 8\n1560\tcommentary lines; its music and sfx; records, qualifying and points; multiplayer as specified; hub variant where\n1561\tlisted; attract segment; headless tests (determinism, bot completes, skill monotonic, every mechanic check of §6);\n1562\ta screenshot reviewed.\n1563\t\n1564\t---\n1565\t\n1566\t## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1567\t\n1568\t| Risk | Impact | Mitigation | Early signal |\n1569\t|---|---|---|---|\n1570\t| Scope: 12 events + ceremonies + hub | an unfinished game | one event contract and widgets; reference event first; reuse kits (sports → hockey, road → downhill + bobsled, rhythm → figure, physics/pinball → curling); events written in order of reuse; nothing beyond this plan | milestone burn-down; DoD per event |\n1571\t| Custom athlete animation looks broken | cheap look, unreadable actions | built-in rig vocabulary first; `O.Pose` + Pose Lab + filmstrips in M3; equipment carries readability (a javelin, a barbell, skis say what the pose is) | M3 filmstrips |\n1572\t| Rigs from behind on `E.Road` | downhill/bobsled unconvincing | M3 spike with a custom rear `E.View`; fallback: skier and sled drawn as code-drawn sprites with 8 lean frames | spike screenshot |\n1573\t| Hub protocol failures | the game is kept out of sessions | M3 spike against the real harness; follow §12.2 literally; test every scenario | harness pass |\n1574\t| Cosmetic `Math.random` use (rigs, particles) | hub card rule broken; flaky tests | engine change 2; gameplay only via `O.rng` streams; proofs run twice | determinism tests; `Math.random` call-count check on the card |\n1575\t| Input conflicts (J/K/Space/○ in menus vs play) | skipped screens, accidental cancels | custom preset without J/K in confirm/cancel; lockouts; `consumeAll` on enter; hold-to-skip cinematics | input tests |\n1576\t| Missing ✕○□△ in the pixel font | `?` in prompts | `O.Prompt` icons + font glyphs (engine change 3) | prompt test for every action × device × glyph style |\n1577\t| Engine HTML menus too small on a TV | 10-foot failure | CSS override; 1920×1080 screenshot | screenshot |\n1578\t| Unbalanced events | boring or unfair | points tables; bot calibration tests per skill; dev sliders; difficulty presets | bot statistics test |\n1579\t| Slow headless tests | tests skipped | sims are draw-free; `--quick`; the full playthrough uses perfect bots | test time printed |\n1580\t| Bundle breakage (`</script>`, order, size) | a broken deliverable | bundler escapes; a bundle test in Chromium from `file://` | bundle test |\n1581\t| Voices grating | players mute everything | cooldowns, priorities, voices volume, subtitles-only | a listening pass with the dev sound test |\n1582\t| Touch-only misdetection on touch laptops | locked-out players | coarse && no fine pointer && no key/pad seen; any key or pad unlocks | touch emulation test |\n1583\t| Curling CPU cost (108 sims) | hitches | 12 candidates per frame, early exits | per-frame timing test |\n1584\t\n1585\t---\n1586\t\n1587\t## 16. Testing\n1588\t\n1589\t### 16.1 The one command\n1590\t\n1591\t`node tests/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) runs every suite: headless Node suites first, then the browser suites\n1592\t(Playwright). It prints **only failures** (suite, check, a one-line detail) and then **one line**:\n1593\t`olympiyikes: 512 checks, 0 failed (headless 41 s, browser 63 s)`; exit code 1 on any failure. `--quick` runs only the\n1594\theadless suites; `--only <suite>` runs one. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. The browser suites\n1595\tload Playwright from the handoff's install (`createRequire(<dev>/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/package.json)('playwright')`),\n1596\tso there is one `npm install` for everything.\n1597\t\n1598\t### 16.2 The harness (`tests/harness.mjs`)\n1599\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2086767-996d-4677-894d-e4b97c87d2db","uuid":"5c5e3a59-0471-4254-a3cd-edcc50444ec1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:44.884Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/work/PLAN.md","content":"\nBuild the spine and one complete event first, de-risk the hard techniques with spikes, then fill in events by reuse.\nEach milestone ends with `node tests/run.mjs` green and a short screenshot review.\n\n| M | Scope | Exit criteria |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0 Setup** | §0.1 fetch; folder; `index.html`; `tests/run.mjs` + harness; `tools/bundle.mjs`; engine changes 1–4 | headless boot to a blank `title`; bundle opens via `tools/check.mjs` with no errors; tests print one line |\n| **M1 Spine** | 00–12 core files: game object, `OLY_KEYS`, pilots, `Mash` and timing widgets, `O.Prompt`, 10-foot widgets, tuning registry, streams, nations + rig factory (basic outfits), scene wrapper, `O.flow` (title → menu → single → event card → event → results → back), EventKit with formats, results/records/points, hype/turbo, yikes, comms (text first), crowd (visual), store | the 100m sim runs headless with 8 bots, deterministic twice, results and records correct; menus navigable by keys, pad codes and mouse in tests; prompts resolve to icons for every device |\n| **M2 Reference event + presentation** | 100m complete (stadium art, crowd, jumbotron, lights, music, sfx, `O.Voice`, crowd audio, commentary with portraits, HUD with glyphs, photo finish, false starts, faceplant, turbo, laurel); podium + anthem generator; medal table; dev panel v1 (TUNE/GLOBAL/CHEATS/JUMP); attract v1 (title → sprint demo → records → loop); touch-only notice; 10-foot CSS for the engine's HTML screens | all 100m targets (§6.1) pass; screenshots of title, stadium, HUD, podium, dev panel at 1920×1080 read well |\n| **M3 Risk spikes** (before more events; independent of M2) | (a) Pose layer + engine change 5: swim crawl, tuck/pike rotation, V-flight, telemark, jerk in the Pose Lab + filmstrips; (b) rear-view skier and gates on `E.Road`; (c) hub: a minimal ghost round with the sprint in the real harness via Playwright; (d) bundle from `file://` at full size; (e) curling ice model calibration (draw/takeout distances); (f) `E.Rhythm` 5-lane chart with the waltz + skater path | each spike has a passing test or an approved filmstrip; findings folded into §6 numbers |\n| **M4 Summer events** | Javelin (reuses the stadium), 50m Free, Diving, Archery, Weightlifting | each meets the event Definition of Done (below) |\n| **M5 Winter events** | Ski Jump, Downhill, Bobsled (reuses Downhill), Figure Skating, Curling, Ice Hockey (from the sports kit) | each meets the event Definition of Done |\n| **M6 The Games** | setup, nations + join, opening ceremony, day cards, all story beats, qualifying/torches/continue, halftime report, closing ceremony, endings, credits, autosave/continue, Quick Games, party points; local multiplayer in every format | the scripted playthrough (§16.3) passes for 1 player and for 2 players |\n| **M7 Front end** | attract (full playlist), Records/Laurels/Cabinet, How to Play, all Game settings, About & Credits pages | attract test passes; every menu screen reachable by keys, pad and mouse in tests |\n| **M8 AI Hub** | §12.2 complete: tags, card, deal, slots, ghosts for the 9 hub events, progress/result/time-up/end/leave, Create+Options | headless hub-stub suite passes; real harness: 2 players auto, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, host-leave → `__hubCheck.pass === true` |\n| **M9 Balance and polish** | bot statistics per event and difficulty, commentary density, audio mix, visual passes per venue, crowd, effects | every event's targets (§6) hold; screenshot review of all venues; no runtime warnings in `check.mjs` |\n| **M10 Ship** | final bundle, full test run, final screenshots, About & Credits filled with real Source Information and feedback, `exit-interview.json` (valid JSON, every field), the chat reply | §17 checklist all ticked |\n\n**Event Definition of Done:** playable start to finish by keyboard, pad (and mouse where §2.2 says), and by bots;\nCPU rivals; HUD with glyph prompts and the event card; ≥ 6 tunables; turbo; every listed yikes; laurel; ≥ 8\ncommentary lines; its music and sfx; records, qualifying and points; multiplayer as specified; hub variant where\nlisted; attract segment; headless tests (determinism, bot completes, skill monotonic, every mechanic check of §6);\na screenshot reviewed.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation | Early signal |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Scope: 12 events + ceremonies + hub | an unfinished game | one event contract and widgets; reference event first; reuse kits (sports → hockey, road → downhill + bobsled, rhythm → figure, physics/pinball → curling); events written in order of reuse; nothing beyond this plan | milestone burn-down; DoD per event |\n| Custom athlete animation looks broken | cheap look, unreadable actions | built-in rig vocabulary first; `O.Pose` + Pose Lab + filmstrips in M3; equipment carries readability (a javelin, a barbell, skis say what the pose is) | M3 filmstrips |\n| Rigs from behind on `E.Road` | downhill/bobsled unconvincing | M3 spike with a custom rear `E.View`; fallback: skier and sled drawn as code-drawn sprites with 8 lean frames | spike screenshot |\n| Hub protocol failures | the game is kept out of sessions | M3 spike against the real harness; follow §12.2 literally; test every scenario | harness pass |\n| Cosmetic `Math.random` use (rigs, particles) | hub card rule broken; flaky tests | engine change 2; gameplay only via `O.rng` streams; proofs run twice | determinism tests; `Math.random` call-count check on the card |\n| Input conflicts (J/K/Space/○ in menus vs play) | skipped screens, accidental cancels | custom preset without J/K in confirm/cancel; lockouts; `consumeAll` on enter; hold-to-skip cinematics | input tests |\n| Missing ✕○□△ in the pixel font | `?` in prompts | `O.Prompt` icons + font glyphs (engine change 3) | prompt test for every action × device × glyph style |\n| Engine HTML menus too small on a TV | 10-foot failure | CSS override; 1920×1080 screenshot | screenshot |\n| Unbalanced events | boring or unfair | points tables; bot calibration tests per skill; dev sliders; difficulty presets | bot statistics test |\n| Slow headless tests | tests skipped | sims are draw-free; `--quick`; the full playthrough uses perfect bots | test time printed |\n| Bundle breakage (`</script>`, order, size) | a broken deliverable | bundler escapes; a bundle test in Chromium from `file://` | bundle test |\n| Voices grating | players mute everything | cooldowns, priorities, voices volume, subtitles-only | a listening pass with the dev sound test |\n| Touch-only misdetection on touch laptops | locked-out players | coarse && no fine pointer && no key/pad seen; any key or pad unlocks | touch emulation test |\n| Curling CPU cost (108 sims) | hitches | 12 candidates per frame, early exits | per-frame timing test |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Testing\n\n### 16.1 The one command\n\n`node tests/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) runs every suite: headless Node suites first, then the browser suites\n(Playwright). It prints **only failures** (suite, check, a one-line detail) and then **one line**:\n`olympiyikes: 512 checks, 0 failed (headless 41 s, browser 63 s)`; exit code 1 on any failure. `--quick` runs only the\nheadless suites; `--only <suite>` runs one. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. The browser suites\nload Playwright from the handoff's install (`createRequire(<dev>/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/package.json)('playwright')`),\nso there is one `npm install` for everything.\n\n### 16.2 The harness (`tests/harness.mjs`)\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1540,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HaPxTfboc3HEn4FFkvgQsX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
